INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-700</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement and manage an analytics solution (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Microsoft Fabric workspace settings (Spark, domain, OneLake, Apache Airflow)</li><li>Implement lifecycle management: version control, database projects, deployment pipelines</li><li>Configure security and governance: workspace/item-level access controls, row/column/object/file-level security, dynamic data masking, sensitivity labels, item endorsement, audit logs, OneLake security</li><li>Orchestrate processes: choose between Dataflow Gen2, pipeline, and notebook; design schedules and event-based triggers; implement orchestration patterns with parameters and dynamic expressions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Ingest and transform data (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement full and incremental data loading patterns, including for dimensional models and streaming data</li><li>Ingest and transform batch data: choose appropriate data store and transformation tool (Dataflows Gen2, notebooks, KQL, T-SQL), create OneLake shortcuts, implement mirroring, ingest via pipelines</li><li>Transform data using PySpark, SQL, and KQL; denormalize, group/aggregate data; handle duplicate, missing, and late-arriving data</li><li>Ingest and transform streaming data: choose streaming engine, process data via Eventstreams, Spark structured streaming, and KQL; create windowing functions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Monitor and optimize an analytics solution (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor Fabric items: data ingestion, data transformation, semantic model refresh, and configure alerts</li><li>Identify and resolve errors in pipelines, Dataflow Gen2, notebooks, Eventhouse, Eventstream, T-SQL, and OneLake shortcuts</li><li>Optimize performance of Lakehouse tables, pipelines, data warehouses, Eventstreams/Eventhouses, Spark jobs, and queries</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1000' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CLF-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Cloud Concepts (24%)</h3><ul><li>Define the benefits of the AWS Cloud (global infrastructure, high availability, elasticity, agility)</li><li>Identify design principles of the AWS Cloud (AWS Well-Architected Framework pillars)</li><li>Understand benefits and strategies for migration to the AWS Cloud (AWS Cloud Adoption Framework, migration strategies)</li><li>Understand concepts of cloud economics (fixed vs. variable costs, licensing strategies, rightsizing, economies of scale)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Security and Compliance (30%)</h3><ul><li>Understand the AWS shared responsibility model</li><li>Understand AWS Cloud security, governance, and compliance concepts (encryption, AWS Artifact, CloudWatch/CloudTrail/Config)</li><li>Identify AWS access management capabilities (IAM, root user protection, least privilege, IAM Identity Center, MFA)</li><li>Identify components and resources for security (AWS WAF, Shield, GuardDuty, Trusted Advisor, AWS Marketplace security products)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Cloud Technology and Services (34%)</h3><ul><li>Define methods of deploying and operating in the AWS Cloud (API/SDK/CLI, Management Console, IaC, deployment models)</li><li>Define the AWS global infrastructure (Regions, Availability Zones, edge locations, high availability)</li><li>Identify AWS compute services (EC2 instance types, containers ECS/EKS, serverless Lambda/Fargate, auto scaling, load balancers)</li><li>Identify AWS database services (RDS, Aurora, DynamoDB, ElastiCache, DMS/SCT)</li><li>Identify AWS network services (VPC components, security groups/NACLs, Route 53, VPN, Direct Connect)</li><li>Identify AWS storage services (S3 storage classes, EBS, EFS/FSx, Storage Gateway, lifecycle policies, AWS Backup)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Billing, Pricing, and Support (12%)</h3><ul><li>Compare AWS pricing models (On-Demand, Reserved, Spot, Savings Plans, Dedicated Hosts/Instances)</li><li>Understand resources for billing, budget, and cost management (AWS Budgets, Cost Explorer, Pricing Calculator, Organizations consolidated billing, cost allocation tags)</li><li>Identify AWS technical resources and AWS Support options (Support plans, Trusted Advisor, AWS Partner Network, AWS Marketplace)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1041' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SK0-005</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Server Hardware Installation and Management (18%)</h3><ul><li>Install physical hardware (racking, power/network cabling, chassis types, HCL-aware component selection)</li><li>Deploy and manage storage (RAID levels 0/1/5/6/10, JBOD, hardware vs. software RAID, capacity planning)</li><li>Perform server hardware maintenance (firmware/driver updates, replacing FRUs, environmental monitoring, capacity/asset planning)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Server Administration (30%)</h3><ul><li>Install server operating systems (installation methods, boot methods, partitioning, driver/firmware considerations)</li><li>Configure servers to use network infrastructure services (DNS, DHCP, NTP, directory services)</li><li>Configure and maintain server functions/features (roles, file/print/web services, storage provisioning)</li><li>Explain key concepts of high availability (clustering, load balancing, failover, redundancy, replication)</li><li>Summarize the purpose and operation of virtualization (hypervisors, VM configuration, resource allocation)</li><li>Summarize scripting basics for server administration (variables, loops, automation use cases)</li><li>Explain the importance of asset management and documentation</li><li>Explain licensing concepts (per-seat, per-core, subscription, open source)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Security and Disaster Recovery (24%)</h3><ul><li>Summarize data security concepts (encryption at rest/in transit, key management)</li><li>Summarize physical security concepts (access control, video surveillance, environmental controls)</li><li>Explain identity and access management concepts (authentication, authorization, MFA, least privilege)</li><li>Explain data security risks and mitigation strategies (threats, vulnerabilities, hardening controls)</li><li>Apply server hardening methods (patching, disabling unused services, host firewalls)</li><li>Explain the importance of backups/restores and disaster recovery (backup types, RTO/RPO, DR sites, testing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Troubleshooting (28%)</h3><ul><li>Explain troubleshooting theory and methodology (identify problem, establish theory, test, implement, document)</li><li>Troubleshoot common hardware failures (POST errors, component failures, environmental issues)</li><li>Troubleshoot storage problems (RAID failures, disk errors, capacity/performance issues)</li><li>Troubleshoot common OS and software problems (boot failures, service crashes, patch issues)</li><li>Troubleshoot network connectivity issues (connectivity loss, name resolution, latency)</li><li>Troubleshoot security problems (unauthorized access, malware, certificate/authentication failures)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1048' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AI-901</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Identify AI concepts and capabilities (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe principles of responsible AI: fairness, reliability & safety, privacy & security, inclusiveness, transparency, accountability</li><li>Describe how generative AI models work</li><li>Identify an appropriate AI model based on its capabilities</li><li>Identify appropriate model deployment options and configuration parameters</li><li>Identify scenarios for common AI workloads, including generative/agentic AI, text analysis, speech, computer vision, and information extraction</li><li>Describe common text analysis techniques: keyword extraction, entity detection, sentiment analysis, summarization</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement AI solutions by using Microsoft Foundry (57.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create effective system and user prompts for generative AI models</li><li>Deploy a model and interact with it in the Foundry portal; build a lightweight chat client app using the Foundry SDK</li><li>Create and test a single-agent solution in the Foundry portal, and build a lightweight client app for an agent</li><li>Build lightweight applications with text analysis and speech capabilities using Azure Speech in Foundry Tools</li><li>Implement computer vision and image-generation capabilities: interpret visual input and generate new visual outputs via a deployed multimodal model</li><li>Extract information from documents, images, audio, and video using Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1071' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Associate</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Setting up a cloud solution environment (20%)</h3><ul><li>Setting up cloud projects and accounts: resource hierarchy, org policies, IAM roles, Cloud Identity users/groups, API enablement</li><li>Assessing quotas and requesting increases; verifying product availability across regions/zones</li><li>Configuring Cloud Asset Inventory and using Gemini Cloud Assist to analyze resources</li><li>Configuring Workforce Identity Federation and setting up cloud networking</li><li>Managing billing configuration: billing accounts, linking projects, budgets/alerts, billing exports</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Planning and implementing a cloud solution (30%)</h3><ul><li>Planning and implementing compute resources: choosing Compute Engine/GKE/Cloud Run/serverless, launching instances, managed instance groups, GKE cluster deployment, GPUs/TPUs</li><li>Planning and implementing storage and data solutions: Cloud SQL, BigQuery, Firestore, Spanner, Bigtable, Cloud Storage classes, data loading, multi-region redundancy</li><li>Planning and implementing networking resources: VPC/subnets, firewall rules and Cloud NGFW policies, network connectivity (VPN/Peering/Interconnect), load balancers, network service tiers</li><li>Planning and implementing resources using tooling: Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, Config Connector, Helm) and AI-assisted planning (Gemini CLI, Gemini Cloud Assist, Application Design Center)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Ensuring the successful operation of a cloud solution (30%)</h3><ul><li>Managing compute resources: Compute Engine instances, snapshots/images, GKE node pools and Kubernetes resources, Pod autoscaling, Cloud Run deployments and traffic splitting</li><li>Managing storage and data solutions: securing Cloud Storage objects, lifecycle policies, querying data instances, backup/restore, cost estimation, CMEK</li><li>Managing networking resources: resizing subnets, static IPs, custom routes, Cloud DNS and Cloud NAT, firewall/NGFW policy management</li><li>Monitoring and logging: Cloud Monitoring alerts and custom metrics, audit logs, log routers/analytics, diagnostic tools (Cloud Trace, Cloud Profiler), Ops Agent, Gemini Cloud Assist and Active Assist for monitoring</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Configuring access and security (20%)</h3><ul><li>Managing IAM: viewing/creating IAM policies, role inheritance in the Organization hierarchy, custom IAM roles</li><li>Managing service accounts: creation, minimum-permission IAM policies, assigning to resources, impersonation, short-lived credentials</li><li>Using Google Cloud service accounts with GKE applications</li><li>Provisioning Workload Identity Federation</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1098' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PT0-003</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Engagement Management (13%)</h3><ul><li>Summarize pre-engagement activities: scope definition, rules of engagement, agreement types (NDA, MSA, SOW, ToS), target selection, shared responsibility model, legal/ethical considerations</li><li>Explain collaboration and communication activities: peer review, stakeholder alignment, escalation path, goal reprioritization, business impact analysis</li><li>Compare and contrast testing frameworks and methodologies (OSSTMM, CREST, PTES, MITRE ATT&CK, OWASP Top 10/MASVS, threat modeling frameworks DREAD/STRIDE/OCTAVE)</li><li>Explain the components of a penetration test report: executive summary, methodology, detailed findings, attack narrative, recommendations/remediation guidance</li><li>Given a scenario, analyze findings and recommend appropriate remediation (technical, administrative, operational, physical controls)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Reconnaissance and Enumeration (21%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, apply information gathering techniques: active/passive reconnaissance, OSINT, DNS lookups, certificate transparency logs, network sniffing, protocol scanning</li><li>Given a scenario, apply enumeration techniques: OS fingerprinting, service/protocol/DNS/directory/host/share/user/email enumeration, attack path mapping</li><li>Given a scenario, modify scripts for reconnaissance and enumeration using Bash, Python, or PowerShell</li><li>Given a scenario, use appropriate tools for reconnaissance and enumeration (Nmap, theHarvester, Shodan, Maltego, Recon-ng, Amass, WHOIS, Wireshark/tcpdump)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Vulnerability Discovery and Analysis (17%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, conduct vulnerability discovery using various techniques: container/application/network scans, DAST/IAST/SAST/SCA, authenticated vs. unauthenticated scans, wireless scanning, ICS vulnerability assessment</li><li>Given a scenario, analyze output from reconnaissance, scanning, and enumeration phases: validating results (false positives/negatives, true positives), public exploit selection, scripting to validate results</li><li>Explain physical security concepts: tailgating, site surveys, USB drops, badge cloning, lock picking</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Attacks and Exploits (35%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, analyze output to prioritize and prepare attacks: target prioritization (CVSS, CVE, CWE, EPSS), capability/tool/exploit selection, attack path and documentation</li><li>Given a scenario, perform network, authentication, and host-based attacks using appropriate tools (Metasploit, Hydra, Mimikatz, CrackMapExec, Impacket, hashcat)</li><li>Given a scenario, perform web application attacks (SQLi, XSS, SSRF, CSRF, file inclusion, JWT manipulation) using tools such as Burp Suite, ZAP, sqlmap, Gobuster</li><li>Given a scenario, perform cloud-based and wireless attacks using appropriate tools (Pacu, ScoutSuite, Prowler, Aircrack-ng, Kismet)</li><li>Given a scenario, perform social engineering attacks (phishing, vishing, pretexting) and explain attacks against specialized systems (mobile, AI/prompt injection, OT/ICS, NFC/Bluetooth)</li><li>Given a scenario, use scripting (PowerShell, Bash, Python) and breach-and-attack simulation tools to automate attacks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Post-exploitation and Lateral Movement (14%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, perform tasks to establish and maintain persistence: scheduled tasks, service creation, reverse/bind shells, backdoors, C2 frameworks, rootkits</li><li>Given a scenario, perform tasks to move laterally throughout the environment: pivoting, relay creation, service/credential enumeration, WMI/WinRM, LOLBins, tools like CrackMapExec, Impacket, PsExec</li><li>Summarize concepts related to staging and exfiltration: file encryption/compression, covert channels (DNS, ICMP, HTTPS, steganography), cloud storage, alternate data streams</li><li>Explain cleanup and restoration activities: removing persistence mechanisms and tester-created credentials/tools, reverting configuration changes, secure data destruction</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1136' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>XK0-006</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 System Management (23%)</h3><ul><li>Linux basics: boot process steps, kernel, filesystems, and architectures</li><li>Device management: kernel modules, hardware components, device utilities</li><li>Storage management: LVM, RAID, partitions, mounted storage</li><li>Network configuration: hosts, DNS, interfaces, network tools</li><li>Shell operations: navigation, editing, redirection, environment variables</li><li>Backups/restores and virtualization: archiving/compression, hypervisors, VMs, disk images</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Services and User Management (20%)</h3><ul><li>Files & directories: permissions, links, special files</li><li>Account management: add/remove/modify users and groups</li><li>Process control: monitor states, adjust priorities, schedule jobs</li><li>Software management: install/update/remove packages and repositories</li><li>Systems management: start/stop/review services, logs, timers</li><li>Containers: operate container runtimes, manage images, create networks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Security (18%)</h3><ul><li>Auth & accounting: PAM, LDAP, Kerberos, auditing</li><li>Firewalls: iptables, nftables, UFW, zone rules</li><li>OS hardening: permissions, sudo configuration, secure remote access</li><li>Account security: password policies, restricted shells, MFA</li><li>Cryptography: file encryption, hashing, certificate management</li><li>Compliance: integrity verification, scans, maintaining standards</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Automation, Orchestration, and Scripting (17%)</h3><ul><li>Automation: Ansible, Puppet, CI/CD tools</li><li>Shell scripting: variables, functions, logic flows, troubleshooting</li><li>Python basics: environments, packages, data types</li><li>Version control: Git workflows and tagging</li><li>AI best practices: responsible code generation and prompt engineering</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Troubleshooting (22%)</h3><ul><li>System monitoring: health, logs, event alerts</li><li>Hardware/storage: diagnose boot, mount, and repair issues</li><li>Networking: firewall, routing, DNS, connectivity problems</li><li>Security: SELinux, permission, and vulnerability issues</li><li>Performance: CPU, memory, I/O analysis and response-time optimization</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1162' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CISA</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Information Systems Auditing Process (18%)</h3><ul><li>IS audit standards, guidelines, and codes of ethics</li><li>Types of audits, assessments, and reviews</li><li>Risk-based audit planning and types of controls</li><li>Audit project management and evidence collection techniques</li><li>Audit testing, sampling methodology, and audit data analytics</li><li>Reporting/communication techniques and quality assurance of the audit process</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Governance & Management of IT (18%)</h3><ul><li>Laws, regulations, and industry standards affecting IT</li><li>Organizational structure, IT governance, and IT strategy</li><li>IT policies, standards, procedures, and enterprise architecture</li><li>Enterprise risk management, privacy program and data governance/classification</li><li>IT resource and vendor management</li><li>IT performance monitoring, reporting, and quality management</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Information Systems Acquisition, Development & Implementation (12%)</h3><ul><li>Project governance and management; business case and feasibility analysis</li><li>System development methodologies and control identification/design</li><li>System readiness and implementation testing</li><li>Configuration and release management</li><li>System migration, infrastructure deployment, and data conversion</li><li>Post-implementation review</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Information Systems Operations & Business Resilience (26%)</h3><ul><li>IT components, asset management, and job scheduling/automation</li><li>System interfaces, shadow IT, end-user computing, and database management</li><li>Systems availability/capacity management and problem/incident management</li><li>IT change, configuration, and patch management; operational log and service-level management</li><li>Business impact analysis and system/operational resilience</li><li>Data backup/storage/restoration, business continuity, and disaster recovery plans</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Protection of Information Assets (26%)</h3><ul><li>Information asset security frameworks, standards, and physical/environmental controls</li><li>Identity and access management; network and endpoint security</li><li>Data loss prevention, data encryption, and public key infrastructure</li><li>Cloud/virtualized environments and mobile, wireless, IoT device security</li><li>Security awareness training and attack methods/techniques</li><li>Security testing/monitoring tools and incident response, evidence collection, and forensics</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1186' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-600</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Perform solution envisioning and requirement analysis (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Initiate solution planning (evaluate business requirements, identify Power Platform solution components, select components from existing apps/Dynamics 365/AppSource/Azure/ISVs, estimate migration and integration effort)</li><li>Identify organization information and metrics (current-state business processes, risk factors, key success criteria)</li><li>Identify existing solutions and systems (enterprise architecture, data sources, use cases/quality standards for existing data)</li><li>Capture requirements (refine high-level requirements, functional and non-functional requirements, future-state business process design)</li><li>Perform fit/gap analyses (feasibility, Dynamics 365/AppSource fit, address functional gaps, determine solution scope)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Architect a solution (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Lead the design process (solution topology, customization approach, UX prototypes, component reuse, data migration/visualization/automation/environment strategy)</li><li>Design the data model (relationships and relationship behaviors, external vs. imported data, models for complex requirements)</li><li>Design integrations (Teams/SharePoint, Power Platform-to-Dynamics 365, third-party and existing-systems integration, authentication strategy, business continuity, RPA, networking)</li><li>Design the security model (business unit/team structure, security roles, column/row-level security, Entra ID groups and app registrations, DLP policies, external user access)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement the solution (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Validate the solution design (evaluate detailed designs, review security including business rules/roles/Entra ID/boundaries, ensure API limit conformance, assess performance impact)</li><li>Resolve automation and integration conflicts</li><li>Support go-live: identify and resolve performance and data migration issues</li><li>Support go-live: resolve deployment plan issues and remediate go-live readiness factors</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1190' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MLA-C01</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Data Preparation for Machine Learning (ML) (28%)</h3><ul><li>Ingest and store data from AWS sources (S3, EFS, FSx) and streaming sources (Kinesis, Apache Flink/Kafka); choose data formats (Parquet, JSON, CSV, ORC, Avro, RecordIO)</li><li>Transform data and perform feature engineering (cleaning, encoding, scaling/normalization, binning) using SageMaker Data Wrangler, AWS Glue/Glue DataBrew, Spark on EMR</li><li>Create and manage features using SageMaker Feature Store; validate and label data using SageMaker Ground Truth / Mechanical Turk</li><li>Ensure data integrity: identify and mitigate bias (class imbalance, DPL) using SageMaker Clarify</li><li>Apply data classification, anonymization, masking and encryption for compliance (PII, PHI, data residency)</li><li>Prepare data for modeling (splitting, shuffling, augmentation) and configure data loading into training resources (EFS, FSx)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: ML Model Development (26%)</h3><ul><li>Choose a modeling approach: assess feasibility, select ML algorithms/AI services (Bedrock, Rekognition, Translate, Transcribe), consider interpretability and cost</li><li>Use SageMaker built-in algorithms, script mode (TensorFlow/PyTorch), and JumpStart/Bedrock foundation models for fine-tuning</li><li>Train and refine models: hyperparameter tuning (SageMaker AMT), regularization (dropout, L1/L2), prevent overfitting/underfitting/catastrophic forgetting</li><li>Combine models via ensembling, stacking, boosting; reduce model size via pruning/compression/quantized data types</li><li>Manage model versions using SageMaker Model Registry for repeatability and audits</li><li>Analyze model performance: select/interpret evaluation metrics (F1, precision/recall, RMSE, ROC/AUC), create baselines, detect bias and convergence issues via SageMaker Clarify/Model Debugger</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Deployment and Orchestration of ML Workflows (22%)</h3><ul><li>Select deployment infrastructure: real-time/serverless/asynchronous endpoints vs batch inference, compute provisioning (CPU/GPU), containers, edge optimization (SageMaker Neo)</li><li>Choose deployment orchestrator and target (SageMaker Pipelines, Airflow, SageMaker endpoints, ECS/EKS, Lambda) and deployment strategy (real time vs batch, blue/green, canary, linear)</li><li>Create and script infrastructure as code (CloudFormation, AWS CDK) including containerization (ECR, EKS, ECS, bring-your-own-container) and SageMaker endpoint auto scaling</li><li>Configure SageMaker endpoints within a VPC and deploy/host models using the SageMaker SDK</li><li>Set up CI/CD pipelines with AWS CodePipeline, CodeBuild, and CodeDeploy, integrated with Git-based version control</li><li>Automate orchestration of training/inference jobs (EventBridge rules, SageMaker Pipelines) and build automated tests plus retraining mechanisms</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: ML Solution Monitoring, Maintenance, and Security (24%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor model inference: detect data/model drift and anomalies using SageMaker Model Monitor and SageMaker Clarify; monitor performance via A/B testing</li><li>Monitor and optimize infrastructure and costs using CloudWatch, X-Ray, CloudTrail, Cost Explorer, Trusted Advisor, and resource tagging strategies</li><li>Rightsize instances and troubleshoot latency/scaling/capacity issues using SageMaker Inference Recommender and AWS Compute Optimizer</li><li>Optimize infrastructure costs via purchasing options (Spot, On-Demand, Reserved Instances, SageMaker Savings Plans)</li><li>Secure AWS resources: configure least-privilege IAM roles/policies for ML systems and applications, including SageMaker Role Manager</li><li>Build VPCs, subnets, and security groups to isolate ML systems; monitor, audit, and log ML systems for continued security and compliance</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1330' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-900</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe the business value of Microsoft Power Platform (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the value of Power Apps to build applications</li><li>Describe the value of Power Automate to automate processes</li><li>Describe the value of Microsoft Dataverse to organize business data</li><li>Describe the value of connectors to integrate services and data for apps and flows</li><li>Describe the value of Power Pages to build websites</li><li>Describe the value of generative AI features in Power Platform and Copilot Studio to create agents</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Manage the Microsoft Power Platform environment (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe differences between traditional databases and Dataverse; tables, columns, relationships, forms and views</li><li>Describe options for business logic in Dataverse, including Power Fx, and using AI to create/edit tables and columns</li><li>Describe environments and the Power Platform security model</li><li>Describe how Power Platform supports data privacy and accessibility guidelines</li><li>Describe monitoring and analytics capabilities</li><li>Describe application lifecycle management (ALM) with Power Platform pipelines</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Demonstrate the capabilities of Power Apps (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases for and capabilities of canvas apps</li><li>Describe use cases for and capabilities of model-driven apps</li><li>Describe use cases for and capabilities of Plan designer and code apps</li><li>Describe how to use AI to create a canvas app or model-driven app</li><li>Describe creating AI-powered apps by using the vibe experience</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Demonstrate the capabilities of Power Automate (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases for cloud and desktop flows</li><li>Describe Power Automate use cases for approvals, Teams, Outlook, SharePoint, Forms, and document automation</li><li>Describe connector triggers and actions for cloud flows</li><li>Describe how to use AI to create and modify cloud flows</li><li>Describe how to use AI to create and modify desktop flows</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Describe features and capabilities of agents in Microsoft Copilot Studio (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases for agents and how to build agent conversation paths by using topics</li><li>Describe how to use knowledge sources in agents</li><li>Describe how tools, including MCP servers and agent flows, are used in agents</li><li>Describe how to publish agents by using channels</li><li>Describe use cases and capabilities for Microsoft Agent 365, and how to monitor agent usage/adoption and agent evaluations</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1358' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-500</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design automations (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Differentiate between cloud flows and desktop flows and choose the right trigger types / run methods (attended vs unattended, concurrency)</li><li>Design automations using other Power Platform features: canvas/model-driven apps, connectors, custom connectors, connection references, and Microsoft Dataverse</li><li>Design automations that analyze and enhance data and documents: Microsoft AI options, OCR capabilities, Document Automation Toolkit</li><li>Design automations using scripting languages in desktop flows: PowerShell, VBScript, JavaScript, and DOM manipulation</li><li>Assess whether work queues are applicable and design custom actions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Develop automations (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Develop cloud flows: call desktop flows, use child flows (pass/return data), call external APIs, implement trigger conditions, concurrency, timeout/retry, data operations, and text parsing (JSON/XML/CSV)</li><li>Develop desktop flows: UI options, datatables/lists/custom objects, subflows, external API calls, timeout/retry, data operations, text parsing, and custom actions</li><li>Implement logic in cloud and desktop flows: flow control/loops, expressions, variables, secure input/output, priority in a queue, exception handling and business-error handling, work queues</li><li>Build custom connectors and implement connector configurations: authentication, policy templates, and code</li><li>Perform automation infrastructure management: credential management, on-premises data gateway, and Dataverse solution components</li><li>Test and finalize automations: test cloud/desktop flows, use environment variables/configuration files, and debugging features</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Deploy and manage automations (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Prepare target environments: implement Power Platform ALM, differentiate credentials per environment, and build virtual desktop environments for unattended runs</li><li>Assess Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies and how they impact cloud/desktop flow actions and custom connectors</li><li>Implement access to RPA components: sharing flows/machines/machine groups, security roles, service accounts and service principals</li><li>Implement machine groups and queues: machine/machine-group registration and management, load balancing via machine groups and queues, run-queue operations</li><li>Analyze cloud and desktop flow run history from the Power Automate portal for monitoring and support</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1384' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-600</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design collaborative app solutions and existing app integration (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Assess Microsoft Teams and existing app integration opportunities (M365 Maturity Model, low-code/no-code options via Power Platform/Logic Apps/Dataverse for Teams)</li><li>Design development and production environments (test/acceptance/production/deployment strategy, Azure services for Teams use cases, CI/CD requirements)</li><li>Develop tooling strategy and select development framework/runtime platform (Teams Toolkit vs Yeoman generator; Node.js, .NET, SPFx)</li><li>Design solution based on technical and business requirements: authentication scenarios (guest users, multitenant)</li><li>Design UI using Microsoft Teams UI Library, Fluent UI React Northstar, Adaptive Cards, Teams UI Kit for Figma</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement Microsoft identity (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Register an application (supported account types, authentication/client credential flow, app roles)</li><li>Implement authentication (MSAL JavaScript configuration, scopes, SSO for bots and tabs)</li><li>Configure permissions to consume an API (delegated vs application permissions, consent requirements)</li><li>Implement authorization to expose or consume an API (incremental consent scopes, AcquireTokenSilent/AcquireToken pattern)</li><li>Implement authorization in an API (validate access tokens, configure effective permissions, role-based app permissions)</li><li>Create a service to access Microsoft Graph (client credentials with certificate, Key Vault, application permissions)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Build apps with Microsoft Graph (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Access data from Microsoft Graph (SDK vs REST API, signed-in user profile, CRUD operations, Graph Toolkit)</li><li>Customize responses using query parameters ($filter, $select, $orderby, $expand, $search, $count, $skip, $top)</li><li>Optimize usage of Microsoft Graph resources (change notifications, $batch, delta query, throttling handling)</li><li>Manage a team lifecycle using Microsoft Graph (provision/update/delete/archive a team, members, owners, resource-specific consent)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Extend and customize Microsoft 365 with SharePoint Framework (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the components of an SPFx solution (web parts, properties, Fluent UI, app pages, branding/theming, Adaptive Card Extensions, Viva Connections)</li><li>Describe SPFx extension types (Application Customizer, Field Customizer, ListView Command Set)</li><li>Describe the process to package and deploy an SPFx solution (tenant-scoped deployment, domain-isolated web parts)</li><li>Describe consumption of Microsoft Graph and third-party APIs secured with Azure AD (Microsoft Entra) from within SPFx (MSGraphClient, AadHttpClient)</li><li>Describe Web Parts as Teams Tabs (considerations and deployment options)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Extend Microsoft Teams (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create a Microsoft Teams app manifest and app package (Developer Portal)</li><li>Create and use task modules (card-based, iframe-based; invoked from tab or bot; chained invocations)</li><li>Implement custom Teams tabs (personal, channel/group, deep link, adaptive card tab, device permissions)</li><li>Create a messaging extension (search command, action command with adaptive card/parameters, link unfurling)</li><li>Create conversational, call, and online media bots (personal/group bots, proactive/actionable messages, call handling and transfer)</li><li>Create a meeting extension (Teams meeting app capabilities, shared meeting stage, meeting lifecycle integration)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Test, deploy, monitor, and maintain modern enterprise-grade app solutions (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Test apps and solutions (design and execute test plans for bots, connectors, messaging extensions, meeting extensions, SSO, Adaptive Cards; sample data via M365 CLI/PowerShell)</li><li>Deploy apps and solutions (create/modify app definitions and manage packages in Developer Portal, upload to App Catalog, automate deployment)</li><li>Monitor and maintain published apps (Microsoft 365 audit logging, App Insights, Graph API permission monitoring via compliance center, assess new SDK versions, analyze logs/usage/audit data)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1388' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-300</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Plan and implement data platform resources (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recommend a database offering and choose an automated deployment method based on requirements</li><li>Identify use cases for Azure Arc-enabled SQL services and Azure SQL Database in Microsoft Fabric</li><li>Plan and configure table partitioning and database sharding</li><li>Deploy database offerings on selected platforms, including hybrid SQL Server solutions</li><li>Evaluate and implement online/offline migration strategies to Azure or between Azure SQL services</li><li>Troubleshoot a migration</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement a secure environment (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Microsoft Entra ID authentication and security principals for Azure SQL Database, Managed Instance, and SQL Server</li><li>Apply the principle of least privilege and manage authorization via T-SQL and graphical tools</li><li>Implement transparent data encryption (TDE), Always Encrypted (incl. VBS enclaves), and object-level encryption</li><li>Configure server/database firewall rules, private links, and service endpoints</li><li>Apply a data classification strategy and configure server/database audits</li><li>Implement dynamic data masking, row-level security, ledger, and change data tracking</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Monitor, configure, and optimize database resources (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Prepare an operational performance baseline and interpret performance metrics</li><li>Monitor using Query Store, Extended Events, database watcher, DMVs, and Intelligent Insights</li><li>Identify and resolve session blocking and implement index/statistics maintenance tasks</li><li>Review execution plans and recommend query construct modifications</li><li>Configure database automatic tuning, Resource Governor, and database-scoped configuration</li><li>Configure compute/storage scaling and apply intelligent query processing (IQP) features</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Configure and manage automation of tasks (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage SQL Server Agent jobs, schedules, alerts, and notifications</li><li>Troubleshoot SQL Server Agent jobs</li><li>Automate deployment of database resources using ARM/Bicep templates, Azure PowerShell, and Azure CLI</li><li>Monitor and troubleshoot automated deployments</li><li>Create and configure elastic jobs and other automated database tasks in Azure</li><li>Configure alerts/notifications and troubleshoot automated database tasks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Plan and configure a high availability and disaster recovery (HA/DR) environment (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recommend an HA/DR strategy based on RPO/RTO requirements, including hybrid and Azure-specific solutions</li><li>Plan and perform database backup and restore (native tools, T-SQL, point-in-time, cloud storage, long-term retention)</li><li>Configure active geo-replication and failover groups</li><li>Configure Always On availability groups (SQL MI and Azure VMs) and Always On Failover Cluster Instances</li><li>Configure log shipping</li><li>Monitor and troubleshoot an HA/DR solution</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1389' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DOP-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: SDLC Automation (22%)</h3><ul><li>Implement CI/CD pipelines (code/image/artifact repos, build processes e.g. AWS CodeBuild, deployment strategies e.g. AWS CodeDeploy)</li><li>Integrate automated testing into CI/CD pipelines (unit, integration, acceptance, UI, security scan tests; load/stress testing at scale)</li><li>Build and manage artifacts (repositories such as CodeArtifact, S3, Amazon ECR; artifact lifecycle)</li><li>Implement deployment strategies for instance, container, and serverless environments (mutable vs immutable, blue/green, canary)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Configuration Management and IaC (17%)</h3><ul><li>Define cloud infrastructure and reusable components using IaC (AWS CloudFormation, AWS SAM, AWS CDK, CloudFormation StackSets)</li><li>Deploy automation to create, onboard, and secure AWS accounts in multi-account/multi-Region environments (AWS Organizations, Control Tower, SCPs)</li><li>Design and build automated solutions for complex tasks and large-scale environments (Systems Manager, AWS Config, Lambda automation, Step Functions)</li><li>Determine optimal configuration management services and maintain software compliance (OpsWorks, Systems Manager State Manager)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Resilient Cloud Solutions (15%)</h3><ul><li>Implement highly available solutions to meet resilience and business requirements (Multi-AZ, multi-Region, cross-Region failover)</li><li>Implement solutions that are scalable to meet business requirements (auto scaling, load balancing, caching, serverless, containers)</li><li>Implement automated recovery processes to meet RTO and RPO requirements (backup/DR strategies, pilot light, warm standby, AWS Backup)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Monitoring and Logging (15%)</h3><ul><li>Configure the collection, aggregation, and storage of logs and metrics (CloudWatch metrics, metric filters/streams, log lifecycle, encryption)</li><li>Audit, monitor, and analyze logs and metrics to detect issues (CloudWatch dashboards/alarms, X-Ray, Athena, anomaly detection)</li><li>Automate monitoring and event management of complex environments (event-driven patterns, auto scaling triggers, alert notifications, health checks)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Domain 5: Incident and Event Response (14%)</h3><ul><li>Manage event sources to process, notify, and take action in response to events (EventBridge, CloudTrail, AWS Health; SQS/SNS/Lambda/Step Functions workflows)</li><li>Implement configuration changes in response to events (fleet management, remediating non-desired system state)</li><li>Troubleshoot system and application failures (analyzing failed deployments via CodePipeline/CodeBuild/CodeDeploy/CloudFormation, root cause analysis)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Domain 6: Security and Compliance (17%)</h3><ul><li>Implement techniques for identity and access management at scale (IAM entities, identity federation, permissions boundaries, organizational SCPs)</li><li>Apply automation for security controls and data protection (WAF, Shield, KMS, CloudHSM, ACM, Macie for sensitive data discovery)</li><li>Implement security monitoring and auditing solutions (CloudTrail, AWS Config, VPC Flow Logs, GuardDuty, Inspector, IAM Access Analyzer)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1391' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SOA-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Monitoring, Logging, and Remediation (20%)</h3><ul><li>Implement metrics, alarms, and filters using AWS monitoring/logging services (CloudWatch Logs, CloudWatch Logs Insights, AWS CloudTrail)</li><li>Collect metrics and logs using the CloudWatch agent</li><li>Create CloudWatch alarms, metric filters, and dashboards</li><li>Configure notifications via Amazon SNS, Service Quotas, CloudWatch alarms, AWS Health events</li><li>Remediate issues based on monitoring/availability metrics using EventBridge rules and Systems Manager Automation documents triggered by AWS Config rules</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Reliability and Business Continuity (16%)</h3><ul><li>Implement scalability and elasticity (Auto Scaling plans, caching, RDS replicas/Aurora Replicas, loosely coupled architectures, horizontal vs vertical scaling)</li><li>Implement high availability and resilient environments (ELB/Route 53 health checks, single-AZ vs Multi-AZ, fault-tolerant workloads, Route 53 routing policies)</li><li>Implement backup and restore strategies (automated snapshots/backups, RTO/RPO, AWS Backup, Data Lifecycle Manager)</li><li>Restore databases (point-in-time restore, promote read replica)</li><li>Implement S3 versioning, lifecycle rules, and Cross-Region Replication</li><li>Execute disaster recovery procedures</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Deployment, Provisioning, and Automation (18%)</h3><ul><li>Provision and maintain cloud resources (create/manage AMIs via EC2 Image Builder, CloudFormation, cross-Region/cross-account provisioning via RAM/StackSets/IAM cross-account roles)</li><li>Select deployment scenarios (blue/green, rolling, canary) and identify/remediate deployment issues (service quotas, subnet sizing, CloudFormation/OpsWorks errors, permissions)</li><li>Automate manual or repeatable processes using OpsWorks, Systems Manager, CloudFormation</li><li>Implement automated patch management</li><li>Schedule automated tasks using EventBridge and AWS Config</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Security and Compliance (16%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage security/compliance policies (IAM features: password policies, MFA, roles, SAML, federated identity, resource policies, policy conditions)</li><li>Troubleshoot and audit access issues using CloudTrail, IAM Access Analyzer, IAM policy simulator</li><li>Validate service control policies, permission boundaries, and secure multi-account strategies (Control Tower, Organizations)</li><li>Review AWS Trusted Advisor security checks and validate Region/service selection for compliance</li><li>Implement data and infrastructure protection: data classification, encryption keys, encryption at rest (KMS) and in transit (ACM, VPN), secrets storage (Secrets Manager, Parameter Store)</li><li>Review reports/findings from Security Hub, GuardDuty, AWS Config, Amazon Inspector</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Domain 5: Networking and Content Delivery (18%)</h3><ul><li>Implement networking features and connectivity (VPC subnets, route tables, network ACLs, security groups, NAT/internet gateway)</li><li>Configure private connectivity (Session Manager, VPC endpoints, VPC peering, VPN) and network protection (AWS WAF, AWS Shield)</li><li>Configure domains, DNS services, and content delivery (Route 53 hosted zones/records, routing policies, Route 53 Resolver, CloudFront + S3 OAI, S3 static website hosting)</li><li>Troubleshoot network connectivity issues by interpreting VPC configurations</li><li>Collect and interpret logs (VPC Flow Logs, ELB access logs, AWS WAF web ACL logs, CloudFront logs)</li><li>Identify/remediate CloudFront caching issues and troubleshoot hybrid/private connectivity issues</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Domain 6: Cost and Performance Optimization (12%)</h3><ul><li>Implement cost optimization strategies (cost allocation tags, identify/remediate underutilized resources via Trusted Advisor/Compute Optimizer/Cost Explorer)</li><li>Configure AWS Budgets and billing alarms; assess usage patterns to qualify workloads for EC2 Spot Instances</li><li>Identify opportunities to use managed services (RDS, Fargate, EFS)</li><li>Implement performance optimization: recommend compute resources based on performance metrics, monitor/modify EBS and RDS configuration (Performance Insights, RDS Proxy)</li><li>Implement S3 performance features (Transfer Acceleration, multipart uploads) and enhanced EC2 capabilities (enhanced network adapter, instance store, placement groups)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1392' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DVA-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Content Domain 1: Development with AWS Services (32%)</h3><ul><li>Create fault-tolerant, resilient applications in a programming language (Java, C#, Python, JS/TS, Go) using architectural patterns (event-driven, microservices, sync/async, loosely coupled)</li><li>Create, extend, and maintain APIs; write and run unit tests; write code that interacts with AWS services via SDKs/APIs</li><li>Develop code for AWS Lambda: configure functions (env vars, memory, concurrency, timeout, layers, triggers, destinations), handle event lifecycle/errors (DLQs), integrate with AWS services, tune performance</li><li>Use data stores in application development: DynamoDB keys/indexing, query vs scan, consistency models, partition key design, caching services, data lifecycle management</li><li>Use messaging/streaming services (SQS, SNS, EventBridge, Kinesis) and implement event-driven patterns</li><li>Implement resilient application code for third-party integrations (retry logic, circuit breakers, error handling)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Content Domain 2: Security (26%)</h3><ul><li>Implement authentication/authorization for applications and AWS services (Cognito, IAM, bearer tokens, federated access, assuming IAM roles)</li><li>Define IAM principal permissions and implement application-level authorization for fine-grained access control</li><li>Implement encryption using AWS services: encryption at rest/in transit, KMS keys, client-side vs server-side encryption, certificate management (ACM/Private CA), key rotation</li><li>Manage sensitive data in application code: data classification (PII/PHI), encrypt environment variables, use Secrets Manager/Parameter Store, sanitize and mask sensitive data</li><li>Handle cross-service authentication in microservice architectures</li><li>Implement data access patterns for multi-tenant applications</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Content Domain 3: Deployment (24%)</h3><ul><li>Prepare application artifacts for deployment: manage dependencies, package configuration (containers, env vars), organize deployment directory structure and repositories</li><li>Test applications in development environments: write integration tests/mock APIs, test via API Gateway stages, test event-driven applications, deploy stack updates to staging</li><li>Automate deployment testing: create test events for Lambda/API Gateway/SAM, implement and deploy IaC templates (SAM, CloudFormation), manage per-service environments</li><li>Deploy code using AWS CI/CD services: Lambda deployment packaging, API Gateway stages/custom domains, commit-triggered build/test/deploy pipelines, orchestrated multi-environment workflows</li><li>Configure deployment strategies (blue/green, canary, rolling) and perform application rollbacks</li><li>Use labels/branches for version and release management; use runtime configuration (staging variables) for dynamic deployments</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Content Domain 4: Troubleshooting and Optimization (18%)</h3><ul><li>Assist in root cause analysis: debug code defects, interpret application metrics/logs/traces, query logs, troubleshoot deployment failures and service integration issues</li><li>Instrument code for observability: differentiate logging/monitoring/observability, implement structured logging strategy, emit custom metrics (CloudWatch EMF), add tracing annotations (X-Ray)</li><li>Implement notification alerts (quota limits, deployment completions) and configure application health checks/readiness probes</li><li>Optimize applications: define and tune concurrency, profile application performance, determine minimum memory/compute for Lambda</li><li>Implement application-level and header-based caching to improve performance</li><li>Analyze application performance issues and use logs to identify bottlenecks; optimize resource usage</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1393' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CKA</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Troubleshooting (30%)</h3><ul><li>Troubleshoot clusters and nodes</li><li>Troubleshoot cluster components</li><li>Monitor cluster and application resource usage</li><li>Manage and evaluate container output streams</li><li>Troubleshoot services and networking</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Cluster Architecture, Installation and Configuration (25%)</h3><ul><li>Manage role based access control (RBAC)</li><li>Prepare underlying infrastructure for installing a Kubernetes cluster</li><li>Create and manage Kubernetes clusters using kubeadm</li><li>Manage the lifecycle of Kubernetes clusters</li><li>Implement and configure a highly-available control plane</li><li>Use Helm and Kustomize to install cluster components</li><li>Understand extension interfaces (CNI, CSI, CRI, etc.)</li><li>Understand CRDs, install and configure operators</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Servicing and Networking (20%)</h3><ul><li>Understand connectivity between Pods</li><li>Define and enforce Network Policies</li><li>Use ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer service types and endpoints</li><li>Use the Gateway API to manage Ingress traffic</li><li>Know how to use Ingress controllers and Ingress resources</li><li>Understand and use CoreDNS</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Workloads and Scheduling (15%)</h3><ul><li>Understand application deployments and how to perform rolling update and rollbacks</li><li>Use ConfigMaps and Secrets to configure applications</li><li>Configure workload autoscaling</li><li>Understand the primitives used to create robust, self-healing, application deployments</li><li>Configure Pod admission and scheduling (limits, node affinity, etc.)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Storage (10%)</h3><ul><li>Implement storage classes and dynamic volume provisioning</li><li>Configure volume types, access modes and reclaim policies</li><li>Manage persistent volumes and persistent volume claims</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1394' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SAP-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design Solutions for Organizational Complexity (26%)</h3><ul><li>Architect network connectivity strategies (multi-VPC, hybrid DNS, Direct Connect/VPN, network segmentation)</li><li>Prescribe security controls (IAM/IAM Identity Center, cross-account access, encryption with KMS/ACM, centralized security auditing)</li><li>Design reliable and resilient architectures using RTO/RPO and disaster recovery strategies (pilot light, warm standby, multi-site)</li><li>Design a multi-account AWS environment (AWS Organizations, Control Tower, resource sharing, central logging)</li><li>Determine cost optimization and visibility strategies (Cost Explorer, Budgets, tagging, purchasing options)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design for New Solutions (29%)</h3><ul><li>Design a deployment strategy meeting business requirements (IaC/CloudFormation, CI/CD, rollback mechanisms)</li><li>Design a solution to ensure business continuity (disaster recovery, backup/restore, multi-AZ/multi-Region availability)</li><li>Determine security controls based on requirements (least privilege IAM, encryption, WAF/Shield/GuardDuty, patch management)</li><li>Design a strategy to meet reliability requirements (multi-AZ/multi-Region, auto scaling, loose coupling, Route 53 routing policies)</li><li>Design a solution to meet performance objectives (caching, buffering, purpose-built databases, rightsizing)</li><li>Determine a cost optimization strategy (pricing models, storage tiering, data transfer cost modeling)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Continuous Improvement for Existing Solutions (25%)</h3><ul><li>Determine a strategy to improve operational excellence (monitoring/logging, CI/CD deployment strategies, automation)</li><li>Determine a strategy to improve security (secrets management, least-privilege auditing, automated remediation, patch/backup practices)</li><li>Determine a strategy to improve performance (auto scaling, CloudFront/Global Accelerator, SLAs/KPIs, bottleneck analysis)</li><li>Determine a strategy to improve reliability (data replication, scaling methodologies, remediating single points of failure)</li><li>Identify opportunities for cost optimizations (Spot Instances, Savings Plans, Cost and Usage Reports, tagging)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Accelerate Workload Migration and Modernization (20%)</h3><ul><li>Select existing workloads and processes for potential migration (7Rs migration strategies, TCO evaluation, wave planning)</li><li>Determine the optimal migration approach (DMS/SCT, DataSync, Snow Family, Application Migration Service, governance model)</li><li>Determine a new architecture for existing workloads (EC2/Fargate/ECS/EKS, storage services, database platform selection)</li><li>Determine opportunities for modernization and enhancements (serverless/Lambda, decoupling, purpose-built databases, EventBridge/Step Functions)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C14' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-400</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design and implement processes and communications (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement traceability and flow of work, including GitHub Flow, feedback cycles/notifications, and integration with GitHub Projects/Azure Boards/repositories</li><li>Design and implement source, bug, and quality traceability</li><li>Design dashboards and metrics for cycle time, time to recovery, and lead time</li><li>Design metrics/queries for project planning, development, testing, security, delivery, and operations</li><li>Configure wikis, process diagrams (Markdown/Mermaid), release notes, and API documentation</li><li>Configure integration via webhooks, Azure Boards <-> GitHub repos, and Teams integration</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design and implement a source control strategy (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design a branching strategy: trunk-based, feature branch, release branch</li><li>Design and implement pull request workflows using branch policies and branch protection rules</li><li>Implement branch merging restrictions</li><li>Design a strategy for managing large files (Git LFS, git-fat) and scaling/optimizing repos (Scalar, cross-repo sharing)</li><li>Configure repository permissions and tags</li><li>Recover or remove specific data from source control using Git commands</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design and implement build and release pipelines (52.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement a package management strategy (GitHub Packages, Azure Artifacts, feeds/views, SemVer/CalVer versioning)</li><li>Design and implement a testing strategy for pipelines: quality/release gates, unit/integration/load tests, test agents, code coverage</li><li>Design and implement pipelines: GitHub Actions vs Azure Pipelines, runner/agent infrastructure, YAML pipelines, triggers, multi-stage/parallel execution, reusable templates, environment approvals/checks</li><li>Design and implement deployment strategies: blue-green, canary, ring, progressive exposure, feature flags, A/B testing, rolling deployments, hotfix paths, resiliency</li><li>Design and implement infrastructure as code (IaC): configuration management, desired state configuration (ARM, Bicep, Azure Automation State Config, Machine Configuration), Azure Deployment Environments</li><li>Maintain pipelines: monitor pipeline health, optimize cost/time/performance/concurrency, artifact retention, migrate classic to YAML pipelines</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Develop a security and compliance plan (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement authentication/authorization: Microsoft Entra service principals vs managed identities, GitHub Apps/GITHUB_TOKEN/PATs, Azure DevOps service connections, permissions/roles/security groups</li><li>Design a strategy for managing sensitive information: Azure Key Vault secrets/keys/certificates, secretless auth (workload identity federation/OIDC), Azure Pipelines secure files, preventing sensitive-data leakage</li><li>Automate security and compliance scanning: dependency, code, secret, and licensing scanning</li><li>Configure Microsoft Defender for Cloud DevOps Security and GitHub Advanced Security (for GitHub and Azure DevOps)</li><li>Automate container scanning and CodeQL analysis; automate open-source vulnerability analysis via Dependabot alerts</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Implement an instrumentation strategy (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Azure Monitor and Azure Monitor Logs integration with DevOps tools</li><li>Configure telemetry collection: Application Insights, VM/Container Insights, Monitor for Storage/Networks</li><li>Configure monitoring, insights, and charts in GitHub; configure alerts for GitHub Actions and Azure Pipelines events</li><li>Inspect infrastructure performance indicators (CPU, memory, disk, network)</li><li>Analyze usage/application performance metrics and distributed tracing via Application Insights</li><li>Interrogate logs using basic Kusto Query Language (KQL) queries</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1402' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-900</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe cloud concepts (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe Microsoft SaaS, IaaS, and PaaS concepts and use cases</li><li>Describe differences between Office 365 and Microsoft 365</li><li>Describe public, private, and hybrid cloud models</li><li>Compare costs and advantages of cloud, hybrid, and on-premises services</li><li>Describe the concept of hybrid work and flexible work</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Describe Microsoft 365 apps and services (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe productivity/content-creation capabilities of core Microsoft 365 Apps (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneNote) and project-management tools (Project, Planner, Bookings, Forms, Lists, To Do, Loop)</li><li>Describe collaboration capabilities of SharePoint, OneDrive, Stream, Exchange/Outlook, and Microsoft Teams/Teams Phone</li><li>Describe the productivity and collaboration capabilities of Microsoft 365 Copilot and Copilot Chat, and the Viva employee-experience apps</li><li>Describe device and cloud endpoint management (Intune, co-management with Configuration Manager, Endpoint Analytics, Windows Autopilot/Autopatch) and Windows 365 vs Azure Virtual Desktop</li><li>Identify deployment/update channels for Microsoft 365 Apps and WaaS deployment rings</li><li>Describe Microsoft 365 admin center, user portal, other admin-center reports, and the Copilot dashboard</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe security, compliance, privacy, and trust in Microsoft 365 (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe identity and access management with Microsoft Entra ID, including cloud/on-prem/hybrid identity</li><li>Describe MFA, self-service password reset (SSPR), and conditional access</li><li>Describe Microsoft Defender XDR / Defender for Endpoint, Office 365, Identity, Cloud Apps, and Secure Score</li><li>Describe the Zero Trust Model</li><li>Describe Microsoft Purview compliance solutions (insider risk, auditing, eDiscovery) and Information Protection (sensitivity labels, DLP)</li><li>Describe data residency support and Microsoft Priva capabilities</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Describe Microsoft 365 pricing, licensing, and support (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the Microsoft cloud services pricing model (enterprise agreements, CSPs, direct billing) and billing/bill-management options</li><li>Describe license management and differences between base and add-on licensing</li><li>Describe how to create a support request and available support options</li><li>Describe service-level agreements (SLAs) including service credits</li><li>Determine service health status via the Microsoft 365 admin center or Entra admin center</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1403' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-700</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design and implement core networking infrastructure (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement IP addressing for Azure resources (VNets, subnets, subnet delegation, public IP prefixes/BYOIP)</li><li>Design and implement name resolution (VNet DNS settings, public/private DNS zones, Azure DNS Private Resolver)</li><li>Design and implement VNet connectivity and routing (peering, Azure Virtual Network Manager, UDRs, Azure Route Server, NAT Gateway)</li><li>Monitor networks (Network Watcher, Azure Monitor for Networks, DDoS protection, Defender for Cloud secure score/attack path)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design, implement, and manage connectivity services (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design, implement, and manage a site-to-site VPN connection (gateway SKU, policy- vs route-based, local network gateway, IPsec/IKE policy)</li><li>Design, implement, and manage a point-to-site VPN connection (tunnel type, authentication incl. RADIUS/Entra ID, Always On VPN)</li><li>Design, implement, and manage Azure ExpressRoute (connectivity models, SKU/tier, Global Reach, FastPath, ExpressRoute Direct, peering)</li><li>Design and implement an Azure Virtual WAN architecture (SKU selection, virtual hub, gateway scale units, hub routing, NVA integration)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design and implement application delivery services (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement Azure Load Balancer and Azure Traffic Manager (SKU/tier, public vs internal, regional vs cross-region, Gateway Load Balancer, NAT/SNAT rules)</li><li>Design and implement Azure Application Gateway (backend pools, health probes, listeners, routing rules, TLS, rewrite rule sets)</li><li>Design and implement Azure Front Door (tiers, routing/origins/endpoints, TLS termination, caching, traffic acceleration, Private Link origin)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Design and implement private access to Azure services (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and create Azure Private Link service and private endpoints</li><li>Configure access to private endpoints and integrate Private Link/Private Endpoint with DNS</li><li>Integrate a Private Link service with on-premises clients</li><li>Choose when to use, create, and configure service endpoints and service endpoint policies</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Design and implement Azure network security services (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage network security groups (NSGs) and application security groups (ASGs), including flow logs and IP flow verify</li><li>Design and implement Azure Firewall and Azure Firewall Manager (SKU selection, deployment, rules, policies, secure hub in Virtual WAN)</li><li>Design and implement a Web Application Firewall (WAF) deployment (detection/prevention mode, rule sets on Front Door and Application Gateway, WAF policy association)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1404' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-305</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recommend a logging solution and a solution for routing logs</li><li>Recommend a monitoring solution</li><li>Recommend an authentication solution and an identity management solution</li><li>Recommend solutions for authorizing access to Azure resources and to on-premises resources</li><li>Recommend a solution to manage secrets, certificates, and keys</li><li>Recommend a structure for management groups/subscriptions/resource groups + tagging strategy, and solutions for compliance and identity governance</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design data storage solutions (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recommend a solution for storing relational data, including database service tier and compute tier</li><li>Recommend a solution for database scalability and for relational data protection</li><li>Recommend solutions for storing semi-structured data and unstructured data</li><li>Recommend a data storage solution that balances features, performance, and costs</li><li>Recommend a data solution for protection and durability</li><li>Recommend a solution for data integration and for data analysis</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design business continuity solutions (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recommend a recovery solution for Azure and hybrid workloads that meets recovery objectives</li><li>Recommend a backup and recovery solution for compute</li><li>Recommend a backup and recovery solution for databases</li><li>Recommend a backup and recovery solution for unstructured data</li><li>Recommend a high availability solution for compute</li><li>Recommend a high availability solution for relational, semi-structured, and unstructured data</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Design infrastructure solutions (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Specify compute components based on workload requirements; recommend VM-based, container-based, serverless-based, and batch-processing compute solutions</li><li>Recommend an application architecture: messaging, event-driven design, API integration, caching, configuration management, automated deployment</li><li>Evaluate a migration solution using the Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure; evaluate on-premises servers/data/applications for migration</li><li>Recommend a solution for migrating workloads to IaaS/PaaS, databases, and unstructured data</li><li>Recommend connectivity solutions to the internet and to on-premises networks</li><li>Recommend solutions to optimize network performance and security, and a load-balancing and routing solution</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1406' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SAA-C03</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Content Domain 1: Design Secure Architectures (30%)</h3><ul><li>Design secure access to AWS resources (IAM users/groups/roles/policies, MFA, role-based access, multi-account strategy with AWS Control Tower/SCPs, federated identity)</li><li>Design secure workloads and applications (VPC security components, security groups, NACLs, AWS Shield, AWS WAF, Secrets Manager, secure external network connections via VPN/Direct Connect)</li><li>Determine appropriate data security controls (encryption at rest with AWS KMS, encryption in transit with ACM/TLS, key rotation, data backup/replication, access policies for encryption keys)</li><li>Apply the AWS shared responsibility model and security best practices (principle of least privilege)</li><li>Align AWS technologies to meet compliance, data retention, and classification requirements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Content Domain 2: Design Resilient Architectures (26%)</h3><ul><li>Design scalable and loosely coupled architectures (microservices, event-driven patterns, queuing/messaging with SQS, API Gateway, load balancing, containers with ECS/EKS, serverless with Lambda/Fargate)</li><li>Determine scaling strategies (horizontal vs vertical scaling) and appropriate use of caching and read replicas</li><li>Design highly available and/or fault-tolerant architectures across Availability Zones and Regions (Route 53, multi-AZ design, immutable infrastructure)</li><li>Select and implement disaster recovery strategies (backup and restore, pilot light, warm standby, active-active failover, RPO/RTO)</li><li>Implement designs that mitigate single points of failure and ensure data durability/availability (backups, replication)</li><li>Use purpose-built AWS services and automation to improve reliability of legacy and cloud-native workloads</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Content Domain 3: Design High-Performing Architectures (24%)</h3><ul><li>Determine high-performing and/or scalable storage solutions (S3, EFS, EBS, hybrid storage)</li><li>Design high-performing and elastic compute solutions (EC2 instance types/Auto Scaling, Lambda, Fargate, container orchestration with ECS/EKS)</li><li>Determine high-performing database solutions (engine and type selection, read replicas, caching with ElastiCache, capacity planning)</li><li>Determine high-performing and/or scalable network architectures (CloudFront, Global Accelerator, load balancing, network topology design)</li><li>Determine high-performing data ingestion and transformation solutions (Kinesis streaming, Glue transformation, DataSync/Storage Gateway transfer, Athena/Lake Formation analytics)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Content Domain 4: Design Cost-Optimized Architectures (20%)</h3><ul><li>Design cost-optimized storage solutions (S3 storage tiering/lifecycle policies, backup and archival strategy, cost-effective storage service selection)</li><li>Design cost-optimized compute solutions (Spot/Reserved Instances, Savings Plans, right-sizing instance families, serverless and container cost optimization)</li><li>Design cost-optimized database solutions (choosing between DynamoDB/RDS/serverless, backup/retention policy design, database migration for cost)</li><li>Design cost-optimized network architectures (NAT gateway strategy, Direct Connect vs VPN vs internet, minimizing data transfer costs, CDN/edge caching)</li><li>Use AWS cost management tools (Cost Explorer, Budgets, Cost and Usage Report, cost allocation tags) to inform design decisions</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1407' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-900</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe core data concepts (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe ways to represent data: structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data</li><li>Identify options for data storage: common file formats, common data stores/databases, Azure datastores for common use cases</li><li>Describe common data workloads: transactional vs analytical workloads</li><li>Identify roles and responsibilities for data workloads: database administrator, data engineer, data analyst</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Identify considerations for relational data on Azure (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe relational concepts: features of relational data, normalization, common SQL statements, common database objects</li><li>Describe the Azure SQL family of products: Azure SQL Database, Azure SQL Managed Instance, SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines</li><li>Identify Azure database services for open-source database systems</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe considerations for working with non-relational data on Azure (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the capabilities of Azure storage: Azure Blob storage, Azure Files, Azure Table storage</li><li>Describe the capabilities and features of Azure Cosmos DB</li><li>Identify use cases for Azure Cosmos DB</li><li>Describe Azure Cosmos DB APIs</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Describe an analytics workload on Azure (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe common elements of large-scale analytics: data ingestion/processing, analytical data stores, Azure Databricks and Microsoft Fabric</li><li>Describe considerations for real-time data analytics: batch vs streaming data, Microsoft cloud services for real-time analytics</li><li>Describe data visualization in Microsoft Power BI: capabilities of Power BI, data models, appropriate visualizations for data</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1415' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CSSC-CLSSWB</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Chapter 1: What is Six Sigma?</h3><ul><li>Distinguish data-driven decision making from intuition/experience-based decision making</li><li>Define Six Sigma (6&#963;) as both a process-improvement methodology and a statistical concept (3.4 defects per million opportunities)</li><li>Calculate sigma level / process yield from number of opportunities and defects</li><li>Apply common Six Sigma principles: customer focus, value streams, process thinking</li><li>Identify common challenges/obstacles to Six Sigma implementation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Chapter 2: Six Sigma History and Application</h3><ul><li>Trace the development of Statistical Process Control (Shewhart/Deming roots)</li><li>Explain Toyota''s contribution to continuous process improvement and Lean</li><li>Describe Motorola''s focus on defects as the origin of Six Sigma</li><li>Explain adoption at ABB, Allied Signal, and General Electric</li><li>Describe the continued growth and cross-industry spread of Six Sigma</li><li>Apply Six Sigma knowledge appropriately within an organization</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Chapter 3: Other Process Improvement and Quality Methods</h3><ul><li>Identify other formal quality/process-improvement programs (e.g. TQM, BPR, Lean, Customer Experience Management, JumpStart) and how they differ from Six Sigma</li><li>Recognize scenarios best suited to each improvement method</li><li>Determine when to use Six Sigma over other methods: unknown root cause, widespread/undefined problems, complex multi-variable problems, cost-critical processes</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C142' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-900</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe cloud concepts (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Define cloud computing and the shared responsibility model</li><li>Define cloud models (public, private, hybrid) and appropriate use cases</li><li>Describe the consumption-based model and compare cloud pricing models</li><li>Describe serverless computing</li><li>Describe benefits of high availability, scalability, reliability, predictability, security, governance, and manageability in the cloud</li><li>Describe cloud service types: IaaS, PaaS, SaaS and appropriate use cases for each</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Describe Azure architecture and services (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe core architectural components: regions, region pairs, availability zones, datacenters, resource groups, subscriptions, management groups, and their hierarchy</li><li>Compare compute types (containers, VMs, functions) and VM options incl. Scale Sets, availability sets, Azure Virtual Desktop; describe app hosting options and virtual networking (VNets, subnets, peering, DNS, VPN Gateway, ExpressRoute, public/private endpoints)</li><li>Compare Azure Storage services, storage tiers, redundancy options, storage account types, and file-migration/movement options (AzCopy, Storage Explorer, Azure File Sync, Azure Migrate, Data Box)</li><li>Describe identity/access/security: Microsoft Entra ID and Domain Services, authentication methods (SSO, MFA, passwordless), external identities, Conditional Access, Azure RBAC, Zero Trust, defense-in-depth, and Microsoft Defender for Cloud</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe Azure management and governance (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe cost management: factors affecting Azure costs, the pricing calculator, cost management capabilities, and the purpose of tags</li><li>Describe governance and compliance tools: Microsoft Purview, Azure Policy, and resource locks</li><li>Describe management/deployment tools: Azure portal, Cloud Shell, Azure CLI, Azure PowerShell, Azure Arc, infrastructure as code, Azure Resource Manager and ARM templates</li><li>Describe monitoring tools: Azure Advisor, Azure Service Health, and Azure Monitor (Log Analytics, alerts, Application Insights)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1426' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-300</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Prepare the data (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Identify and connect to data sources or a shared semantic model; choose between DirectLake, DirectQuery, and Import</li><li>Change data source settings (credentials, privacy levels) and create/modify parameters</li><li>Profile data (statistics, column properties) and resolve inconsistencies, nulls, and import errors</li><li>Select appropriate column data types; create and transform columns; group and aggregate rows</li><li>Pivot/unpivot/transpose data; convert semi-structured data to a table; create fact and dimension tables</li><li>Identify/create appropriate keys for relationships; merge and append queries; configure data loading</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Model the data (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure table and column properties; implement role-playing dimensions</li><li>Define relationship cardinality and cross-filter direction; create a common date table</li><li>Identify use cases for calculated columns and calculated tables</li><li>Create DAX measures: single aggregations, CALCULATE, time intelligence, statistical functions, semi-additive measures</li><li>Create quick measures, calculation groups, calculated tables/columns</li><li>Optimize model performance (remove unnecessary rows/columns, use Performance Analyzer and DAX query view, reduce granularity)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Visualize and analyze the data (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Select and format appropriate visuals; apply themes, conditional formatting, slicing/filtering; create visual calculations with DAX</li><li>Use Copilot to create/suggest report pages and narrative visuals; choose when to use a paginated report</li><li>Enhance reports for usability: bookmarks, custom tooltips, visual interactions, navigation, drillthrough, sync slicers</li><li>Design reports for mobile and accessibility; configure export settings and automatic page refresh</li><li>Identify patterns and trends using the Analyze feature, grouping/binning/clustering, AI visuals, forecasting and reference lines</li><li>Detect outliers/anomalies; use Copilot to summarize the underlying semantic model</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage and secure Power BI (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure workspaces; publish, import, or update items; create dashboards and apps</li><li>Choose a distribution method; configure subscriptions and data alerts; promote or certify content</li><li>Identify when a gateway is required; configure semantic model scheduled refresh</li><li>Assign workspace roles and configure item-level access and access to semantic models</li><li>Implement row-level security roles and configure RLS group membership</li><li>Apply sensitivity labels</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1433' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SC-100</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design solutions that align with security best practices and priorities (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design a resiliency strategy for ransomware and other attacks (BCDR, secure backup/restore for hybrid & multicloud, privileged-access prioritization)</li><li>Design solutions aligned with the Microsoft Cybersecurity Reference Architectures (MCRA) and Microsoft Cloud Security Benchmark (MCSB), including AI solutions</li><li>Design solutions that align with the Zero Trust adoption framework and best practices for insider/external/supply-chain attack protection</li><li>Design a security & governance strategy based on the Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) for Azure and the Azure Well-Architected Framework (WAF), including Azure landing zones</li><li>Design a DevSecOps process aligned with CAF best practices</li><li>Design a strategy for secure AI adoption</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design security operations, identity, and compliance capabilities (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design a solution for detection and response (XDR/SIEM) and for security orchestration and automated response (SOAR) using Microsoft Sentinel and Microsoft Defender XDR</li><li>Design centralized logging/auditing (Microsoft Purview Audit) and evaluate threat detection coverage using MITRE ATT&CK matrices</li><li>Design a solution for Microsoft Entra ID including hybrid/multicloud, external identities (B2B, decentralized identity), and agent identities</li><li>Design a modern authentication and authorization strategy (Conditional Access, continuous access evaluation, risk scoring, protected actions) and harden Active Directory Domain Services</li><li>Design solutions for securing privileged access using the enterprise access model, Microsoft Entra PIM, entitlement management, and secure workstations</li><li>Design solutions for regulatory compliance using Microsoft Purview and Azure Policy, validated against Microsoft Defender for Cloud benchmarks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design security solutions for infrastructure (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design security posture management for hybrid/multicloud environments using Microsoft Defender for Cloud, Secure Score, and Azure Arc</li><li>Specify security requirements for server and client endpoints, including mobile devices, IoT/OT/ICS (Microsoft Defender for IoT), and Windows LAPS</li><li>Specify security baselines and requirements for SaaS, PaaS, and IaaS services, including containers and container orchestration</li><li>Evaluate network security designs and Security Service Edge (SSE) solutions, including Microsoft Entra Internet Access and Private Access</li><li>Design a solution for Microsoft Defender External Attack Surface Management (EASM) and Security Exposure Management attack paths</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Design security solutions for applications and data (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Evaluate security posture for Microsoft 365 workloads using Secure Score, Defender for Office 365, Defender for Cloud Apps, and Microsoft Intune</li><li>Design and implement a full lifecycle strategy for application security, including threat modeling of business-critical applications</li><li>Design a solution for workload identities, API management/security, and Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF)</li><li>Evaluate solutions for data discovery and classification, and specify priorities for mitigating threats to data</li><li>Design encryption solutions for data at rest and in transit (Azure Key Vault, infrastructure encryption) and security for data used in AI workloads</li><li>Design a security solution for data in Azure workloads (Azure SQL, Synapse Analytics, Cosmos DB, Azure Storage) including Defender for Storage/Databases</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1436' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Professional</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design innovative, scalable, and highly available cloud database solutions (32%)</h3><ul><li>Perform database capacity and usage planning (sizing based on workload metrics, performance/cost tradeoffs, compute and storage sizing)</li><li>Evaluate database high availability and disaster recovery options (multi-regional vs regional vs zonal tradeoffs, maintenance windows/notifications)</li><li>Determine how applications connect to the database (networking, key management, encryption, security, session poolers, auditing)</li><li>Evaluate appropriate database solutions on Google Cloud (managed vs unmanaged, SQL vs NoSQL, cost analysis, regulatory/compliance fit)</li><li>Consider solutions spanning multiple database technologies (federation, exports, hybrid deployments)</li><li>Leverage database technologies to support generative AI and LLM use cases</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Manage a solution that can span multiple database technologies (25%)</h3><ul><li>Determine database connectivity and access management (IAM, policies, user authentication and access)</li><li>Configure database monitoring and troubleshooting (slow queries, locking, missing indexes, RAM/CPU/storage/I/O vitals, quotas, alerts)</li><li>Design database backup and recovery solutions (backup/recovery options, export/import, RTO/RPO/PITR, data retention)</li><li>Optimize database cost and performance (scale up/out, replication strategies, query optimization)</li><li>Automate common database tasks (maintenance, scheduled exports, managed upgrades, SLA/SLO monitoring)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Migrate data solutions (23%)</h3><ul><li>Develop and execute migration strategies and plans (zero/near-zero downtime, extended outage, fallback)</li><li>Implement reverse replication from Google Cloud back to source</li><li>Plan and perform database migration including DDL/DML conversion</li><li>Determine correct database migration tools for a given scenario (including sources hosted outside Google Cloud)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud (20%)</h3><ul><li>Provision highly available database solutions in Google Cloud</li><li>Test high availability and disaster recovery strategies</li><li>Set up multi-regional replication for databases</li><li>Deploy and scale read replicas</li><li>Automate database instance provisioning</li><li>Configure monitoring for highly available databases</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C150' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Professional</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Designing and planning a Google Cloud VPC network (21%)</h3><ul><li>Design overall network architecture: network tiers (Premium/Standard), HA/failover/DR/scale, DNS topology, load balancer selection, GKE networking, IAM roles, connectivity to managed services (PSC, Serverless VPC Access), quotas/limits</li><li>Design VPC networks: standalone vs Shared VPC, interconnection method (VPC Peering, Network Connectivity Center mesh/star, PSC), IPAM strategy (subnets, IPv6, BYOIP, PUPI, Private NAT), global vs regional, MTU sizing, third-party appliance insertion with custom routes</li><li>Design resilient hybrid and multi-cloud network: Dedicated/Partner/Cross-Cloud Interconnect, Cloud VPN, SD-WAN, Direct/Verified Peering, multi-region HA/DR routing, accessing multiple VPCs and Google services privately, hybrid DNS topology, MTU sizing, interconnect encryption (MACsec, HA VPN)</li><li>Design for GKE: public/private nodes and control plane, subnet primary/secondary ranges, IP addressing options (RFC1918, non-RFC1918, PSC, PUPI), IPv6, load balancing design, node pool configuration</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implementing a VPC network (20%)</h3><ul><li>Configure VPCs: create networks/subnets/firewall rules, VPC Peering, Shared VPC and IAM permissions, Private Google Access, subnet range expansion, VPC Service Controls perimeters</li><li>Configure VPC routing: static/dynamic routing via Cloud Router, global/regional dynamic routing, tag- and priority-based routing, internal LB as next hop, custom route import/export, policy-based routing</li><li>Configure Network Connectivity Center: spoke types (VPC, hybrid, producer), topology (star, hub-and-spoke, mesh), Private NAT/PSC propagation, IP/CIDR filters, monitoring and troubleshooting</li><li>Configure and maintain GKE clusters: VPC-native clusters with alias IPs, Shared VPC clusters, private clusters/control planes, authorized networks, Dataplane V2, SNAT/IP Masquerade, network policies, Pod/service ranges, DNS (Cloud DNS, kube-dns)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Configuring managed network services (16%)</h3><ul><li>Configure load balancing: choose internal/external, regional/global, application/proxy/passthrough LB; configure backend services and autoscaling (NEGs, MIGs); balancing method, session affinity, URL maps, health checks; GKE load balancing (Gateway/Ingress controllers); Application LB traffic management (splitting, mirroring, URL rewrites)</li><li>Configure Cloud CDN: enable for MIGs, Cloud Storage, Cloud Run, and external/internet NEG backends; invalidate cached content</li><li>Configure Cloud DNS: manage zones/records, migrate to Cloud DNS, routing policies (geolocation, failover), DNSSEC, DNS forwarding and server policies, split-horizon DNS, cross-project binding and peering, GKE external-DNS integration</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Configuring and implementing hybrid and multicloud network interconnectivity (16%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Cloud Interconnect: Dedicated, Partner, and Cross-Cloud Interconnect connections and VLAN attachments; HA VPN over Interconnect; 99.9%/99.99% SLA topologies</li><li>Configure site-to-site IPSec VPN: HA VPN to on-prem gateways and other Google Cloud VPCs; Classic VPN (route-based/policy-based)</li><li>Configure Cloud Router: BGP attributes (ASN, MED, link-local, authentication), BFD, custom advertised/learned routes, legacy vs standard best-path selection</li><li>Configure Network Connectivity Center: hybrid spokes (VPN, VLAN attachment), site-to-site data transfer, router appliances, resolving transitivity issues</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Managing, monitoring, and troubleshooting network operations (14%)</h3><ul><li>Log and monitor with Google Cloud Observability: Cloud Logging for VPN, Router, VPC Service Controls, NGFW, Firewall Insights, VPC Flow Logs, DNS, NAT, NCC; monitor networking metrics</li><li>Maintain and troubleshoot connectivity: drain/redirect traffic on Application LB, troubleshoot VPNs, Cloud Interconnect, Cloud Router BGP peering, use VPC Flow Logs/firewall logs/Packet Mirroring</li><li>Use Network Intelligence Center: Network Topology, Connectivity Tests, Performance Dashboard, Firewall Insights, Network Analyzer, Flow Analyzer and VPC Flow Logs</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Configuring, implementing and managing a cloud network security solution (13%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Google Cloud Armor: edge/backend security policies, WAF rules (SQLi, XSS, RFI), DDoS/Adaptive Protection, rate limiting, bot management, Google Threat Intelligence</li><li>Configure and manage NGFW policies and VPC firewall rules: firewall strategy, hierarchical rule evaluation, Cloud NGFW for GKE/Load Balancing, layer 7 inspection (Enterprise tier), migration from VPC rules to NGFW, rule criteria and logging, micro-segmentation via tags/service accounts</li><li>Configure and secure internet egress: public Cloud NAT IP addressing and port allocation, Secure Web Proxy</li><li>Configure self-managed network virtual appliances and Packet Mirroring: multi-NIC VM routing/inspection, internal LB/policy-based routes as next hop for HA, out-of-band security integration, Packet Mirroring to self-managed collectors</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C151' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Cloud</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Digital Transformation with Google Cloud (17%)</h3><ul><li>Define cloud, digital transformation, cloud-native, open source/open standard and explain the benefits of cloud technology (scalable, flexible, agile, secure, cost-effective)</li><li>Differentiate on-premises, public, private, hybrid, and multicloud infrastructure</li><li>Describe Google Cloud''s business transformation benefits: intelligence, freedom, collaboration, trust, sustainability</li><li>Explain flexibility, scalability, reliability, elasticity, agility, and TCO, and the CapEx-to-OpEx shift</li><li>Define IaaS, PaaS, SaaS and compare their tradeoffs (TCO, flexibility, shared responsibility, staffing)</li><li>Describe the cloud shared responsibility model across IaaS/PaaS/SaaS</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Exploring Data Transformation with Google Cloud (16%)</h3><ul><li>Explain how data drives business insight and decision-making; differentiate databases, data warehouses, and data lakes</li><li>Differentiate Google Cloud data products by use case: Cloud Storage, Cloud Spanner, Cloud SQL, Cloud Bigtable, BigQuery, Firestore</li><li>Define relational vs non-relational, object storage, SQL vs NoSQL</li><li>Describe BigQuery as a serverless, managed multicloud data warehouse/analytics engine</li><li>Differentiate Cloud Storage classes: Standard, Nearline, Coldline, Archive</li><li>Describe how Looker, streaming analytics, Pub/Sub, and Dataflow make data useful and accessible</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Innovating with Google Cloud Artificial Intelligence (16%)</h3><ul><li>Define AI and ML and differentiate them from data analytics/BI; discuss the business value ML creates</li><li>Explain why high-quality data matters and the importance of explainable/responsible AI</li><li>Compare pre-trained APIs, AutoML, and custom model tradeoffs (speed, effort, differentiation, expertise)</li><li>Select the right pre-trained API for a use case: Natural Language, Vision, Cloud Translation, Speech-to-Text, Text-to-Speech</li><li>Discuss BigQuery ML, AutoML, and building custom models with the Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform (formerly Vertex AI)</li><li>Recognize TensorFlow and Cloud TPU as ML build/training tools</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Modernize Infrastructure and Applications with Google Cloud (17%)</h3><ul><li>Define migration terms: workload, retire, retain, rehost, replatform, refactor, reimagine</li><li>Define compute terms: VMs, containers, microservices, serverless, preemptible VMs, Kubernetes, autoscaling, load balancing</li><li>Discuss serverless products (Cloud Run, App Engine, Cloud Functions) and container products (GKE, Cloud Run)</li><li>Explain the business value of APIs and Apigee API Management</li><li>Discuss hybrid/multicloud strategy and GKE as a single control plane</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section 5: Trust and Security with Google Cloud (17%)</h3><ul><li>Describe top cybersecurity threats and cloud vs on-prem security differences</li><li>Explain control, compliance, confidentiality, integrity, and availability in cloud security</li><li>Describe Google''s defense-in-depth infrastructure, encryption, authentication/authorization/auditing, 2SV, and IAM</li><li>Describe DDoS protection via Google Cloud Armor and Security Operations (SecOps)</li><li>Discuss Google Cloud''s trust principles, transparency reports, third-party audits, data sovereignty/residency</li><li>Describe the Compliance Resource Center and Compliance Reports Manager</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Section 6: Scaling with Google Cloud Operations (17%)</h3><ul><li>Discuss cloud financial governance, resource hierarchy, quota policies, budget thresholds, and Cloud Billing Reports</li><li>Describe operational excellence: resilient, fault-tolerant, scalable infrastructure for high availability and disaster recovery</li><li>Define key DevOps and SRE terms</li><li>Describe Google Cloud Customer Care and the support case lifecycle</li><li>Discuss Google Cloud''s sustainability commitments and related products</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C154' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>N/A</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Managing user accounts, domains, and Directory (20%)</h3><ul><li>Manage the user life cycle: manual/automated provisioning-deprovisioning, third-party IdP/SAML SSO, GCDS/Directory Sync, license and password administration</li><li>Design and create organizational unit (OU) hierarchies aligned to org structure</li><li>Manage groups: distribution lists, collaborative inboxes, dynamic groups, security groups</li><li>Manage domains: add/verify primary & secondary domains, domain aliases</li><li>Manage buildings and bookable resources (rooms, equipment, booking permissions)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Managing core Workspace services (23%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Gmail: MX records, mail routing, content compliance, spam/phishing/malware controls, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, mail migration</li><li>Configure Drive and Docs: default sharing, trust rules, Shared Drives, storage quotas, Drive Labels, template settings</li><li>Configure Calendar: resource calendars, booking policies, sharing/delegation, external sharing controls</li><li>Configure Meet and Chat: enablement, safety settings, recordings/transcripts, chat history/moderation</li><li>Administer generative AI (Gemini) settings and usage reporting</li><li>Support Workspace development use cases via AppSheet and Apps Script</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Managing data governance and compliance (15%)</h3><ul><li>Use Google Vault for eDiscovery: retention policies, legal holds, search/export, audit reports</li><li>Create and manage DLP rules across Gmail, Drive, and Chat based on content detectors/regex</li><li>Create and manage Drive trust rules to limit or block sharing by OU, domain, or user</li><li>Determine data storage/export approach: Google Takeout settings, Data Export tool, data region/geography</li><li>Classify data using labels for DLP, default, and AI-based classification</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Managing security policies and access controls (20%)</h3><ul><li>Secure user access: password policy enforcement, 2-step verification methods, context-aware access, Session Control</li><li>Assign prebuilt and custom administrative roles and delegate admin tasks</li><li>Report, audit, and investigate security risks using audit/investigation tools and the security center (security health page)</li><li>Create activity rules and alerts for security events</li><li>Enable and restrict Google Workspace Marketplace, Play Store, and third-party SSO applications</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Managing browsers and endpoints (10%)</h3><ul><li>Determine when to use basic, advanced, or third-party mobile device management</li><li>Apply security policies to mobile devices, including BYOD, via Google basic mobile management</li><li>Offboard mobile devices from former employees</li><li>Apply Chrome browser policies (update, offline access) and enroll browsers</li><li>Manage Chrome extensions/apps (allow, block, force-install) by OU or group</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Monitoring and troubleshooting common issues (13%)</h3><ul><li>Diagnose issues via Admin console audit logs and the Google Workspace Status Dashboard</li><li>Troubleshoot email delivery problems using Email Log Search and SPF/DKIM/DMARC headers via Admin Toolbox</li><li>Troubleshoot Calendar, Drive, and Meet issues (sync, sharing/permissions, offline access, quality)</li><li>View and manage reports/audit logs: app usage, storage limits, device activity</li><li>Use Google support resources: HAR file generation, log collection, and best practices for opening a support case</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C155' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-120</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Migrate SAP workloads to Azure (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Identify requirements for target infrastructure (sizing, supported deployment scenarios, compute/storage/network requirements, licensing and cost implications, migration strategy: lift-and-shift, lift-shift-migrate, lift-shift-migrate to HANA)</li><li>Design and implement an Azure environment to support SAP workloads (authorization/access control, governance via Azure Policy, authentication, management hierarchy, Azure landing zones for SAP)</li><li>Design and implement integration with SAP RISE (networking, compute/network/storage services, data management integration, identity and security integration)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design and implement an infrastructure to support SAP workloads on Azure (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement a compute solution (SAP-certified VM selection, Azure VM extension for SAP, OS deployment via Marketplace/custom image, IaC deployment via Bicep/ARM, SAP Deployment Automation Framework, Azure Center for SAP solutions)</li><li>Design and implement networking (virtual networks/subnets, Accelerated Networking, proximity placement groups, latency requirements, network security, service/private endpoints, DNS, ExpressRoute)</li><li>Design and implement storage (storage type selection, disk striping vs simple volumes, storage security, data protection, disk caching, Write Accelerator, encryption, Azure NetApp Files, Azure Files)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design and implement high availability and disaster recovery (HADR) (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement high availability (SLA design, availability sets/zones, load balancing, clustering for HANA/SCS and SQL, Pacemaker and STONITH, Azure fence agent/SBD, storage-level replication, restart of SAP systems)</li><li>Design and implement disaster recovery (Azure Site Recovery strategy, regional DR design, network configuration for DR, backup strategy for SLA, backup/snapshot policies, backup and restore, DR testing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Maintain SAP workloads on Azure (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Optimize performance and costs (Azure Advisor recommendations, network performance analysis, Savings Plans/Reserved Instances, VM resizing, storage cost optimization, data archiving, application server/database performance and cost tuning)</li><li>Monitor and maintain SAP on Azure (Azure Monitor for VMs, HA, storage, networking; Azure Network Watcher; Azure Monitor for SAP solutions; Azure Backup management; start/stop and manage instances via Azure Center for SAP solutions; SAP Landscape Management (LaMa) connector for Azure)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1745' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-140</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Plan and implement an Azure Virtual Desktop infrastructure (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan, implement, and manage networking (RDP Shortpath/Multipath, QoS, Azure Private Link)</li><li>Plan and implement storage for user data (FSLogix, storage accounts, file shares, Azure NetApp Files)</li><li>Plan host pools and session hosts (resource groups, OS, licensing, host pool architecture)</li><li>Implement host pools and session hosts via Azure portal, PowerShell, CLI, ARM/Bicep</li><li>Create and manage session host images (manual, VM Image Builder, Azure Compute Gallery)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Plan and implement identity and security (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement identity integration (AD DS, Microsoft Entra ID, Entra Domain Services)</li><li>Plan and implement Azure RBAC and Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policies</li><li>Plan and implement authentication options (passwordless, smart card, MFA, SSO)</li><li>Plan and implement security via Microsoft Defender for Cloud, Defender Antivirus, Defender for Endpoint</li><li>Implement network security (UDRs, NSGs, Azure Firewall, Bastion/JIT access)</li><li>Plan Windows threat protection features, confidential VMs, and Trusted Launch</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Plan and implement user environments and apps (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement FSLogix (Profile Containers, ODFC containers, Cloud Cache, app masking)</li><li>Plan and implement user experience and client settings (client choice/deployment, device/multimedia redirection, printing, RDP properties, session timeouts, Start VM on Connect)</li><li>Choose a method for deploying apps and configure application groups</li><li>Publish RemoteApps and manage Microsoft 365 Apps, OneDrive, Microsoft Teams, browsers</li><li>Configure dynamic application delivery via App attach</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Monitor and maintain an Azure Virtual Desktop infrastructure (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure log collection and analysis for session hosts</li><li>Monitor Azure Virtual Desktop using Azure Monitor and customize AVD Insights workbooks</li><li>Optimize session host capacity/performance and implement autoscaling</li><li>Recommend an update strategy for session hosts</li><li>Plan and implement disaster recovery and multi-region implementation</li><li>Design and implement backup strategy, including FSLogix profiles, personal desktops, and images</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1747' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-420</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design and implement data models (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design a non-relational data model for Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL (multi-entity containers, denormalization, referencing, partition key/id/unique keys, TTL, versioning)</li><li>Design a data partitioning strategy (choose partition key, synthetic and hierarchical partition keys, evaluate cross-partition query cost, throughput/data distribution)</li><li>Plan and implement sizing and scaling (serverless vs provisioned vs free tier, database-level throughput, cost of global distribution)</li><li>Implement client connectivity options in the SDK (gateway vs direct mode, singleton client, region config, SDK logging)</li><li>Implement data access using the SQL query language (arrays, nested objects, aggregation, correlated subqueries, functions)</li><li>Implement data access using the SDKs (point vs query operations, patch, transactional batch, bulk, optimistic concurrency, consistency, pagination, TTL) and server-side programming with JavaScript (stored procedures, triggers, UDFs)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Design and implement data distribution (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement a replication strategy (automatic/manual failover, consistency models, RU cost and latency impact)</li><li>Design and implement multi-region writes</li><li>Implement a custom conflict resolution policy for Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL</li><li>Specify application connections to replicated data</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Integrate an Azure Cosmos DB solution (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Enable Azure Cosmos DB analytical workloads (Fabric Mirroring vs Spark connector, analytical store, Synapse Spark/SQL queries, Change Data Capture)</li><li>Integrate events with other applications using Azure Functions and Event Hubs</li><li>Denormalize data using Change Feed and Azure Functions</li><li>Enforce referential integrity and aggregate data using Change Feed and Azure Functions</li><li>Archive data using Change Feed and Azure Functions</li><li>Implement Azure AI Search for an Azure Cosmos DB solution</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Optimize an Azure Cosmos DB solution (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Optimize query performance (adjust indexes, calculate RU cost of queries/point operations, integrated cache)</li><li>Design and implement change feeds (Azure Functions trigger, change feed estimator, denormalization/referential enforcement/aggregation/archiving via change feed)</li><li>Define and implement an indexing strategy (read-heavy vs write-heavy, index types, custom indexing policy, composite indexes, index performance tuning)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Maintain an Azure Cosmos DB solution (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor and troubleshoot (response status codes, Normalized RU Consumption, server-side latency, Azure Monitor alerts and resource logs, partition throughput/distribution, security logging)</li><li>Implement backup and restore (periodic vs continuous backup, point-in-time restore)</li><li>Implement security (encryption keys, network access control, RBAC for control plane, Microsoft Entra ID for data plane, CORS, Key Vault, Always Encrypted)</li><li>Implement data movement (client SDK bulk, Azure Data Factory/Synapse pipelines, Kafka connector, Stream Analytics, Spark connector, IoT Hub endpoint)</li><li>Implement a DevOps process (declarative vs imperative operations, ARM templates for provisioning and indexing policies, standard/autoscale migration and regional failover via PowerShell/CLI)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1750' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-600</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Maintain a data analytics solution (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement workspace-level, item-level, row-level, column-level, object-level, and file-level access controls</li><li>Apply sensitivity labels to items and endorse items</li><li>Configure version control for a workspace and manage Power BI Desktop projects (.pbip)</li><li>Create and configure deployment pipelines</li><li>Perform impact analysis of downstream dependencies (lakehouses, warehouses, dataflows, semantic models)</li><li>Deploy/manage semantic models via the XMLA endpoint; create reusable assets (.pbit, .pbids, shared semantic models)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Prepare data (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create data connections; discover data via OneLake catalog and Real-Time hub; ingest/access data and choose between data stores</li><li>Implement OneLake integration for Eventhouse and semantic models</li><li>Create views, functions, and stored procedures; enrich data with new columns/tables</li><li>Implement a star schema; denormalize, aggregate, merge/join data</li><li>Identify and resolve duplicate data, missing data, or null values; convert column data types; filter data</li><li>Query and analyze data using the Visual Query Editor, SQL, KQL, and DAX</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement and manage semantic models (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Choose a storage mode; implement a star schema and relationships (bridge tables, many-to-many)</li><li>Write DAX calculations using variables and functions (iterators, table filtering, windowing, information functions)</li><li>Implement calculation groups, dynamic format strings, and field parameters</li><li>Configure large semantic model storage format; design and build composite models</li><li>Implement performance improvements in queries/report visuals and improve DAX performance</li><li>Configure Direct Lake (default fallback, refresh behavior, Direct Lake on OneLake vs SQL analytics endpoint); implement incremental refresh</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1751' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-700</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement and manage an analytics solution (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Microsoft Fabric workspace settings (Spark, domain, OneLake, Apache Airflow)</li><li>Implement lifecycle management in Fabric: version control, database projects, deployment pipelines</li><li>Configure security and governance: workspace/item-level access, row/column/object/folder-file-level access, dynamic data masking, sensitivity labels, item endorsement, audit logs, OneLake security</li><li>Orchestrate processes: choose between Dataflow Gen2, pipeline and notebook; design schedules and event-based triggers; implement orchestration patterns with notebooks and pipelines (parameters, dynamic expressions)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Ingest and transform data (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement full and incremental data loads; prepare data for a dimensional model; design a loading pattern for streaming data</li><li>Ingest and transform batch data: choose data store and transformation tool (Dataflows Gen2, notebooks, KQL, T-SQL), create OneLake shortcuts, implement mirroring, ingest via pipelines</li><li>Transform data using PySpark, SQL, and KQL; denormalize, group/aggregate data; handle duplicate, missing, and late-arriving data</li><li>Ingest and transform streaming data: choose streaming engine, use Eventstreams/Spark structured streaming/KQL, choose native tables vs OneLake shortcuts, create windowing functions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Monitor and optimize an analytics solution (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor Fabric items: data ingestion, data transformation, semantic model refresh, configure alerts</li><li>Identify and resolve errors in pipelines, Dataflow Gen2, notebooks, Eventhouse, Eventstream, T-SQL, and OneLake shortcuts</li><li>Optimize performance of Lakehouse tables, pipelines, data warehouse, Eventstreams/Eventhouses, Spark, and query performance</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1752' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-230</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Manage cases in Customer Service (53%)</h3><ul><li>Implement record creation/update rules and configure the case resolution experience, security roles, and timeline control</li><li>Create and administer knowledge management: internal/external search, tables, translated articles, AI suggestions and Copilot-led article creation</li><li>Manage collaboration via Microsoft Teams chat, calls, and AI/rules-based suggested contacts</li><li>Manage Copilot in Service features: Ask a Question, case/timeline/conversation summaries, Draft a Response, Case Management Agent, and agent plug-in/knowledge-source integration</li><li>Create and manage SLAs for cases: SLA settings, Power Automate actions, SLA items/KPIs, warning/success actions, and timer controls</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Configure representative experience and routing (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure workstreams, queues, and routing for records</li><li>Configure work classification, assignment rules, and basic routing rulesets</li><li>Configure skills-based routing, skill finder models, and capacity profiles</li><li>Configure productivity tools: scripts, slugs, and macros</li><li>Configure the Copilot Service workspace: session templates, experience profiles, Inbox custom views, application tab templates</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Extend Customer Service (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure forms, views, columns, tables, and relationships</li><li>Configure model-driven app components, Dataverse search, and alerts/in-app notifications</li><li>Create and manage email templates</li><li>Trigger, personalize, and distribute a Customer Voice survey</li><li>Populate and analyze survey results against cases and conversations</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1753' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-240</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Configure field service applications (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure core Field Service components: security for standard user groups, territories/postal codes/organizational units, characteristics & proficiency models, resource roles/categories, Field Service settings, trades & trade coverages, not-to-exceed values, Copilot summary</li><li>Configure product and service pricing, minimum charge amounts/durations, pricing rules, price lists</li><li>Configure bookable resources: frontline workers, start/end locations, pay types & rates, working hours, time off, technician time tracking, facilities/equipment</li><li>Configure scheduling of multiple resources: requirement group templates, resource pools and crews, schedule board visualization</li><li>Integrate other tools with Field Service: Dynamics 365 Remote Assist, Dynamics 365 Guides, Field Service Portal</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Manage work orders and customer assets (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure the work order lifecycle: work order types/resolutions, booking status and sub-status values</li><li>Create and manage work orders, including price list/SLA/entitlement association, closing/resolution, and Copilot-in-Outlook creation</li><li>Manage incidents: incident types & suggestions, requirement group templates, service tasks, products/services</li><li>Create and manage agreements: agreement configuration, automatic work order generation, booking setup, invoicing, entitlements</li><li>Manage inspections: inspection templates, association with work orders/customer assets, standalone inspections</li><li>Configure customer assets: creation/management, automatic asset creation, child assets, 3D asset models, functional locations, property templates</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Schedule and dispatch work orders (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage scheduling options: schedule board and schedule assistant, fulfillment preferences, quick scheduling, multi-day resource requirements, appointments</li><li>Configure, customize, and manage schedule boards, including the Requirements panel and board settings</li><li>Configure the schedule assistant: settings, filtering constraints, troubleshooting</li><li>Configure Universal Resource Scheduling: enabling scheduling on a table, geocoding, booking timestamps/journals/actuals</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage the Field Service mobile app (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Deliver work orders via the mobile app: completing tasks/bookings/follow-ups/signatures/images/technician reports</li><li>Service and maintain customer assets including IoT devices; perform inspections and ad hoc inspections</li><li>Manage working offline and perform time entry; launch related apps (Remote Assist, Guides)</li><li>Set up the mobile app: security roles, form/view/page/navigation customization, location tracking & geofencing</li><li>Configure mobile offline profiles, push notifications, barcode features, and technician service reports</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Manage inventory and purchasing by using the built-in inventory management system (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Set up inventory and warehouses; view and adjust product inventory levels</li><li>Transfer inventory between warehouses; manually update inventory via inventory journals</li><li>Create purchase orders and receivable product lists</li><li>Create return merchandise authorizations, return-to-vendor transactions, and finalize returns</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Implement Microsoft Power Platform (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure model-driven apps: create and configure forms and views</li><li>Configure navigation for model-driven apps</li><li>Create task-specific canvas apps and custom pages; embed apps in Field Service</li><li>Use Power Automate cloud flows to automate tasks and enhance Field Service</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1754' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-280</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement Dynamics 365 Sales (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure core Dynamics 365 Sales functionality: predictive lead/opportunity scoring, lead qualification, opportunity pipeline view, Copilot in Sales, sales order processing (quotes/orders/invoices)</li><li>Set up the product catalog: product lifecycle (create/revise/clone/retire), product bundles, product families, price lists and discount lists</li><li>Configure goals and forecasting, including rollup queries and forecast templates</li><li>Configure and use Sales Insights (standard vs. premium features, relationship analytics, conversation intelligence)</li><li>Configure sales engagement: Sales accelerator, sequences, assignment rules, lead/opportunity segments</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Configure and customize Dataverse and model-driven apps (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Perform tasks in the Power Platform Environment Settings app: email/Word/Excel templates, duplicate detection</li><li>Configure Dataverse table components: tables, fields, relationship behaviors, auditing, connection roles</li><li>Implement business logic: business rules, formula/rollup columns, business process flows, Dataverse connector in cloud flows</li><li>Customize the user experience: forms/views, timeline control, embedded Power BI, model-driven app creation/visualizations</li><li>Manage security: hierarchy security, security roles, owner/access teams, access checker, Entra ID groups, column-level security</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Demonstrate Dynamics 365 Customer Insights capabilities (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure core Customer Insights - Journeys functionality: personalized marketing emails, journeys, marketing forms, text messages</li><li>Create marketing segments and build journeys using unified profiles/segments from Customer Insights - Data</li><li>Configure consent management (Compliance Profiles, Consent Center) and differentiate segment types across Sales/Journeys/Data</li><li>Create and manage events: event creation, registration forms, waitlists and attendees</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Extend and enhance Dynamics 365 Sales capabilities (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement collaboration features: document management configuration</li><li>Configure Microsoft Teams calling, dialer, and Teams collaboration</li><li>Manage sales data and interactions in Outlook: track/create records, apply email templates, add sales literature/knowledge articles</li><li>Customize the Dynamics 365 App for Outlook</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1755' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-310</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement financial management (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design and configure the chart of accounts, financial dimensions, and account structures/advanced rules</li><li>Configure ledgers, currencies, exchange types/rates, and currency revaluation</li><li>Implement and manage journals, including approvals, intercompany accounting, and Excel-based entry</li><li>Implement and manage cash and bank, including bank reconciliation and cash flow forecasting</li><li>Perform periodic processes: period/year-end closing, financial consolidation and elimination, financial reporting</li><li>Configure, collect, and report sales and withholding taxes</li><li>Implement cost management (cost groups, item model groups, inventory costing/closing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement accounts receivable, credit, collections, and subscription billing (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage accounts receivable: customers, free text invoices, sales order invoicing, payments</li><li>Configure customer posting profiles, change approvals, and AR foreign currency revaluation</li><li>Manage credit and collections: credit management, collections activities, aging, write-offs, interest notes</li><li>Configure and manage subscription billing: billing schedules, contract billing, milestone setup</li><li>Configure revenue and expense deferrals/recognition and process recognition schedules</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement and manage accounts payable and expenses (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure invoice validation policies and invoice matching setup</li><li>Configure vendor groups, vendors, vendor posting profiles, and shared vendors</li><li>Process purchase order invoices/credit memos, prepayments, and recurring vendor invoices</li><li>Configure vendor payment methods, bank accounts, change approvals, and AP foreign currency revaluation</li><li>Process and generate vendor payments, centralized payments, and vendor invoice automation</li><li>Configure and use expense management: categories, per diem, mileage, and expense reports</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage budgeting (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure budgeting components: budget models, codes, allocation terms, transfer rules</li><li>Create and manage budget register entries and compare budgeted vs. actual values</li><li>Configure budget controls: parameters, fund availability options, rules and groups, over-budget permissions</li><li>Activate or deactivate budget control configurations</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Manage fixed assets (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage fixed asset groups, posting profiles, parameters, books, and depreciation profiles</li><li>Process fixed asset acquisitions via purchase orders, journals, and projects</li><li>Process fixed asset depreciation, disposal (including via free text invoices), split, reclassification, and transfer</li><li>Create fixed asset budgets and transfer to the budgeting module</li><li>Process acquisition and depreciation for derived books</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1756' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-330</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement product information management (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and release products and product variants; create BOMs and BOM versions; configure category hierarchies</li><li>Configure inventory, storage, tracking, and product dimension groups; item model groups; reservation hierarchies; unit sequence groups</li><li>Create/assign bar codes and GTIN codes; configure product unit conversions and default order settings</li><li>Configure and maintain costing versions (standard/planned costs); price groups; trade agreements (prices/discounts)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement inventory and asset management (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and process inventory journals (BOM, item arrival, output, transfer, movement, adjustment, counting) and transfer orders</li><li>Configure inventory closing/adjustment process, blocking, batch disposition codes, ABC classification reporting</li><li>Manage quality: nonconformances, quality associations, quality/quarantine orders</li><li>Configure asset management: work orders, assets/asset types, capacity, preventive/reactive maintenance, asset loans, lifecycle models</li><li>Implement asset management: maintenance plans, functional locations, maintenance requests, work order consumption and scheduling</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement and manage supply chain processes (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement procurement and sourcing: vendors, purchase requisitions/RFQs/POs, purchase agreements, vendor rebates, consignment inventory, vendor returns, procurement workflows</li><li>Implement landed cost: landed cost parameters, voyage statuses, cost estimations, tracking control center, cost type codes and auto-costs</li><li>Implement common sales and marketing features: customers, sales agreements, sales quotations/orders/returns, commissions, intercompany orders, customer rebates, ATP/CTP, product bundles</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Implement warehouse management and transportation management (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure warehouse management: sites, warehouses, locations, work policies, location directives, wave/load/work templates, labels, packing, inbound/outbound processes</li><li>Perform warehouse management processes: replenishment, load planning workbench, inventory movements via warehouse work, cycle counting, Warehouse Management mobile app, containerization, cross docking</li><li>Implement transportation management: shipping carriers, load/shipment planning, freight bills/invoices, route plans/guides, dock appointment scheduling, freight reconciliation</li><li>Implement the Warehouse Management mobile app: device menus/menu items, detours, install/configure app, manage warehouse workers</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Implement master planning (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure master planning: coverage groups and item coverage, master planning parameters and master plans, positive/negative days, action messages/delay/time fences, period templates</li><li>Manage master plans: run master planning and analyze results, evaluate/process planned purchase and transfer orders, Supply Schedule form, safety margins, safety stock journals</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1757' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-335</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Configure products (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure formula items, planning items, co-products, and by-products; catch weight items and handling policies</li><li>Configure inventory batches, batch attributes, lot inheritance, and hazardous materials/export control</li><li>Create and manage product configuration model components, calculations, BOM lines, and route operations for constraint-based configurations</li><li>Validate, approve, and test product configuration models and configure their pricing</li><li>Design the engineering product lifecycle: engineering categories, product readiness/release policies</li><li>Create, release, and process engineering change requests and change orders</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Configure production prerequisites (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage work calendars, resource capabilities, resources, and resource groups</li><li>Create and manage operations and routes, including routes to manage scrap</li><li>Create production units, groups, pools, and production journal names; configure production control parameters</li><li>Manage production reservations (partial/re-reservations) and warehouse picking/put-away processes for a unified (mixed mode) manufacturing process</li><li>Configure costing sheets, indirect costs, cost groups, costing versions, and cost categories</li><li>Calculate and activate item cost prices, configure production posting profiles, and analyze production cost variances</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement production methods (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage the discrete production order lifecycle (create, estimate, schedule, release, start, report as finished, end) and related BOM/BOM versions</li><li>Create and process picking list, job card/route card, and report-as-finished journals; substitute materials</li><li>Configure process manufacturing: batch reservations, consolidated batch orders, batch balancing/sequencing, formulas and formula versions</li><li>Create and process batch orders (incl. co-products/by-products) and rework batch orders</li><li>Create value streams, production flows, and kanban rules</li><li>Process and manage kanban orders using kanban boards</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Configure and manage production control (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement subcontracting for discrete and process manufacturing, including BOM/formula lines, resources, routes, and warehouses</li><li>Create and process purchase orders and transfer orders for subcontracting items and service prices</li><li>Configure manufacturing execution features and the production floor execution interface for production/batch orders</li><li>Configure time and attendance prerequisites and calculate/approve time registrations</li><li>Configure production scheduling parameters, infinite/finite scheduling, and capacity for machines/labor/tooling</li><li>Set up and run operations/job scheduling, including Gantt-based production job scheduling</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Implement additional supply chain management features (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure Rebate management parameters and reduction principles; process, review, and post rebates</li><li>Evaluate and process planned production and kanban orders; configure intercompany master planning</li><li>Configure forecast models, plans, and parameters; run and adjust demand forecasting</li><li>Execute explosion and validate planning results; configure supply chain calendars</li><li>Configure Demand Driven Material Requirements Planning (DDMRP)</li><li>Configure the Planning Optimization Add-in and manage demand forecast lines</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1758' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-500</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Plan the architecture and solution design (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Differentiate between the cloud and on-premises versions of finance and operations apps</li><li>Extend the functionality of finance and operations apps into the Microsoft ecosystem</li><li>Manage environments by using Lifecycle Services (LCS) tools and components</li><li>Manage package deployments between environments</li><li>Manage Unified Developer Experience (UDE) developer environments in Power Platform admin center</li><li>Manage environments by using the Implementation portal</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Apply developer tools (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage extension models</li><li>Manage metadata by using Application Explorer</li><li>Synchronize data dictionary changes with the application database</li><li>Create, check out, review, and check in code via Azure DevOps version control</li><li>Branch and merge code; compare code and resolve version conflicts</li><li>Implement continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design and develop AOT elements (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and extend forms, menus, and menu items</li><li>Create and use label files</li><li>Create and extend tables, views, queries, and maps</li><li>Create and extend data entities</li><li>Create and extend classes</li><li>Add event handler methods, attributes, or modifiers to a class</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Develop and test code (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement structured programming constructs of X++ and CRUD data operations</li><li>Implement variable scoping, inheritance, and abstraction concepts</li><li>Implement query objects, the QueryBuilder class, and Chain of Command (CoC)</li><li>Implement the SysOperation, workflow, and SysExtensionSerializer frameworks</li><li>Assess the extensibility of code and avoid breaking changes</li><li>Create and run unit tests by using the SysTest framework, Task recorder, and Test Explorer</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Implement reporting (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and modify report data sources and supporting classes; implement reporting security</li><li>Differentiate among reporting datastores and determine when to use a specific reporting tool</li><li>Create, modify, and deploy reports by using SSRS</li><li>Create and modify reports by using Power BI, Microsoft Excel, and Electronic reporting</li><li>Design and implement key performance indicators (KPIs) and drill-through workspace elements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Integrate and manage data solutions (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Contrast data integration patterns and select an appropriate data integration API</li><li>Consume external web services by using RESTful APIs and SOAP; implement custom services and Batch OData API</li><li>Import and export data using entities, composite/aggregate data entities, and data projects</li><li>Enable change tracking for entities and monitor entity status/availability</li><li>Integrate Dataverse with finance and operations apps via dual-write and virtual entities</li><li>Implement business events and Azure Key Vault</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Implement security and optimize performance (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and extend duties, roles, and privileges; enforce security policies</li><li>Implement Extensible Data Security (XDS) policies</li><li>Apply caching mechanisms for tables/forms; implement global cache and singleton</li><li>Create and modify temporary tables; assess set-based vs. row-based queries for optimization</li><li>Capture and analyze traces by using Trace Parser</li><li>Create and modify indexes for tables and views; implement Async and Sandbox frameworks</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1759' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-700</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Architect solutions (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Identify operational/organizational challenges and existing business processes; identify optimization opportunities</li><li>Gather data migration requirements and expected data migration volumes; categorize business requirements and perform gap-fit analyses</li><li>Map business requirements to functional components and the business process catalog</li><li>Evaluate build-vs-buy for gap requirements; identify Microsoft/ISV solution components; apply the Success by Design framework</li><li>Create overall solution architecture diagrams</li><li>Document the solution blueprint: org/company/locations, implementation timeline and roll-out strategy, instances/environments/solution components, required security strategy</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Define solution strategies (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Select a deployment strategy: deployment model, One Version/release cadence, phased delivery, upgrade tooling</li><li>Define an application lifecycle management (ALM) strategy: code/data flow, Power Platform solution management, build automation, roll-back strategy</li><li>Determine a data management strategy: transactional vs historical vs master data, data quality/cleansing/transformation, migration and cut-over/retention plans</li><li>Define the security architecture: Azure vs finance-and-operations vs infrastructure security, record-level and role-based security, segregation of duties</li><li>Define the integration architecture: select integration patterns (OData, Power Platform, Batch Data API, business events, Azure Synapse Link, dual-write), design integrations and error-handling/testing strategy</li><li>Define the business intelligence and reporting architecture: data sources, tool selection (Power BI, SSRS, Electronic Reporting), printing requirements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Manage implementations (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage interactions with FastTrack: eligibility, engagement types/roles, workshop types, go-live checklist, Implementation Portal</li><li>Determine support options: post-go-live support plan, SLAs, Power Platform Admin Center Support tool</li><li>Determine licensing requirements: license types, License Sizing estimator, ongoing licensing cost estimation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage testing (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Define a testing strategy covering all required test types, including regression testing and automation opportunities</li><li>Review test coverage for business scenarios; select tools (RSAT, SysTest, Postman, ATL, Azure DevOps Test Plans, Leapworks)</li><li>Define a performance testing strategy: goals/requirements, monitoring tools, benchmarks and success criteria</li><li>Design a performance and load testing strategy and troubleshoot performance issues</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1760' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-800</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Set up Business Central (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure a company: Assisted Setup, configuration worksheets/packages, journal opening balances, data migration</li><li>Manage security: user profiles, permissions and permission sets, security filters, security groups, security auditing</li><li>Set up core functionality: report layouts, job queues, number series, enable Copilot and agent capabilities</li><li>Set up dimensions: dimension values, global/shortcut dimensions, default dimensions for master data and account types, dimension priorities</li><li>Manage approvals by using workflows: native workflows, notification system, approval/workflow user groups</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Configure financials (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Set up financial management: general ledger setup, accounting periods, payment terms, deferrals, currencies/exchange rates, payment methods</li><li>Manage the chart of accounts: GL accounts, account categories/subcategories, financial reporting, GL allocations</li><li>Set up posting groups: specific/general posting groups, general and inventory posting setup, multiple posting groups</li><li>Set up journals and bank accounts, journal templates/batches, recurring journal templates</li><li>Set up accounts payable and accounts receivable: vendor/customer accounts, Purchases & Payables / Sales & Receivables setup, payment journals, cash receipt journals, payment registration</li><li>Configure fixed assets: depreciation books, fixed asset classes/subclasses, depreciation methods</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Configure sales and purchasing (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Set up inventory: inventory setup, item categories/attributes/units of measure/variants, locations, costing methods, stockkeeping units</li><li>Configure master data for sales: customer settings including shipping agents, locations, shipping addresses</li><li>Configure master data for purchasing: vendor settings including order address, lead time, locations</li><li>Manage pricing and discounts: vendor purchase prices, customer sales prices, purchase/sales line and invoice discounts</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Perform Business Central operations (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Perform basic tasks: design vs. customize vs. personalize pages, filters, Edit in Excel, data analysis mode</li><li>Process purchases: quotes, purchase orders, receipts, posted invoices, recurring/blanket purchase lines, deferrals</li><li>Process sales: quotes, sales orders/invoices, item availability, shipments, recurring/blanket sales lines, deferrals</li><li>Process financial documents: purchase/sales invoices and credit memos, combining shipments/receipts, corrections, prepayments</li><li>Process journals and payments: payment journals, cash receipts, applying/reversing entries, bank reconciliation, recurring journals, GL allocations, currency revaluation, Dimension Correction Tool</li><li>Process fixed asset and inventory transactions: acquisitions, depreciation, disposals, receipts/shipments, transfers, cost adjustment, counting</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1761' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-820</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe Business Central (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the components and capabilities of Business Central architecture and the core solution/extensions approach</li><li>Describe the update lifecycle for customizations of Business Central</li><li>Differentiate Business Central online vs on-premises features</li><li>Differentiate between the base app and the system app</li><li>Describe the functionality of apps and the process of bringing an app to AppSource</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Install, develop, and deploy for Business Central (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Install and configure the Business Central development environment</li><li>Manage configuration files for an AL extension and manage multiple AL extensions in one workspace</li><li>Debug an extension with Visual Studio Code</li><li>Create, modify, and deploy a Business Central extension in Visual Studio Code</li><li>Manage multilanguage development and maintain extensions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Develop by using AL objects (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Build and extend tables, pages, Role Centers, and enums</li><li>Build and extend reports, including layouts, document reports, data model design, multilanguage support, triggers/functions, and request pages</li><li>Design and create XMLports (properties, nodes, use in AL code)</li><li>Develop codeunits: create/access codeunits, use events/triggers, implement interfaces, create install/upgrade codeunits</li><li>Create and troubleshoot entitlement and permission set objects</li><li>Create queries: link/join data items, apply filters, aggregate data, use queries in reports</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Develop by using AL (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Customize the UI experience and implement onboarding (profiles, views, teaching tips, in-app tours, onboarding checklist)</li><li>Describe essential development standards (data process model, table types, document standards, master data patterns)</li><li>Create custom procedures and use data types in AL code</li><li>Manipulate data and manage files by using code</li><li>Use AL built-in functions, statements, expressions, and variables</li><li>Manage errors and use access modifiers to limit access</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Work with development tools (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Test applications in Business Central using semiautomated test processes</li><li>Install and run the Test Toolkit and develop test codeunits/procedures</li><li>Monitor, analyze, and configure telemetry</li><li>Create custom telemetry signals</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Integrate Business Central with other applications (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Access REST services from within Business Central using HTTP classes</li><li>Get data from and send data to an external REST service; use and read JSON</li><li>Create and work with APIs</li><li>Create and manage OData bound and unbound actions</li><li>Use Read Scale-Out to improve performance</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1762' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-920</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases, product master records, product variants/dimensions, pricing/trade agreements, and intercompany capabilities</li><li>Describe manufacturing strategies (lean, discrete, process) and bills of materials (BOMs), formulas, routes, and operations for production orders</li><li>Describe inventory costing methods, on-hand inventory, inventory journals, quality management, and use cases for Warehouse (WMS) and Transportation (TMS) Management</li><li>Describe the order-to-cash process: sales order creation, fulfillment, inventory reservations, picking and packing</li><li>Describe the procure-to-pay process: purchase requisitions, purchase order creation, and purchase order receipts</li><li>Describe master planning and planning optimization, and landed cost use cases</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Describe Dynamics 365 Finance (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe organization and legal entities, reporting vs. accounting currency, tax capabilities, and cost accounting concepts</li><li>Describe charts of accounts, fiscal calendar, financial dimensions/dimension sets, accounting structure, and financial journals</li><li>Describe core accounts payable components (vendors, purchase orders, vendor invoices) and vendor payments/three-way matching</li><li>Describe core accounts receivable components (customers, customer invoices, free text invoices), credit management, collections, and subscription billing</li><li>Describe cash and bank management, expense management, fixed asset management, and budgeting capabilities</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe the core capabilities of the finance and operations apps (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe enterprise resource planning (ERP) concepts and the finance and operations user interface</li><li>Describe the business value of Commerce, Human Resources, and Project Operations, and finance and operations apps use cases</li><li>Describe built-in reporting capabilities (including workspaces) and options for analyzing data with Power BI</li><li>Describe Microsoft 365 integration (Excel, SharePoint, Teams) and Microsoft Power Platform integration options</li><li>Describe security, workflow, and batch job capabilities</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1764' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-721</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Plan and design collaboration communications systems (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and design Teams meetings, webinars, town halls, and Teams Premium/Copilot usage</li><li>Plan and design Teams Phone and PSTN connectivity, including Operator Connect, Direct Routing, and phone number strategy</li><li>Design call flows for auto attendants and call queues, and design dynamic emergency calling</li><li>Plan and design Teams-certified device solutions (Teams Rooms, BYOD, interoperability)</li><li>Prepare and evaluate the network for Teams, including QoS, network roaming policy, and Call Quality Dashboard configuration</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Configure and manage Teams meetings, webinars, and town halls (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage meeting policies, settings, templates, and controlled-content policies</li><li>Configure meeting recording/transcription to support Copilot and Teams Premium</li><li>Configure and manage Audio Conferencing (bridges, numbers, toll-free)</li><li>Configure webinar roles, policies, and attendee experience</li><li>Configure Town Hall settings, eCDN, and integration with Viva Engage/Stream</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement and configure Teams Phone (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure Teams Phone policies (dial plans, calling, mobility, voicemail, caller ID)</li><li>Create and configure resource accounts, auto attendants, and call queues</li><li>Configure emergency calling locations, routing, and policies</li><li>Assign Teams Phone licenses, phone numbers, and policies to users</li><li>Configure calling features (Cloud Voicemail, call forwarding, delegation, private lines)</li><li>Configure and manage Direct Routing (SBC connectivity, PSTN gateway, voice routes/policies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Configure and manage Teams Rooms and devices (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage and maintain Teams Rooms and devices via Teams admin center and Pro Management portal</li><li>Configure and manage Teams Android devices, including AOSP/MDEP and Intune requirements</li><li>Configure and manage Teams Rooms on Windows, including group policy and peripheral settings</li><li>Configure optional features (content camera, proximity join, Direct Guest Join, hot desking, AI-enabled capabilities)</li><li>Configure BYOD spaces and bookable desks, including room type publishing and inventory management</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1768' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>GH-100</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Manage GitHub Identities and Access (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe differences between managed users and personal accounts</li><li>Configure and enforce SAML SSO and 2FA</li><li>Understand SCIM and team synchronization: implementation and key differences</li><li>Choose and configure identity providers; explain GitHub''s authentication and authorization model</li><li>Configure organization and repository roles; define and manage enterprise teams</li><li>Audit access and permissions; manage settings, policies, rulesets, and roles</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Administer GitHub Enterprise Environment (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Identify issues resolvable by admins vs. GitHub Support; generate support bundles and diagnostics</li><li>Recommend standards for developer processes (workflows, branching, reviews, releases)</li><li>Describe GitHub Enterprise deployment scenarios (GHEC with EMU, GHEC with Data Residency + EMU, GHEC with personal accounts, GHES)</li><li>Explain licensing and billing models</li><li>Monitor license usage and consumption</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement Secure Software Development and Compliance (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Define organization and enterprise security policies and rulesets</li><li>Strengthen enterprise security posture and data protection; implement audit logging and reporting</li><li>Configure vulnerability alerts, secret scanning, and CodeQL</li><li>Manage Dependabot and security advisories; define a security response plan</li><li>Configure personal access tokens and understand rate limits for PATs and GitHub Apps</li><li>Describe GitHub Apps and OAuth Apps; approve or deny app usage based on policy</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage GitHub Actions (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure and manage reuse of actions and workflows at the enterprise/repository level</li><li>Apply organizational policies for GitHub Actions</li><li>Manage runner groups; administer GitHub-hosted vs. self-hosted runner options</li><li>Apply IP allow lists and configure networking (including Azure private networking)</li><li>Monitor and troubleshoot runner performance</li><li>Define scope/access for encrypted secrets; configure secrets at org and repo levels; integrate third-party vaults</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Monitor and Optimize GitHub Usage (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Analyze audit logs and API usage</li><li>Distinguish admin responsibilities vs. GitHub Support and generate diagnostics</li><li>Evaluate enterprise usage patterns to identify adoption, activity, and underutilized features</li><li>Interpret usage reports for metered products</li><li>Recommend strategies for license and resource optimization</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1772' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Tableau</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Connecting to & Preparing Data (25%)</h3><ul><li>Create live connections and extracts; explain live vs. extract tradeoffs</li><li>Create a data source that uses multiple connections; save metadata properties in a .TDS</li><li>Create and manage the data model: add relationships, joins, and unions; explain join vs. relationship</li><li>Rename data fields and assign aliases to data values</li><li>Assign geographic roles to data fields; change data type (number, date, string, Boolean, etc.)</li><li>Change default field properties (number format, aggregation, color, date format, etc.)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Exploring & Analyzing Data (35%)</h3><ul><li>Create basic charts: bar, line, scatterplot, geographic map, combined axis, dual axis, stacked bar, density map, crosstab/highlight table</li><li>Organize data with groups and sets (via marks, headers, and the data pane); build dimension hierarchies</li><li>Add filters to a view, including date filters</li><li>Apply worksheet analytics: manual/computed sorts, reference lines, quick table calculations, bins and histograms</li><li>Create calculated fields (string, date, simple arithmetic) and know when to use a parameter</li><li>Display totals on a worksheet</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Sharing Insights (25%)</h3><ul><li>Format views for presentation: mark colors, fonts, mark shapes, viz animations, mark sizing, legend show/hide</li><li>Create and modify dashboards: add worksheets, configure layout and device-specific dashboards</li><li>Add interactive elements for consumers (show filters, data highlighter, tooltips) and dashboard actions (filter, highlight, parameter control, URL action)</li><li>Create a story and story points</li><li>Share a workbook (e.g., .twbx as PDF or image, publish to Tableau Server)</li><li>View/export underlying data and export to Microsoft PowerPoint</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Understanding Tableau Concepts (15%)</h3><ul><li>Explain what kind of information dimensions vs. measures usually contain, and the difference between them</li><li>Explain how discrete vs. continuous fields are displayed</li><li>Explain the difference between discrete date parts and continuous date values</li><li>Explain the default aggregation for measures</li><li>Describe how an aggregated measure changes when dimensions are added to a view</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C181' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITS-201</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Database Design</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, design tables for storing data (identify entities, rows/records, columns/fields)</li><li>Given a scenario, identify the appropriate primary key (primary key, composite/compound key)</li><li>Given a scenario, choose data types to meet requirements (text, numbers, dates/times, Boolean)</li><li>Given a scenario, design relationships between tables (primary/foreign keys, ERDs, referential integrity)</li><li>Normalize a database to third normal form (3NF)</li><li>Given a scenario, identify data protection measures (backups/restore, least privilege, GRANT/REVOKE, roles, encryption, hashing, masking, auditing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Database Object Management using DDL</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze queries that create, alter, and drop tables (ANSI SQL syntax; NULL/NOT NULL)</li><li>Construct and analyze queries that create, alter, and drop views; purpose of views</li><li>Construct and analyze stored procedures and functions (input/output parameters, return values)</li><li>Given a scenario, choose between clustered and non-clustered indexes</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Data Retrieval</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze queries that select data using INNER/LEFT/RIGHT/CROSS/FULL OUTER JOIN and self joins</li><li>Combine result sets using UNION and INTERSECT; DISTINCT; column alias; computed columns; concatenation (+ operator, CONCAT()); NULLIF()</li><li>Construct and analyze queries that sort and filter data (ORDER BY, WHERE, LIKE, BETWEEN, AND/OR/NOT, TOP/LIMIT, IN, ANY, ALL, NULL handling, comparison operators)</li><li>Construct and analyze queries that aggregate data (GROUP BY, HAVING, MIN, MAX, COUNT, AVG, SUM)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Data Manipulation using DML</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze INSERT statements (INSERT INTO SELECT, INSERT INTO VALUES)</li><li>Construct and analyze UPDATE statements (update data in a single table)</li><li>Construct and analyze DELETE statements (delete data from a single table)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Troubleshooting</h3><ul><li>Troubleshoot data object management query failures (syntax and runtime errors)</li><li>Troubleshoot data retrieval query failures (syntax and runtime errors)</li><li>Troubleshoot data manipulation query failures (syntax and runtime errors)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1810' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITS-305</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Core Programming Concepts</h3><ul><li>Describe computer storage and data types (memory stacks/heaps, numeric vs textual data, garbage collection)</li><li>Construct and analyze algorithms and flowcharts (decision structures, if/else, switch, for/while/do-while loops, recursion)</li><li>Incorporate error handling into applications or modules (try-catch-finally, unit testing, exceptions, defensive coding, debugging)</li><li>Construct and analyze code based on functional programming patterns (events, delegates, promises, sync vs async, immutability)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Software Development Principles</h3><ul><li>Describe software development lifecycle (SDLC) management (requirements, design, implementation, testing, deployment, maintenance, Agile/SCRUM)</li><li>Interpret application specifications (translating specs into prototypes/code, selecting appropriate app type/components)</li><li>Construct and analyze code using algorithms and data structures (arrays, stacks, queues, linked lists, dictionaries, sorting/searching algorithms)</li><li>Describe the purpose of version control systems (GitHub, check-in/out, merge, branch, rollback, code review)</li><li>Describe secure coding concepts (encryption, hashing, digital signatures, CSRF mitigation, SQL injection, iframe risks)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Object-Oriented Programming</h3><ul><li>Construct, analyze, and use classes (properties, methods, events, fields, constructors, access modifiers, encapsulation, composition)</li><li>Construct and analyze code that uses inheritance (base/derived classes, generic classes, abstract classes)</li><li>Construct and analyze code that uses polymorphism (method overriding, interfaces, overloading)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Web Applications</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze web applications (HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript ES6, HTTP request/response, state management, cookies/local/session storage)</li><li>Describe and configure web hosting (virtual directories, publishing web apps, role of the web server)</li><li>Describe and configure web services (JSON, REST API, OAuth, XML, consuming services from client applications)</li><li>Describe and identify architectural patterns (MVC, MVVM, single page application/SPA)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Databases</h3><ul><li>Design and normalize a database (ERDs, normalization to 3NF, indexes, constraints, primary/foreign keys, relationships)</li><li>Construct, analyze, and optimize ANSI SQL queries (stored procedures, DML vs DDL, functions, triggers, cursors, joins)</li><li>Manage transactions (commit, rollback, concurrency, isolation levels, locking)</li><li>Describe database access methods (Entity Framework Code-first/Database-first, connection pools, LINQ)</li><li>Describe types of NoSQL databases (document databases, key-value databases)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1811' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITS-302</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 JavaScript Operators, Methods, and Keywords</h3><ul><li>Complete and debug code using assignment and arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /, %, +=, -=, *=, /=, %=)</li><li>Apply JavaScript best practices: comments, indentation, naming conventions, noscript, constants, reserved keywords, debugger keyword, breakpoints, console.log</li><li>Evaluate the use of internal vs. external scripts and behavior when used at multiple levels</li><li>Implement exception handling with try, catch, finally</li><li>Complete and debug code that interacts with the Browser Object Model (BOM): displaying dialogs, determining screen size</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Variables, Data Types, and Functions</h3><ul><li>Declare and use variables of primitive data types (Number, Boolean, String, null, undefined), typeof, type conversion (parseInt, parseFloat), string/number formatting methods</li><li>Declare and use single- and multi-dimensional arrays: iteration, sorting/searching, push/pop/shift/unshift, length property</li><li>Complete and debug code that uses objects: properties, methods, instantiation, Date object and date manipulation</li><li>Complete and debug code using built-in Math functions: random, round, abs, floor, ceil, min, max, pow, sqrt</li><li>Complete and debug functions that accept parameters and return values: scope (local vs global), passing by value vs. reference, return values</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Decisions and Loops</h3><ul><li>Evaluate expressions using logical and comparison operators (!=, ==, <, >, <=, >=, !, &&, ||)</li><li>Complete and debug decision statements: if, if-else, switch, nested if</li><li>Complete and debug loops: for, for-in, while, do-while, break, continue</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Document Object Model</h3><ul><li>Identify and construct the DOM tree: window, document, body, other HTML elements</li><li>Identify and handle document, form, keyboard, and mouse events (onload, onfocus, onblur, onchange, onkeydown/up/press, onclick, onmouseover/out)</li><li>Complete and debug code that outputs to an HTML document: document.write, innerHTML, textContent</li><li>Complete and debug code that locates, modifies, and adds HTML elements/attributes: getElementById, getElementsByTagName, getElementsByClassName, setAttribute, createElement</li><li>Create events using event handlers and listeners: DOM events, HTML attribute events, addEventListener</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 HTML Forms</h3><ul><li>Complete and debug code that retrieves form input and sets form field values, including prepopulating, masking, and updating values</li><li>Complete and debug code that performs input validation: case, string comparisons, NaN, not-blank checks</li><li>Describe the form submission process: onsubmit, POST vs. GET, submission targets</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1813' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-104</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Cloud Concepts</h3><ul><li>Explain cloud advantages to stakeholders (infrastructure, IaaS/PaaS/SaaS, faster/cheaper app building)</li><li>Explain cost to stakeholders (compute/data/network costs, support plans for PASR, ROI)</li><li>Explain performance, reliability (SLA, disaster recovery/backup), and availability to stakeholders</li><li>Explain scalability to stakeholders (auto-scaling rules based on demand)</li><li>Recommend off-the-shelf (e.g. Office 365, Adobe Express) vs custom cloud solutions (Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, IBM Cloud)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Developing Cloud Architecture</h3><ul><li>Choose between public, private, and hybrid cloud implementations</li><li>Draw an architectural diagram showing compute/data/network components, logical groupings, and data flows</li><li>Define requirements: virtualization decisions, serverless benefits, networking/storage/memory needs</li><li>Identify how services communicate via APIs</li><li>Create virtual machines (OS, sizing, geographic/latency/legal factors, scaling and backup configuration)</li><li>Identify data storage requirements (structured vs unstructured, capacity, location, security)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implementing the Cloud Development Life Cycle</h3><ul><li>Create content in virtual environments using source-code management systems (e.g. GitHub)</li><li>Perform testing: test cases, scenarios, scripts, and iterative bug reporting</li><li>Structure the overall cloud-based solution: integrate with legacy/third-party systems, choose containers (Docker) vs VMs (Hyper-V) vs microservices</li><li>Deploy applications: deployment strategy, version control, CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Actions)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Deploying the Application (Managing Cloud Operations)</h3><ul><li>Manage operational costs via usage-based pricing and scale up/down cost-effectively</li><li>Develop business continuity and disaster recovery policy (risk scenarios, on-prem vs offsite backup)</li><li>Provide support to users (security policies, application/hardware support, training tools)</li><li>Monitor cloud systems: log events, monitor hardware/software dashboards, configure alerts/notifications</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Understanding Cloud Governance</h3><ul><li>Comply with privacy and regulatory requirements (HIPAA, PDPA, FERPA, COPPA, GDPR, CCPA, NIST/ISO frameworks)</li><li>Comply with ethical guidelines (bias, transparency, accountability in prebuilt services)</li><li>Manage cloud security: identity verification/MFA, access policies (least privilege, custom vs vendor roles), data encryption, intrusion detection/firewalls</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1814' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-306</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Application Lifecycle Management</h3><ul><li>Describe the application lifecycle management stages: plan, design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain</li><li>Debug and test web apps: input validation errors, runtime errors, breakpoints</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Graphics and Animation</h3><ul><li>Use the canvas element to create graphics and animations (shape, color, line, translate/move, rotate, scale, interactivity)</li><li>Use the svg element to create and display graphics (inline vs. referenced XML, shapes, color, SVG filter effects)</li><li>Transform, style, and enhance text and graphics (rounded corners, shadows, transparency, gradients, typography, Web Open Font Format, 2-D/3-D transforms, keyframes)</li><li>Apply CSS filters to images: grayscale, blur, sepia, opacity, drop-shadow, saturate</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Forms</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze markup that uses form elements: datalist, fieldset, meter, legend, output</li><li>Configure input validation: validation attributes, pattern attribute for regex, correct data type, length, required value</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Layouts</h3><ul><li>Manage content layout, positioning, and flow with CSS (inline vs. block flow, float vs. absolute positioning, overflow, basic styling)</li><li>Construct layouts using responsive design: grid view, background-size, images, picture, viewport, responsive width, media queries</li><li>Construct flexible responsive layouts using CSS flexbox (flex container/items properties)</li><li>Construct grid-based layouts using CSS grid: container, items, templates, gap</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 JavaScript Coding</h3><ul><li>Create and use custom classes: instantiation, properties, methods, inheritance</li><li>Perform data access using JavaScript: send/receive data, transmit/parse complex objects, load/save files, XML, JSON</li><li>Construct code that responds to events via event listeners/handlers (gesture events, multiple events, Event object, bubbling vs. cascading)</li><li>Construct code that uses JavaScript APIs: Google Charts, jQuery, Geolocation</li><li>Manage the state of an application: session state vs. app state, local vs. session storage</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1815' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITS-301</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 HTML Fundamentals</h3><ul><li>Construct markup that uses metadata elements: script, noscript, style, link, meta tags (encoding, keywords, viewport, description)</li><li>Construct well-formed page markup: DOCTYPE declaration, html, head, body, proper syntax, closing tags, commonly used symbols</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 CSS Fundamentals</h3><ul><li>Analyze and implement inline styles, internal (embedded) style sheets, and external style sheets, including when to use each</li><li>Understand precedence when combining inline styles and style sheets, and browser default style</li><li>Construct and analyze CSS rule sets with valid syntax</li><li>Use selectors: class, id, elements, pseudo-class, and descendant</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Document Structure using HTML</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze markup to structure content and organize data (table, tr, th, td, h1-h6, p, br, hr, div, span, ul, ol, li)</li><li>Construct and analyze markup using HTML5 semantic elements (header, nav, section, article, aside, footer, details, summary, figure, caption)</li><li>Construct and analyze markup that implements navigation (target, anchor/a href, bookmark, relative vs absolute links, folder hierarchies, map, area)</li><li>Construct and analyze markup that uses form elements (form attributes, action, method, submission methods, input types, select, textarea, button, option, label)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Multimedia Presentation using HTML</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze markup that displays images: img and picture elements and their attributes</li><li>Construct and analyze markup that plays video and audio: video, audio, track, source, iframe</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Webpage Styling using CSS</h3><ul><li>Construct and analyze styles that position content: positioning (float, relative, absolute, static, fixed), max-width, overflow, height, width, align, display, inline vs block, visibility, box model, margins and padding</li><li>Construct and analyze styles that format text: font-family, color, font-style, font-size, font-weight, font-variant, link colors, text alignment/decoration, indentation, line-height, word-wrap, letter-spacing</li><li>Construct and analyze styles that format backgrounds and borders: border-color/style/width, background properties, colors</li><li>Construct and analyze styles that create a simple responsive layout: units of measurement (%, px, em, vw, vh), viewport and media query, frameworks/templates, breakpoints, grids</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Accessibility, Readability, and Testing</h3><ul><li>Construct well-formed HTML and CSS markup conforming to industry best practices: reusing rules/rule sets, commenting, web-safe fonts, cross-platform usability, separation of structure and style</li><li>Apply accessibility principles and evaluate content accessibility: text alternatives, color contrast, legibility of typography, tab order, text resizing, text hierarchy, translate</li><li>Evaluate the structural integrity of HTML and CSS markup: syntax errors, tag mismatch, cascading issues</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1816' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-308</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Foundational Concepts</h3><ul><li>Distinguish structured vs. unstructured data and data types</li><li>Apply logical reasoning and Boolean operators; recognize logical ambiguities/fallacies</li><li>Explain the core concepts of computational thinking: decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, algorithms</li><li>Describe the purpose of automation in solving problems</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Identify and Collect Data</h3><ul><li>Assess what data is needed to solve a given problem</li><li>Evaluate data quality, validity, and reliability</li><li>Select appropriate tools/methods to collect data</li><li>Clean and prepare data for analysis</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Apply Abstraction</h3><ul><li>Identify patterns and trends within data</li><li>Organize and sort/filter data to reveal relationships</li><li>Represent data and processes through abstraction</li><li>Build abstract/conceptual models to simplify a problem</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Specify a Solution</h3><ul><li>Decompose a problem statement into component parts</li><li>Identify requirements and constraints of a solution</li><li>Select and justify an appropriate design/problem-solving process</li><li>Sequence the steps needed to reach a solution</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Automate a Solution</h3><ul><li>Construct and evaluate algorithmic sequences of steps, including reusable functions</li><li>Apply iteration (loops) within an algorithm</li><li>Implement selection/conditional (if-then) logic</li><li>Use variables to store and manipulate data in an algorithm</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Present and Improve a Solution</h3><ul><li>Choose an effective medium to create a computational artifact</li><li>Communicate and present a solution to stakeholders</li><li>Incorporate collaboration and feedback into a design</li><li>Prototype, test, and iteratively improve an automated solution</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1817' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-103</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Windows Installation and Configuration</h3><ul><li>Install Windows using default settings (time zone, Microsoft vs. local account, upgrade vs. custom install)</li><li>Configure user account options (cloud/local, local user vs. administrative account types)</li><li>Configure desktop settings (Start menu, display, taskbar, power, window management)</li><li>Manage accessibility settings (Magnifier, Narrator, Sticky Keys, high contrast, speech recognition, on-screen keyboard)</li><li>Manage updates (Windows Update settings, driver updates, update history)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Application and Peripheral Management</h3><ul><li>Manage applications and Windows features (install/modify/remove apps, optional Windows features, Microsoft Store)</li><li>Compare and contrast peripheral connection types (HDMI, DisplayPort, VGA, mini-HDMI, USB, USB-C, adapters/converters)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Data Access and Management</h3><ul><li>Describe cloud services (cloud storage/collaboration, common providers, file sharing permissions, VMs, offline sync)</li><li>Describe and configure file sharing and permissions (NTFS/share permissions, effective permissions, mapped drives, ownership)</li><li>Manage backup and restore (backup types, full backup/restore, restore previous versions)</li><li>Describe data access and retention policies (MOUs, Acceptable Use Policies, data ownership, remote wipe)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Device Security</h3><ul><li>Describe network firewall settings (Windows Defender Firewall, private/public/guest networks)</li><li>Describe user authentication (MFA, smart cards, biometrics, secure password requirements for BYOD/corporate devices)</li><li>Given an attack type, describe mitigation methods (viruses, ransomware, phishing, keyloggers, social engineering, antivirus/antimalware config)</li><li>Manage User Account Control (UAC) settings</li><li>Manage mobile device security (MDM, securing/enrolling devices, transport limitations)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Troubleshooting</h3><ul><li>Perform troubleshooting tasks (Windows tools, gpupdate/gpresult, local vs. group policy precedence)</li><li>Troubleshoot operating system and application issues (reset/roll back OS, safe mode, Store app issues, app repair/reinstall)</li><li>Troubleshoot device issues (hardware connections/ports/power, driver update/roll back, Device Manager)</li><li>Troubleshoot device connections to networks and domains (wired/wireless, APIPA, domain joining)</li><li>Troubleshoot peripheral device connections (keyboard, mouse, display, storage, printers, scanners, drivers, cables)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1818' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-202</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Data Basics</h3><ul><li>Define the concept of data science</li><li>Describe basic data variable types (Boolean, numeric, string, date/time)</li><li>Describe basic structures used in data analytics (tables, rows, columns, lists, tuples)</li><li>Gather and categorize data (qualitative, quantitative, structured, unstructured, metadata, big data)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Data Manipulation</h3><ul><li>Import, store, and export data &mdash; ETL processes, data manipulation languages (SQL, R, Python, Excel/Power Query), common storage file formats (delimited, XML, JSON)</li><li>Clean data using SQL, R, Python, and Excel (handle NULLs, special characters, trimming, inconsistent formatting, duplicates, imputing, validation)</li><li>Organize data using SQL, R, Python, and Excel (sorting, filtering, slicing, transposing, appending, truncating)</li><li>Aggregate data using SQL, R, Python, and Excel (grouping, joining/merging, summarizing, pivoting)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Data Analysis</h3><ul><li>Differentiate types of data analysis (descriptive, diagnostic, hypothesis testing, predictive, prescriptive, principal component, cluster, association)</li><li>Differentiate data aggregation and interpretation metrics (Sum, Max, Min, Count, Avg/Mean, Mode, Median, Std Dev)</li><li>Differentiate exploratory data analysis methods (data relationships, data drilling/granularity, data mining &mdash; anomalies, correlation, patterns, outliers)</li><li>Evaluate and explain results of data analyses (trends, expected values, predictive-model results, p-values, t-tests, regression)</li><li>Define and describe the role of AI and machine learning in data analysis</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Data Visualization and Communication</h3><ul><li>Report data &mdash; effectively display information in tables and charts; explain when/why to disaggregate data</li><li>Create visualizations from data &mdash; practices that minimize misinterpretation; select visualization types matching the underlying data/question (comparison, time/trend, part-to-whole, relationship, distribution, correlation, box-and-whisker, scatter, bar, Sankey, histogram, pie, column, etc.)</li><li>Derive conclusions from a data visualization &mdash; translate a visual into words; identify gaps between an analysis claim and its graphical representation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Responsible Analytics Practices</h3><ul><li>Describe data privacy laws and best practices (GDPR, FERPA, HIPAA, IRB, PCI)</li><li>Describe best practices for responsible data handling (PII handling, securing data, anonymity in small data sets, interpretability-vs-accuracy trade-offs, limits of population-level generalization)</li><li>Given a scenario, describe types of bias affecting collection/interpretation of data (confirmation bias, human cognitive bias, motivational bias, sampling bias) and select visualizations/representations to avoid bias</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C1819' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITS-102</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Defense in Depth</h3><ul><li>Identify core security principles (confidentiality, integrity, availability, non-repudiation, threat, risk, vulnerability, principle of least privilege, attack surfaces including IoT)</li><li>Define and enforce physical security (site security, computer security, removable devices/drives, mantraps)</li><li>Identify security policy types (administrative controls, technical controls)</li><li>Identify attack types (buffer overflow, viruses, worms, Trojans, spyware, ransomware, rootkits, DoS, XSS, SQL injection, brute force, MITM/MITB, social engineering, keyloggers, logic bombs)</li><li>Identify backup and restore types (full, incremental, differential)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Operating System Security</h3><ul><li>Identify client and server protection (hardening, patch management, group policy, UAC, secure dynamic DNS updates)</li><li>Configure user authentication (multifactor authentication, password policies, remote access, Run As/sudo, domain/local user & group creation, Kerberos)</li><li>Manage permissions in Windows and Linux (file/folder/share permissions, inheritance, take ownership, delegation)</li><li>Facilitate non-repudiation using audit policies and log files</li><li>Demonstrate knowledge of encryption (file/folder/drive encryption, TPM, VPN encryption methods, public/private key, certificates, BitLocker)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Network Device Security</h3><ul><li>Implement wireless security (encryption strength, SSIDs, MAC filtering, default configuration/OOBE)</li><li>Identify the role of network protection devices (firewalls, IDS/IPS, SIEM, content filtering, blacklisting/whitelisting)</li><li>Identify network isolation methods (routing, honeynet, DMZ, NAT/PAT, VPN, IPsec, air gap, DirectAccess, VLAN)</li><li>Identify protocol security concepts (tunneling, DNSSEC, network sniffing, well-known ports: FTP, HTTP, HTTPS, DNS, RDP, Telnet, SSH, LDAP/LDAPS, SNMP, SMTP, IMAP, SFTP)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Secure Computing</h3><ul><li>Implement email protection (antispam, spoofing, phishing, pharming, client protection, user training)</li><li>Manage browser security (browser settings, cache management, private browsing)</li><li>Install and configure anti-malware and antivirus software (install/uninstall/update, remediation, scheduling scans, investigating alerts)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C184' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AIF-C01</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Fundamentals of AI and ML (20%)</h3><ul><li>Explain basic AI/ML terminology (AI, ML, deep learning, neural networks, NLP, LLM, GenAI, agentic AI) and differentiate AI, ML, GenAI, deep learning, and agentic AI</li><li>Describe types of AI/ML learning (supervised, unsupervised, reinforcement) and types of data/inferencing (batch, real-time, labeled/unlabeled, etc.)</li><li>Identify practical AI/ML use cases, select appropriate techniques (regression, classification, clustering), and recognize when AI/ML is NOT appropriate</li><li>Explain capabilities of AWS managed AI/ML services (Amazon SageMaker AI, Transcribe, Translate, Comprehend, Lex, Polly)</li><li>Describe the AI/ML development lifecycle/pipeline and MLOps fundamentals (experimentation, monitoring, retraining, production readiness)</li><li>Describe model performance metrics (accuracy, precision, recall, F1 score) and business metrics (cost per user, ROI) to evaluate ML models</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Fundamentals of GenAI (24%)</h3><ul><li>Define foundational GenAI concepts (tokens, chunking, embeddings, vectors, prompt engineering, transformer-based LLMs, foundation models, diffusion models)</li><li>Identify GenAI use cases (image/video/audio generation, summarization, AI assistants, code generation, customer service agents)</li><li>Describe the foundation model (FM) lifecycle: data selection, model selection, pre-training, fine-tuning, evaluation, deployment, feedback</li><li>Understand capabilities and limitations of GenAI for business problems (hallucinations, interpretability, nondeterminism) and model selection factors</li><li>Describe AWS infrastructure/services for building GenAI applications (Amazon Bedrock, SageMaker AI/JumpStart, Strands Agents, Bedrock AgentCore)</li><li>Describe the token-based pricing model and cost tradeoffs of AWS GenAI services</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Applications of Foundation Models (28%)</h3><ul><li>Identify FM selection criteria (cost, modality, latency, model size, customization) and the effect of inference parameters (e.g. temperature)</li><li>Define Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) and identify AWS vector database services (Amazon OpenSearch Service, Aurora, Neptune, RDS for PostgreSQL)</li><li>Choose effective prompt engineering techniques (chain-of-thought, zero-shot, few-shot, prompt templates) and recognize risks (prompt injection, jailbreaking, hijacking)</li><li>Describe FM training and fine-tuning methods (instruction tuning, transfer learning, continuous pre-training, RLHF) and data preparation practices</li><li>Describe methods/metrics to evaluate FM performance (ROUGE, BLEU, BERTScore, LLM-as-a-judge, benchmark datasets, human-in-the-loop)</li><li>Identify approaches to evaluate FM-based applications (RAG, agents, workflows) against business objective alignment metrics</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Guidelines for Responsible AI (14%)</h3><ul><li>Identify features of responsible AI: bias, fairness, inclusivity, robustness, safety, veracity</li><li>Explain tools to identify/monitor bias, trustworthiness, and truthfulness (Amazon SageMaker Clarify, SageMaker Model Monitor, Amazon A2I, Bedrock Guardrails)</li><li>Identify legal and ethical risks of working with GenAI (IP infringement claims, biased model outputs, hallucinations, loss of customer trust)</li><li>Recognize the importance of transparent and explainable models and related tools (SageMaker Model Cards, Bedrock Model Evaluations)</li><li>Describe tradeoffs between model safety and transparency, and principles of human-centered design for explainable AI</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Domain 5: Security, Compliance, and Governance for AI Solutions (14%)</h3><ul><li>Identify AWS services/features to secure AI systems (IAM roles/policies, encryption, Amazon Macie, AWS PrivateLink, Bedrock Guardrails, Bedrock AgentCore Identity)</li><li>Describe security and privacy considerations for AI systems (prompt injection, data leakage prevention, output filtering/validation, audit trail and logging)</li><li>Describe hallucination detection methods and grounding techniques (RAG grounding, output validation, confidence scoring)</li><li>Identify AWS services for governance and regulation compliance (AWS Config, Amazon Inspector, AWS Audit Manager, AWS Artifact, AWS CloudTrail, Trusted Advisor)</li><li>Describe data governance strategies (data lifecycles, residency, retention, monitoring) and governance frameworks (e.g. Generative AI Security Scoping Matrix)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C19' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-102</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Deploy and manage a Microsoft 365 tenant (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create a tenant; implement and manage domains; configure org settings (Security & privacy, Organization profile)</li><li>Monitor Microsoft 365 service health and Network connectivity insights; configure/monitor software updates via the admin center; monitor adoption/usage; configure Microsoft 365 Backup</li><li>Create and manage users in Microsoft Entra ID (incl. external users) and contacts in the admin center</li><li>Create and manage groups (incl. Microsoft 365 Groups) and shared mailboxes; manage/monitor licenses incl. group-based licensing; bulk user management via Graph/Entra PowerShell</li><li>Implement and manage roles in Microsoft 365 and Microsoft Entra ID; manage permissions for Defender XDR/Purview via roles or role groups</li><li>Manage delegation via administrative units and Microsoft Entra ID roles in Privileged Identity Management (PIM)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement and manage Microsoft Entra identity and access (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Prepare for and implement identity synchronization (IdFix, Microsoft Entra Connect Sync / Cloud Sync); monitor via Connect Health; troubleshoot sync issues</li><li>Implement and manage authentication methods, self-service password reset (SSPR), and Microsoft Entra Password Protection; investigate/resolve authentication issues</li><li>Plan for identity protection and implement/manage Microsoft Entra Identity Protection</li><li>Plan and implement/manage Conditional Access policies, including multifactor authentication (MFA) via Conditional Access</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Manage security and threats by using Microsoft Defender XDR (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Review/respond to threats via Microsoft Security Exposure Management (incl. Secure Score); respond to Defender XDR incidents/alerts including advanced hunting; act on Defender XDR reports and Defender Threat Intelligence findings</li><li>Implement threat policies/rules and alert policies in Microsoft Defender for Office 365; investigate/respond to email and collaboration threats; manage attack simulation training campaigns and restricted entities (blocked users)</li><li>Onboard devices to Microsoft Defender for Endpoint; configure endpoint settings; review/respond to vulnerabilities in the Vulnerability Management dashboard</li><li>Configure the Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps app connector, policies/alerts, activity log interpretation, and Cloud App Discovery; respond to Cloud App Discovery findings</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage compliance by using Microsoft Purview (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement sensitive information types (keywords, keyword lists, regular expressions)</li><li>Implement retention labels, retention label policies, and retention policies</li><li>Implement sensitivity labels and sensitivity label policies; monitor label usage via Content explorer, Activity explorer, and label reports</li><li>Configure DLP policies across Microsoft 365 workloads (Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, OneDrive, Teams, Power BI, Microsoft 365 Copilot) and Endpoint DLP</li><li>Review and respond to DLP alerts, events, and reports</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C251' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MLA-C01</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Data Preparation for Machine Learning (ML) (28%)</h3><ul><li>Ingest and store data from AWS sources (S3, EFS, FSx, Kinesis, Kafka, Flink) in formats like Parquet, JSON, CSV, ORC, Avro, RecordIO</li><li>Merge data from multiple sources using AWS Glue, Apache Spark, or SageMaker Data Wrangler</li><li>Transform data and perform feature engineering (scaling, binning, log transform, encoding, tokenization)</li><li>Validate and label data using SageMaker Ground Truth or Amazon Mechanical Turk</li><li>Identify and mitigate bias (class imbalance, difference in proportions of labels) using SageMaker Clarify</li><li>Ensure data integrity, encryption, classification, and compliance (PII/PHI, data residency) before modeling</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 ML Model Development (26%)</h3><ul><li>Choose a modeling approach: compare ML algorithms, SageMaker built-in algorithms, AI services (Rekognition, Transcribe, Bedrock), and foundation models via SageMaker JumpStart</li><li>Train models using SageMaker built-in algorithms, script mode with TensorFlow/PyTorch, and fine-tune pre-trained models</li><li>Tune hyperparameters (random search, Bayesian optimization) via SageMaker Automatic Model Tuning</li><li>Prevent overfitting/underfitting/catastrophic forgetting via regularization, ensembling, stacking, boosting</li><li>Manage model versions and repeatability using SageMaker Model Registry</li><li>Evaluate model performance using metrics (F1, precision, recall, RMSE, ROC/AUC, confusion matrix) and SageMaker Clarify/Model Debugger</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Deployment and Orchestration of ML Workflows (22%)</h3><ul><li>Select deployment infrastructure and endpoint types (real-time, serverless, asynchronous, batch) based on cost/latency/performance tradeoffs</li><li>Choose deployment targets (SageMaker endpoints, ECS, EKS, Lambda) and containers (built-in vs. BYOC)</li><li>Provision and script infrastructure as code (CloudFormation, AWS CDK) and configure SageMaker endpoint auto scaling</li><li>Optimize edge deployments using SageMaker Neo</li><li>Set up CI/CD pipelines with CodePipeline, CodeBuild, and CodeDeploy for ML workflow automation</li><li>Apply deployment/rollback strategies (blue/green, canary, linear) and build automated retraining and testing mechanisms</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 ML Solution Monitoring, Maintenance, and Security (24%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor model inference in production for drift, data quality, and anomalies using SageMaker Model Monitor and Clarify</li><li>Conduct A/B testing and compare shadow vs. production variant performance</li><li>Monitor and optimize infrastructure and cost using CloudWatch, X-Ray, CloudTrail, Cost Explorer, and Trusted Advisor</li><li>Rightsize instances and select purchasing options (Spot, On-Demand, Reserved, SageMaker Savings Plans)</li><li>Secure ML resources via IAM least-privilege policies, roles, and SageMaker Role Manager</li><li>Build VPCs, subnets, and security groups to isolate ML systems and secure CI/CD pipelines</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C279' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ITIL</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Understand the key concepts of service management (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recall definitions: service, utility, warranty, customer, user, service management, sponsor</li><li>Describe key concepts of creating value with services: cost, value, organization, outcome, output, risk, utility, warranty</li><li>Describe key concepts of service relationships: service offering, service relationship management, service provision, service consumption</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Understand how the ITIL guiding principles can help an organization adopt and adapt service management (15%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the nature, use and interaction of the guiding principles</li><li>Focus on value</li><li>Start where you are; Progress iteratively with feedback</li><li>Collaborate and promote visibility; Think and work holistically</li><li>Keep it simple and practical; Optimize and automate</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Understand the four dimensions of service management (5%)</h3><ul><li>Organizations and people</li><li>Information and technology</li><li>Partners and suppliers</li><li>Value streams and processes</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Understand the purpose and components of the ITIL service value system (2.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the ITIL service value system (SVS) as a whole &mdash; how its components (guiding principles, governance, service value chain, practices, continual improvement) work together to enable value co-creation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Understand the activities of the service value chain, and how they interconnect (5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the interconnected nature of the service value chain and how it supports value streams</li><li>Describe the purpose of each value chain activity: Plan, Improve, Engage, Design & transition, Obtain/build, Deliver & support</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Know the purpose and key terms of 15 ITIL practices (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Recall the purpose of 15 named practices, e.g. information security management, relationship management, supplier management, IT asset management, monitoring and event management, release management, service configuration management, deployment management (plus the 7 practices covered in more depth elsewhere: continual improvement, change enablement, incident management, problem management, service request management, service desk, service level management)</li><li>Recall definitions of key ITIL terms: IT asset, event, configuration item, change, incident, problem, known error</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Understand 7 ITIL practices in detail (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Continual improvement (including the continual improvement model)</li><li>Change enablement</li><li>Incident management</li><li>Problem management</li><li>Service request management</li><li>Service desk</li><li>Service level management</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C348' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SCS-C03</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Detection (16%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement monitoring and alerting solutions for an AWS account or organization</li><li>Aggregate security and monitoring events and create metrics/alerts/dashboards (GuardDuty, Security Hub, Macie, Security Lake)</li><li>Identify sources for log ingestion and storage based on requirements</li><li>Configure logging for AWS services and applications (CloudTrail, CloudWatch Logs)</li><li>Implement log storage/data lakes and integrate with third-party security tools; analyze/normalize/correlate logs</li><li>Troubleshoot security monitoring, logging, and alerting solutions (misconfigurations, missing logs)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Incident Response (14%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement response plans and runbooks for security incidents</li><li>Use AWS service features to be prepared for incidents (Shield Advanced, blast-radius minimization)</li><li>Test and validate incident response plan effectiveness (Fault Injection Service, Resilience Hub)</li><li>Use AWS services to automatically remediate incidents (Systems Manager, Step Functions, Lambda)</li><li>Capture forensic artifacts and search/correlate logs across applications and services</li><li>Validate findings, contain/eradicate/recover affected resources, and conduct root cause analysis (Detective)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Infrastructure Security (18%)</h3><ul><li>Design and implement security controls for network edge services (CloudFront, WAF, Shield Advanced, CORS)</li><li>Design edge controls/rules (geo restrictions, rate limiting, client fingerprinting) and integrate third-party WAF/OCSF data</li><li>Design and implement hardened EC2 AMIs/container images and apply instance/service/execution roles</li><li>Scan compute resources for vulnerabilities and deploy patches (Inspector, Patch Manager); secure admin access (Session Manager)</li><li>Implement protections/guardrails for generative AI applications (GenAI OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications)</li><li>Design/troubleshoot network security controls, hybrid/multi-cloud connectivity, segmentation, and identify unnecessary access</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Identity and Access Management (20%)</h3><ul><li>Design identity solutions for human, application, and system authentication (IAM Identity Center, Cognito, MFA, IdP integration)</li><li>Configure mechanisms to issue temporary credentials (STS, S3 presigned URLs) and troubleshoot authentication issues</li><li>Design and evaluate authorization controls for cross-account/human/application access (resource policies, role trust policies)</li><li>Design ABAC and RBAC strategies</li><li>Design, interpret, and implement least-privilege IAM policies (permission boundaries, session policies)</li><li>Analyze authorization failures and investigate/correct unintended permissions (IAM Access Analyzer, Policy Simulator)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Data Protection (18%)</h3><ul><li>Design and configure encryption-in-transit requirements (ELB security policies, TLS enforcement)</li><li>Design secure/private access mechanisms (PrivateLink, VPC endpoints, Client VPN, Verified Access) and inter-resource encryption</li><li>Design and configure data-at-rest encryption (KMS, CloudHSM, client-side vs server-side)</li><li>Design data integrity, lifecycle management, retention, replication, and backup solutions (S3 Object Lock, AWS Backup)</li><li>Design management/rotation of credentials and secrets (Secrets Manager) and manage imported/external key material</li><li>Mask sensitive data and create/manage encryption keys and certificates across Regions (KMS, Private CA)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Security Foundations and Governance (14%)</h3><ul><li>Develop a strategy to centrally deploy and manage AWS accounts (AWS Organizations, Control Tower)</li><li>Implement organization policies to manage permissions (SCPs, RCPs, declarative policies) and manage root user credentials</li><li>Implement a secure/consistent deployment strategy using infrastructure as code (CloudFormation StackSets, Guard, cfn-lint)</li><li>Use tagging for resource organization and securely share resources across accounts (RAM, Service Catalog)</li><li>Create/enable rules to detect and remediate noncompliant resources (AWS Config, Security Hub)</li><li>Use AWS audit services (Audit Manager, Artifact) and evaluate architecture against AWS security best practices (Well-Architected)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C371' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DP-600</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Maintain a data analytics solution (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement workspace-level, item-level, and row/column/object/file-level access controls</li><li>Apply sensitivity labels to items and endorse items</li><li>Configure version control (Git integration) for a workspace</li><li>Create and manage Power BI Desktop projects (.pbip) and configure deployment pipelines</li><li>Perform impact analysis of downstream dependencies across lakehouses, warehouses, dataflows, and semantic models</li><li>Deploy/manage semantic models via the XMLA endpoint and build reusable assets (.pbit, .pbids, shared semantic models)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Prepare data (47.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create data connections; discover data via OneLake catalog and Real-Time hub; choose between data stores</li><li>Ingest/access data and implement OneLake integration for Eventhouse and semantic models</li><li>Create views, functions, and stored procedures; implement a star schema; denormalize, aggregate, and merge/join data</li><li>Enrich data with new columns/tables; resolve duplicate, missing, or null data; convert data types; filter data</li><li>Select, filter, and aggregate data using the Visual Query Editor</li><li>Select, filter, and aggregate data using SQL, KQL, and DAX</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement and manage semantic models (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Choose a storage mode and implement a star schema for a semantic model</li><li>Implement relationships, including bridge tables and many-to-many relationships</li><li>Write DAX calculations using variables and functions (iterators, table filtering, windowing, information functions)</li><li>Implement calculation groups, dynamic format strings, field parameters, and design composite models</li><li>Configure Direct Lake, including default fallback/refresh behavior, and choose Direct Lake on OneLake vs. SQL analytics endpoint</li><li>Improve query, report-visual, and DAX performance; implement incremental refresh for semantic models</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C389' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>FC0-U71</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 IT Concepts and Terminology (13%)</h3><ul><li>Explain the basics of computing (input, processing, output, storage)</li><li>Identify notational systems (binary, hexadecimal, decimal, octal)</li><li>Compare and contrast common units of measure (storage, throughput, processing speed)</li><li>Explain the troubleshooting methodology (identify problem, establish theory, test, plan of action, verify, document)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Infrastructure (24%)</h3><ul><li>Explain common computing devices and their purposes (smartphones, laptops, servers, IoT devices, VR/AR systems)</li><li>Explain the purpose of common internal computing components (motherboard, BIOS, RAM, CPU, GPU, storage, NIC)</li><li>Compare and contrast storage types (volatile vs. non-volatile, local storage, local network storage)</li><li>Install and configure common peripheral devices (printers, scanners, keyboards, displays, UPS)</li><li>Compare and contrast common I/O device interfaces (wired/wireless networking, display ports, peripheral device connectors)</li><li>Compare and contrast virtualization and cloud technologies (hypervisor, IaaS/PaaS/SaaS, deployment models)</li><li>Compare and contrast common internet service types; identify basic networking concepts (IP/MAC address, routers, switches, LAN/WAN); explain small wireless network capabilities (802.11, 2.4GHz/5GHz/6GHz)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Applications and Software (18%)</h3><ul><li>Identify components of an OS (filesystem, file management, system applications/utilities, interfaces)</li><li>Explain the purpose of operating systems (disk/task/application/device management, access control, OS types)</li><li>Explain the purpose and proper use of software (productivity, collaboration, instant messaging, web-browsing, remote support software)</li><li>Configure and use web browser features (private browsing, add-ons/extensions, caching, pop-up blockers, password management)</li><li>Identify common uses of artificial intelligence (AI chatbots, AI assistants, generative AI, AI predictions and suggestions)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Software Development Concepts (13%)</h3><ul><li>Compare and contrast programming language categories (interpreted, compiled, query, assembly)</li><li>Identify fundamental data types and their characteristics (char, strings, numbers, Boolean)</li><li>Explain the purpose and use of programming concepts (identifiers, variables, constants, arrays, functions, objects)</li><li>Identify programming organizational techniques and logic concepts (pseudo code, flow charts, branching, looping)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Data and Database Fundamentals (13%)</h3><ul><li>Explain the value of data and information (critical vs. non-critical data, data-driven business decisions, data monetization, big data)</li><li>Explain database concepts and the purpose of a database (create, import/input, query, reports, storage, data persistence, availability)</li><li>Compare and contrast various database structures (structured/semistructured/non-structured, relational databases with schema/tables/keys, non-relational databases)</li><li>Explain basic data backup concepts (file backups, system backups, restoring data, local vs. cloud storage location)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Security (19%)</h3><ul><li>Explain fundamental security concepts and frameworks (CIA triad, privacy, PII, GDPR, authentication/authorization/accounting)</li><li>Explain methods to secure devices and security best practices (social engineering, anti-malware, firewall, patching, physical device security, software licensing/sources)</li><li>Explain password best practices (length, complexity, history, expiration, managers, reuse)</li><li>Identify common use cases for encryption (data at rest/in transit, file/disk level, VPN, HTTPS)</li><li>Configure security settings for a small wireless network (SSID, default password, WPA/WPA2/WPA3)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C402' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-200</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Configure Microsoft Dataverse (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create/modify standard, activity, or virtual tables and relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many)</li><li>Create or modify columns including rollup and formula columns; configure table properties</li><li>Configure Dataverse search, manage the search index, and manage auditing</li><li>Configure duplicate detection settings and bulk deletion; describe import/export options</li><li>Manage business units, security roles, users and teams, column security, hierarchy security</li><li>Configure Microsoft Entra ID group teams</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Create apps by using Microsoft Power Apps (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure model-driven app forms, views, and custom pages</li><li>Configure modern commanding with Power Fx; embed canvas apps and Power BI in model-driven apps</li><li>Describe canvas app structure, navigation, formulas, variables/collections, and error handling</li><li>Describe how Power Automate flows are called from a canvas app</li><li>Configure Power Pages: pages, forms, lists, navigation, and website security (web roles, page access)</li><li>Describe Power Pages advanced features (document management, search, multi-step forms) and authentication options</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Create and manage logic and process automation (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe cloud flow types, use cases, connectors, and classic workflow scenarios</li><li>Implement logic controls (branches, loops, conditions, error handling, variables) and dynamic content/expressions</li><li>Work with the Dataverse connector; manage and troubleshoot flows</li><li>Configure and manage business process flows (stages, workflow steps, BPF table)</li><li>Configure and troubleshoot classic Dataverse workflows and manage workflow logs</li><li>Configure low-code plug-ins, Power Fx functions/formulas, and business rules</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage environments (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases for app checker and solution checker</li><li>Create and manage Dataverse solutions (managed vs unmanaged); import/export solutions</li><li>Manage Power Platform environments for development</li><li>Configure email integration and SharePoint integration</li><li>Describe document management options and work with Word templates</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C405' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>KCNA</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Kubernetes Fundamentals (44%)</h3><ul><li>Kubernetes Core Concepts (pods, nodes, clusters, namespaces, control plane)</li><li>Administration (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, basic cluster admin)</li><li>Scheduling (how the scheduler places workloads onto nodes)</li><li>Containerization (container basics underpinning Kubernetes workloads)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Container Orchestration (28%)</h3><ul><li>Networking (Kubernetes networking model, service discovery)</li><li>Security (basic Kubernetes security concepts)</li><li>Troubleshooting (diagnosing orchestration issues)</li><li>Storage (Kubernetes storage fundamentals, volumes)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Cloud Native Application Delivery (16%)</h3><ul><li>Application Delivery (CI/CD practices, GitOps-style delivery to Kubernetes)</li><li>Debugging (troubleshooting application delivery pipelines)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Cloud Native Architecture (12%)</h3><ul><li>Observability (monitoring, logging, tracing concepts &mdash; e.g. Prometheus, Fluentd)</li><li>Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles (microservices, immutable infrastructure, CNCF landscape projects like Envoy, gRPC, OpenTracing)</li><li>Cloud Native Community and Collaboration (CNCF governance, open source collaboration model)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C426' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-102</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Deploy and manage a Microsoft 365 tenant (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create a tenant, implement and manage domains, and configure org settings (Security & privacy, Organization profile)</li><li>Monitor Service Health (incl. notifications), Network connectivity insights, and software updates via the M365 admin center</li><li>Create and manage users, external users, contacts, groups (incl. M365 Groups) and shared mailboxes</li><li>Manage and monitor M365 licenses (incl. group-based licensing) and perform bulk user management via Graph/Entra PowerShell</li><li>Implement and manage roles/role groups in M365 and Entra ID, administrative units, and Entra ID roles in Privileged Identity Management (PIM)</li><li>Configure and manage Microsoft 365 Backup and monitor M365 adoption/usage</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C432' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>220-1201</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Mobile Devices (Core 1) (13%)</h3><ul><li>Install components like batteries, cameras, and Wi-Fi antennas</li><li>Configure USB, Bluetooth, NFC, and docking stations</li><li>Configure Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, cellular data, and synchronization settings</li><li>Identify and fix mobile hardware and connectivity issues</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Networking (Core 1) (23%)</h3><ul><li>Networking protocols, ports, and wireless technologies</li><li>Set up small office/home office (SOHO) networks, including IP addressing and VPNs</li><li>Troubleshoot networks with crimpers, cable testers, and Wi-Fi analyzers</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Hardware (Core 1) (25%)</h3><ul><li>Set up RAM, CPUs, and storage devices</li><li>Work with HDMI, Ethernet, and USB cables</li><li>Install and maintain printers, scanners, and other peripherals</li><li>Configure motherboards, power supplies, and cooling solutions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Virtualization and Cloud Computing (Core 1) (11%)</h3><ul><li>Understand virtual machines, hypervisors, and desktop virtualization</li><li>Learn about IaaS, SaaS, and PaaS cloud service models</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Hardware and Network Troubleshooting (Core 1) (28%)</h3><ul><li>Identify and fix hardware, network, and connectivity problems</li><li>Use multimeters, cable testers, and loopback plugs for diagnostics</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Operating Systems (Core 2) (28%)</h3><ul><li>OS installation: work with Windows, macOS, Linux, and mobile operating systems</li><li>Windows tools: manage systems with Task Manager, Command Prompt, and Disk Management</li><li>File systems: handle file systems, updates, and OS upgrades</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Security (Core 2) (28%)</h3><ul><li>Security measures: encryption, access controls, and wireless security protocols</li><li>Malware prevention: detect, remove, and prevent malware threats</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 8 Software Troubleshooting (Core 2) (23%)</h3><ul><li>OS issues: diagnose and resolve problems with operating systems and applications</li><li>Mobile troubleshooting: address connectivity, app, and performance issues</li><li>Security concerns: fix unauthorized access and malware issues</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 9 Operational Procedures (Core 2) (21%)</h3><ul><li>Documentation: best practices for system changes and documentation</li><li>Safety and communication: follow safety protocols and communicate effectively</li><li>Backup and recovery: set up workstation backups and recovery processes</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C471' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SC-900</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe the concepts of security, compliance, and identity (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the shared responsibility model</li><li>Describe defense-in-depth and the Zero Trust model</li><li>Describe encryption and hashing</li><li>Describe Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) concepts</li><li>Define identity as the primary security perimeter; authentication vs authorization</li><li>Describe identity providers, directory services/Active Directory, and federation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Describe the capabilities of Microsoft Entra (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe Microsoft Entra ID, identity types (incl. agent ID), and hybrid identity</li><li>Describe authentication methods and multifactor authentication (MFA)</li><li>Describe password protection and management capabilities</li><li>Describe Microsoft Entra Conditional Access</li><li>Describe Microsoft Entra roles and role-based access control (RBAC)</li><li>Describe Microsoft Entra ID Governance, access reviews, Privileged Identity Management, and Identity Protection</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe the capabilities of Microsoft security solutions (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe core Azure infrastructure security services: DDoS Protection, Firewall, WAF, virtual network segmentation, NSGs, Bastion, Key Vault</li><li>Describe Microsoft Defender for Cloud and Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li><li>Describe security policies/standards/recommendations and cloud workload protection</li><li>Describe SIEM/SOAR concepts and Microsoft Sentinel''s threat detection and mitigation capabilities</li><li>Describe Microsoft Defender XDR services (Defender for Office 365, Endpoint, Cloud Apps, Identity)</li><li>Describe Microsoft Defender Vulnerability Management, Defender Threat Intelligence, and the Defender portal</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Describe the capabilities of Microsoft compliance solutions (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the Service Trust Portal offerings and Microsoft''s privacy principles</li><li>Describe the Microsoft Purview portal, Compliance Manager, and compliance score</li><li>Describe data classification, Content explorer/Activity explorer, sensitivity labels and policies</li><li>Describe data loss prevention (DLP), records management, and retention policies/labels</li><li>Describe insider risk management</li><li>Describe eDiscovery and audit solutions in Microsoft Purview</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C472' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MD-102</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Prepare infrastructure for devices (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Add devices to Microsoft Entra ID (join type selection, device join/registration, dynamic device groups)</li><li>Enroll devices to Microsoft Intune (Windows automatic enrollment, macOS/iOS/iPadOS personal enrollment, Android enrollment profiles, Apple Business Manager, Samsung Knox / Google Zero Touch)</li><li>Manage built-in and custom RBAC roles, scope tags and scoped administration, multi-admin approval</li><li>Implement compliance policies across platforms and Conditional Access policies requiring compliance status</li><li>Configure Windows Hello for Business and Windows LAPS via Intune/Entra ID</li><li>Manage local group membership on Windows devices by using Intune</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Manage and maintain devices (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Deploy/upgrade Windows clients via Windows Autopilot (deployment profiles, modes, ESP, device naming) and Windows 11 upgrades</li><li>Provision and configure Windows 365 Cloud PCs (provisioning policies, network connections, image management) and Windows Backup and Restore</li><li>Plan and implement device configuration profiles for Windows, Android, iOS/iPadOS, macOS, and specialty devices; target via assignment filters</li><li>Implement Intune Suite add-ons: Endpoint Privilege Management, Enterprise App Catalog, Remote Help, Microsoft Cloud PKI, Microsoft Tunnel for MAM, Intune Advanced Analytics</li><li>Perform remote actions on devices (sync/restart/retire/wipe, bulk actions, rotate BitLocker/local admin passwords, KQL device queries)</li><li>Collect device diagnostics and logs using Microsoft Intune Troubleshooting blade</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Protect devices (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create antivirus, disk encryption (BitLocker), firewall, and Attack Surface Reduction policies via Intune</li><li>Plan and implement security baselines; integrate Intune with Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (EDR policies, threat investigation, incident triage, onboarding)</li><li>Configure App Control for Business policies</li><li>Plan for and manage device updates: update rings, feature/quality updates, Windows Autopatch and Hotpatch, Settings Catalog update policies for iOS/iPadOS/macOS, Android update management, Delivery Optimization</li><li>Monitor device updates by using Intune</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Manage and secure applications (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Prepare and deploy apps via Intune (Win32, LOB, Microsoft Store apps); configure Quiet Time policies</li><li>Deploy and manage Microsoft 365 Apps (Office Deployment Tool, Autopilot deployment, Microsoft 365 Apps admin center)</li><li>Deploy apps from platform app stores (Apple VPP, Google Play); monitor deployment status and troubleshoot failures</li><li>Plan and implement app protection policies for managed/unmanaged (BYOD) devices</li><li>Implement Conditional Access policies for app protection; plan and implement app configuration policies</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Optimize endpoint operations by using automation, monitoring, and reporting (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Automate Intune management tasks using PowerShell and Microsoft Graph; extend device compliance via PowerShell</li><li>Use Security Copilot agents in Intune to investigate threats, analyze device performance, and review recommendations</li><li>Implement reporting/data visibility (workbooks, dashboards, exports) and monitor endpoint performance via Endpoint Analytics</li><li>Configure and manage proactive remediation scripts</li><li>Analyze endpoint reliability/user experience scores; monitor tenant health and Intune service communications</li><li>Configure alerts and notifications for policy/compliance changes</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C476' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CLSSGB-001</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Six Sigma and Organizational Goals</h3><ul><li>Define what Six Sigma is and its value proposition</li><li>Identify organizational drivers and metrics</li><li>Build the business case for a Six Sigma initiative</li><li>Align Six Sigma projects with organizational goals and strategy</li><li>Understand the Six Sigma implementation roadmap</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Lean Principles in the Organization</h3><ul><li>Apply core Lean concepts and tools</li><li>Differentiate value-added vs. non-value-added activities</li><li>Apply the Theory of Constraints</li><li>Understand how Lean integrates with Six Sigma (Lean Six Sigma)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design for Six Sigma (DFSS) in the Organization</h3><ul><li>Apply Quality Function Deployment (QFD)</li><li>Conduct Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA, DFMEA, PFMEA)</li><li>Follow a DFSS roadmap for new process/product design</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Introduction to the Define Phase</h3><ul><li>Identify process elements and boundaries</li><li>Identify and analyze customers and Voice of the Customer (VOC)</li><li>Collect and analyze Define-phase data</li><li>Translate customer requirements into project requirements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Project Management Basics</h3><ul><li>Develop a project charter and define scope</li><li>Select and track project metrics</li><li>Use project planning tools</li><li>Perform risk analysis</li><li>Execute project closure procedures</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Other Tools and Techniques</h3><ul><li>Apply Design of Experiments (DOE)</li><li>Use charting methods for process analysis</li><li>Apply core Six Sigma statistical fundamentals</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Process Analysis and Documentation</h3><ul><li>Build process models and map inputs/outputs</li><li>Apply basic statistics and probability concepts</li><li>Interpret sampling distributions</li><li>Document process analysis findings</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 8 Collecting and Summarizing Data</h3><ul><li>Distinguish data types (continuous vs. discrete)</li><li>Apply data collection methods and plans</li><li>Ensure data integrity</li><li>Calculate descriptive statistics</li><li>Use graphical methods to summarize data</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 9 Lean Process Improvement</h3><ul><li>Apply Lean thinking to process improvement</li><li>Understand the Toyota Production System</li><li>Identify the types of waste (muda)</li><li>Apply the PDSA (Plan-Do-Study-Act) cycle</li><li>Run Kaizen events</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C481' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SC-401</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement information protection (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage data classification (sensitive info types, EDM, document fingerprinting, trainable classifiers, OCR support)</li><li>Implement and manage sensitivity labels in Microsoft Purview (roles/permissions, label + auto-labeling + publishing policies, container labeling for Teams/M365 Groups/Power BI/SharePoint, labeling via Defender for Cloud Apps)</li><li>Implement information protection for Windows, file shares, and Exchange (Purview Information Protection client, on-prem scanner bulk classification, Purview Message Encryption, Advanced Message Encryption)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement data loss prevention and retention (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure DLP policies (design, roles/permissions, Adaptive Protection, policy/rule precedence, Defender for Cloud Apps file policies)</li><li>Implement and monitor Microsoft Purview Endpoint DLP (device requirements/extensions, advanced device rules, just-in-time protection, endpoint activity monitoring)</li><li>Implement and manage retention (retention labels + adaptive policy scopes, publish/auto-apply label policies, policy precedence/Policy lookup, retention policies, content recovery)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Manage risks, alerts, and activities (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and manage Microsoft Purview Insider Risk Management (roles/permissions, connectors, Defender for Endpoint integration, policy indicators/templates, Adaptive Protection risk levels, case/alert workflow, forensic evidence, notice templates)</li><li>Manage information security alerts and activities (Purview Audit Premium licensing, unified audit investigation, audit retention, Activity explorer, DLP/insider-risk alert response, Defender XDR alert response, Defender for Cloud Apps file-policy alerts, eDiscovery searches)</li><li>Protect data used by AI services (Purview + M365 workload controls for AI environments, DSPM for AI prerequisites/roles/permissions/policies/activity monitoring)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C482' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CISSP</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Security and Risk Management (16%)</h3><ul><li>Understand, adhere to, and promote professional ethics</li><li>Understand and apply security concepts (CIA triad, etc.)</li><li>Evaluate and apply security governance principles</li><li>Understand legal, regulatory, and compliance issues relating to information security</li><li>Understand requirements for investigation types</li><li>Develop, document, and implement security policy, standards, procedures, and guidelines</li><li>Understand and apply risk management concepts, threat modeling, and Supply Chain Risk Management</li><li>Establish and maintain a security awareness, education, and training program</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Asset Security (10%)</h3><ul><li>Identify and classify information and assets</li><li>Establish information and asset handling requirements</li><li>Provision resources securely</li><li>Manage data lifecycle</li><li>Ensure appropriate asset retention</li><li>Determine data security controls and compliance requirements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Security Architecture and Engineering (13%)</h3><ul><li>Research, implement, and manage engineering processes using secure design principles</li><li>Understand the fundamental concepts of security models</li><li>Select controls based on systems security requirements</li><li>Understand security capabilities of Information Systems</li><li>Assess and mitigate vulnerabilities in systems</li><li>Select and determine cryptographic solutions; understand methods of cryptanalytic attacks</li><li>Apply security principles to site and facility design and controls</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Communication and Network Security (13%)</h3><ul><li>Assess and implement secure design principles in network architectures</li><li>Secure network components</li><li>Implement secure communication channels according to design</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Identity and Access Management (IAM) (13%)</h3><ul><li>Control physical and logical access to assets</li><li>Design identification and authentication strategy</li><li>Federated identity with a third-party service</li><li>Implement and manage authorization mechanisms</li><li>Manage the identity and access provisioning lifecycle</li><li>Implement authentication systems</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Security Assessment and Testing (12%)</h3><ul><li>Design and validate assessment, test, and audit strategies</li><li>Conduct security control testing</li><li>Collect security process data</li><li>Analyze test output and generate reports</li><li>Conduct or facilitate security audits</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Security Operations (13%)</h3><ul><li>Understand and comply with investigations and support them</li><li>Conduct logging and monitoring activities; apply resource protection</li><li>Perform configuration management, patch and vulnerability management, and incident management</li><li>Operate and maintain detective and preventative measures</li><li>Implement recovery strategies and disaster recovery processes; test DR plans</li><li>Participate in Business Continuity planning and exercises</li><li>Implement and manage physical security and personnel safety concerns</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 8 Software Development Security (10%)</h3><ul><li>Understand and integrate security in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)</li><li>Identify and apply security controls in development ecosystems</li><li>Assess the effectiveness of software security</li><li>Assess the security impact of acquired software</li><li>Define and apply secure coding guidelines and standards</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C483' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DOP-C02</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Content Domain 1: SDLC Automation (22%)</h3><ul><li>Implement CI/CD pipelines (repositories, build processes e.g. CodeBuild, deployment strategies e.g. CodeDeploy, managing build/deployment secrets)</li><li>Integrate automated testing into CI/CD pipelines (unit/integration/acceptance/UI tests, security scans, load/stress testing)</li><li>Build and manage artifacts (artifact repositories e.g. CodeArtifact/S3/ECR, automating EC2/container image builds e.g. EC2 Image Builder)</li><li>Implement deployment strategies for instance, container, and serverless environments (blue/green, canary, mutable vs immutable patterns)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Content Domain 2: Configuration Management and IaC (17%)</h3><ul><li>Define cloud infrastructure and reusable components using IaC (AWS SAM, CloudFormation, CDK, StackSets)</li><li>Deploy automation to create, onboard, and secure AWS accounts in multi-account/multi-Region environments (AWS Organizations, Control Tower, SCPs)</li><li>Design and build automated solutions for complex tasks and large-scale environments (Systems Manager, AWS Config, Lambda, Step Functions)</li><li>Maintain software and configuration compliance at scale</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Content Domain 3: Resilient Cloud Solutions (15%)</h3><ul><li>Implement highly available solutions to meet resilience and business requirements (Multi-AZ, multi-Region, replication/failover)</li><li>Implement solutions that are scalable to meet business requirements (auto scaling, load balancing, caching, containers, serverless)</li><li>Implement automated recovery processes to meet RTO and RPO requirements (AWS Backup, pilot light, warm standby, failover testing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Content Domain 4: Monitoring and Logging (15%)</h3><ul><li>Configure the collection, aggregation, and storage of logs and metrics (CloudWatch metrics/logs, metric filters, log lifecycle, encryption)</li><li>Audit, monitor, and analyze logs and metrics to detect issues (CloudWatch dashboards/alarms, X-Ray, Athena, Config rules, CloudTrail)</li><li>Automate monitoring and event management of complex environments (EventBridge, auto scaling triggers, health checks, S3 event processing)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Content Domain 5: Incident and Event Response (14%)</h3><ul><li>Manage event sources to process, notify, and take action in response to events (EventBridge, CloudTrail, SQS/SNS/Lambda/Step Functions workflows)</li><li>Implement configuration changes in response to events (Systems Manager, AWS Config remediation of non-desired system state)</li><li>Troubleshoot system and application failures (analyzing failed deployments via CodePipeline/CodeBuild/CodeDeploy/CloudFormation, root cause analysis)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Content Domain 6: Security and Compliance (17%)</h3><ul><li>Implement techniques for identity and access management at scale (IAM entities, identity federation, permissions boundaries, least privilege)</li><li>Apply automation for security controls and data protection (network security, encryption/KMS, Macie, defense in depth)</li><li>Implement security monitoring and auditing solutions (CloudTrail, Config, VPC Flow Logs, GuardDuty, Inspector, IAM Access Analyzer)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C503' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Professional</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Bootstrapping and maintaining a Google Cloud organization (20%)</h3><ul><li>Design the overall resource hierarchy (application-centric org/projects/folders, shared networking via Shared VPC/VPC Peering/Private Service Connect, multi-project monitoring/logging, IAM roles + org policies, service accounts, data residency)</li><li>Manage infrastructure with IaC tooling (Infrastructure Manager, Cloud Foundation Toolkit, Config Connector, GitOps, Terraform, Helm) and scripting automation (Python, Go)</li><li>Design CI/CD architecture stacks across Google Cloud, hybrid, and multi-cloud (Cloud Build, Cloud Deploy with Kustomize/Skaffold, Artifact Registry, Jenkins/Argo CD/Packer/kpt, CI/CD tooling security)</li><li>Manage multiple environments (ephemeral environments, configuration/policy management, GKE fleets, safe patching and upgrading)</li><li>Enable secure cloud development environments (Cloud Workstations, Cloud Shell, bootstrapping with custom images/IDE/Cloud SDK, AI-assisted dev/ops via Gemini Code Assist/Cloud Assist/CLI)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Building and implementing CI/CD pipelines, including continuous testing, for application, infrastructure, and machine learning workloads (25%)</h3><ul><li>Design pipelines (CI/CD of apps and infrastructure, artifact management, deployment to hybrid/multi-cloud/GKE, pipeline triggers, approval flows)</li><li>Implement and manage pipelines (auditing/tracking deployments via Cloud Audit Logs, deployment strategies like canary/blue-green/rolling/traffic-splitting/feature flags, troubleshooting deployment issues)</li><li>Manage pipeline configuration and secrets (Cloud KMS, Secret Manager, Certificate Manager, Parameter Manager, Workload Identity Federation, build vs runtime secret injection)</li><li>Secure the deployment pipeline (Artifact Analysis/vulnerability scanning, Binary Authorization, SLSA framework, environment-based IAM policies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Applying site reliability engineering practices (18%)</h3><ul><li>Balance change velocity and reliability (defining SLIs/SLOs/SLAs, error budgets, opportunity cost of risk vs number of nines)</li><li>Manage service lifecycle (planning, deployment, maintenance, retirement)</li><li>Capacity planning (quotas, limits, reservations, Dynamic Workload Scheduler) and autoscaling (managed instance groups, Cloud Run, GKE)</li><li>Mitigate incident impact on users (draining/redirecting traffic, adding capacity, rollback strategies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Implementing observability practices and troubleshooting issues (25%)</h3><ul><li>Instrument and collect telemetry (Ops Agent, OpenTelemetry, Cloud Audit/VPC Flow Logs, log optimization, metrics collection incl. Managed Service for Prometheus, synthetic monitors, custom/log-based metrics)</li><li>Manage and analyze logs (Logs Explorer, Logging query language, exporting to BigQuery/Pub/Sub/Cloud Storage, PII/PHI redaction, Gemini Cloud Assist log analysis)</li><li>Manage metrics, dashboards, and alerts (Metrics Explorer, dashboards/PromQL, alerting policies on SLIs/SLOs/cost, third-party integrations like PagerDuty, Gemini Cloud Assist for metrics)</li><li>Capture and analyze distributed traces (OpenTelemetry, trace waterfalls/spans, correlating trace IDs with logs, Gemini Cloud Assist trace analysis)</li><li>Troubleshoot infrastructure, CI/CD pipeline, application, observability, and performance/latency issues</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section 5: Optimizing performance and cost (12%)</h3><ul><li>Collect performance information via application performance monitoring and Active Assist insights/recommendations</li><li>Implement FinOps practices for observability costs and Spot VMs</li><li>Optimize resource usage for cost/efficiency and plan infrastructure cost (committed-use/sustained-use discounts, network tiers)</li><li>Leverage Google Cloud recommenders (cost, security, performance, manageability, reliability) and optimize individual workload costs (GKE, Cloud Run, Compute Engine)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C504' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>N/A</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Designing data processing systems (22%)</h3><ul><li>Designing for security and compliance (IAM, encryption/key management, PII handling, data sovereignty, legal/regulatory compliance, project/dataset/table governance architecture, multi-environment dev vs prod)</li><li>Designing for reliability and fidelity (data prep/cleaning with Dataform/Dataflow/Cloud Data Fusion, pipeline monitoring and orchestration, disaster recovery and fault tolerance, ACID compliance and availability decisions, data validation)</li><li>Designing for flexibility and portability (mapping current/future business requirements, multi-cloud and data residency portability, data staging/cataloging/profiling/discovery)</li><li>Designing data migrations (analyzing stakeholder needs and planning target state, planning migration/validation via BigQuery Data Transfer Service, Database Migration Service, Transfer Appliance, Datastream)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Ingesting and processing the data (25%)</h3><ul><li>Planning the data pipelines (defining sources/sinks, transformation and orchestration logic, networking fundamentals, data encryption)</li><li>Building the pipelines (data cleansing; choosing services such as Dataflow, Apache Beam, Dataproc, Cloud Data Fusion, BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Spark, Hadoop, Kafka; batch vs streaming transformations incl. windowing and late-arriving data; AI data enrichment; data acquisition/import and integrating new sources)</li><li>Deploying and operationalizing the pipelines (job automation/orchestration via Cloud Composer and Workflows; CI/CD)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Storing the data (20%)</h3><ul><li>Selecting storage systems (analyzing access patterns; choosing managed services like BigQuery, BigLake, AlloyDB, Bigtable, Spanner, Cloud SQL, Cloud Storage, Firestore, Memorystore; planning for cost/performance; data lifecycle management)</li><li>Planning for using a data warehouse (data model design, degree of normalization, mapping business requirements, architecture for access patterns)</li><li>Using a data lake (managing discovery/access/cost controls, processing data, monitoring the lake)</li><li>Designing for a data platform (building a platform with Dataplex, Dataplex Catalog, BigQuery, Cloud Storage; federated governance model for distributed data systems)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Preparing and using data for analysis (15%)</h3><ul><li>Preparing data for visualization (connecting to BI tools, precalculating fields, BigQuery BI features like BI Engine and materialized views, troubleshooting poor-performing queries, security/data masking/IAM/Cloud DLP)</li><li>Preparing data for AI and ML (feature engineering and training/serving ML models e.g. BigQuery ML; preparing unstructured data for embeddings and RAG)</li><li>Sharing data (defining sharing rules, publishing datasets, publishing reports/visualizations, BigQuery sharing via Analytics Hub)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section 5: Maintaining and automating data workloads (18%)</h3><ul><li>Optimizing resources (minimizing costs, ensuring sufficient resources for business-critical processes, persistent vs job-based clusters e.g. Dataproc)</li><li>Designing automation and repeatability (creating DAGs for Cloud Composer, scheduling/orchestrating jobs repeatably)</li><li>Organizing workloads based on business requirements (capacity management via BigQuery Editions/reservations, interactive vs batch query jobs)</li><li>Monitoring and troubleshooting processes (observability via Cloud Monitoring/Logging/BigQuery admin panel, monitoring usage, troubleshooting errors/billing/quotas, managing jobs/queries/compute capacity)</li><li>Maintaining awareness of failures and mitigating impact (fault tolerance and restart design, multi-region/zone jobs, preparing for data corruption/missing data, replication and failover e.g. Cloud SQL, Redis clusters)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C511' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PMP</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 People (33%)</h3><ul><li>Develop a common/shared vision with key stakeholders and keep it current</li><li>Manage conflicts (identify sources, analyze context, implement resolution strategy)</li><li>Lead the project team (empower team, establish roles/responsibilities, determine leadership style)</li><li>Engage stakeholders and align expectations across internal/external customers</li><li>Help ensure knowledge transfer (identify critical knowledge, foster knowledge-transfer environment)</li><li>Plan and manage communication, reporting, and governance support</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Process (41%)</h3><ul><li>Develop an integrated project management plan and recommend a development approach (predictive/adaptive/hybrid)</li><li>Develop and manage project scope; help ensure value-based delivery</li><li>Plan and manage resources, procurement, and finance</li><li>Plan and optimize quality of products/deliverables</li><li>Plan and manage schedule (create, baseline, execute, analyze variance)</li><li>Evaluate project status and manage project closure</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Business Environment (26%)</h3><ul><li>Define and establish project governance (structure, rules, success metrics, escalation paths)</li><li>Plan and manage project compliance (security, health/safety, sustainability, regulatory)</li><li>Manage and control changes via the change control process</li><li>Remove impediments and manage issues; distinguish risks from issues</li><li>Plan and manage risk (identify, analyze, monitor/control, maintain risk register)</li><li>Support continuous improvement, organizational change, and evaluate external business environment changes</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C523' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>IASSC-CYB</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 1.0 Define Phase</h3><ul><li>Basics of Six Sigma &mdash; meanings & history of Six Sigma, deliverables of a Lean Six Sigma project, the problem-solving strategy Y=f(x), Voice of the Customer/Business/Employee, Six Sigma roles & responsibilities</li><li>Fundamentals of Six Sigma &mdash; defining a process, Critical to Quality characteristics (CTQs), Cost of Poor Quality (COPQ), Pareto Analysis (80:20 rule), basic Six Sigma metrics (DPU, DPMO, FTY, RTY, Cycle Time)</li><li>Selecting Lean Six Sigma Projects &mdash; building a business case & project charter, developing project metrics, financial evaluation & benefits capture</li><li>The Lean Enterprise &mdash; understanding Lean and its history, Lean & Six Sigma integration, the Seven Elements of Waste, 5S (Sort, Straighten, Shine, Standardize, Self-Discipline)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 2.0 Measure Phase</h3><ul><li>Process Definition &mdash; cause & effect/fishbone diagrams, process mapping/SIPOC/value stream map, X-Y diagram, Failure Modes & Effects Analysis (FMEA)</li><li>Six Sigma Statistics &mdash; basic and descriptive statistics, normal distributions & normality, graphical analysis</li><li>Measurement System Analysis &mdash; precision & accuracy, bias/linearity/stability, Gage Repeatability & Reproducibility (Gage R&R), variable & attribute MSA</li><li>Process Capability &mdash; capability analysis, concept of stability, attribute & discrete capability, monitoring techniques</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 3.0 Control Phase</h3><ul><li>Lean Controls &mdash; control methods for 5S</li><li>Lean Controls &mdash; Kanban</li><li>Lean Controls &mdash; Poka-Yoke (mistake proofing)</li><li>Six Sigma Control Plans &mdash; cost-benefit analysis</li><li>Six Sigma Control Plans &mdash; elements of the control plan</li><li>Six Sigma Control Plans &mdash; elements of the response plan</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C524' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SC-200</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Manage a security operations environment (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure automation for Microsoft Defender XDR and Microsoft Sentinel (automation rules, playbooks, automated investigation/response, automatic attack disruption)</li><li>Configure the Microsoft Sentinel SIEM and platform (roles, data retention across Analytics/Data lake/XDR tiers, workbooks, SOC optimization)</li><li>Ingest data into the Sentinel SIEM and platform (data connectors, Windows Security Events via AMA/WEF, Syslog/CEF via AMA, Azure activity logs, threat indicators, custom log tables)</li><li>Configure detections (custom detection rules via Advanced Hunting, Sentinel analytics rules &mdash; scheduled/NRT/threat intelligence/ML, MITRE ATT&CK coverage analysis, anomalies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Respond to security incidents (37.5%)</h3><ul><li>Respond to alerts and incidents in Microsoft Defender XDR (Defender for Office 365, Purview, Defender for Cloud, Defender for Cloud Apps, Entra ID, Defender for Identity, Sentinel)</li><li>Investigate incidents using agentic AI / embedded Security Copilot and handle complex multi-stage, multi-domain, lateral-movement attacks</li><li>Respond to alerts and incidents in Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (device timelines, live response, evidence/entity investigation, automatic attack disruption remediation)</li><li>Investigate Microsoft 365 activities to identify threats (Purview Audit, eDiscovery Content search, Microsoft Graph activity logs)</li><li>Manage security incidents using case management</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Perform threat hunting (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Detect threats using Microsoft Defender XDR (KQL queries, Advanced Hunting, threat analytics interpretation, hunting graphs / blast radius, Sentinel Graph entity relationships)</li><li>Detect threats using the Microsoft Sentinel platform (hunting queries, KQL jobs in Data lake, Summary rule tables, Notebooks incl. Sentinel MCP Server connection)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C542' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SC-300</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Implement and manage user identities (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure and manage a Microsoft Entra tenant (roles, administrative units, domains, company branding, tenant/user/group/device settings)</li><li>Create, configure, and manage Microsoft Entra identities (users, groups, custom security attributes, bulk operations, device join/registration, licensing)</li><li>Implement and manage identities for external users and tenants (B2B collaboration, cross-tenant access/sync, external identity providers)</li><li>Implement and manage hybrid identity (Entra Connect Sync/Cloud Sync, password hash sync, pass-through auth, seamless SSO, AD FS migration, Entra Connect Health)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement authentication and access management (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan, implement, and manage Microsoft Entra user authentication (MFA, SSPR, Windows Hello for Business, passwordless/FIDO2, Entra Kerberos, password protection)</li><li>Plan, implement, and manage Microsoft Entra Conditional Access (policy assignments/controls, session management, continuous access evaluation, authentication context, protected actions)</li><li>Manage risk by using Microsoft Entra ID Protection (user/sign-in risk policies, MFA registration campaigns, remediate risky users/sign-ins/workload identities)</li><li>Implement Global Secure Access (clients, Private Access, Internet Access, Internet Access for Microsoft 365)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Plan and implement workload identities (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement identities for applications and Azure workloads (managed identities, service principals, managed service accounts)</li><li>Plan, implement, and monitor the integration of enterprise applications (Application Proxy, SaaS app integration, app roles, consent, application collections)</li><li>Plan and implement app registrations (authentication, API permissions, app roles)</li><li>Manage and monitor app access by using Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps (cloud discovery, connected apps, Conditional Access app control, session policies, OAuth app policies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Plan and automate identity governance (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement entitlement management (catalogs, access packages, access requests, terms of use, connected organizations)</li><li>Plan, implement, and manage access reviews in Microsoft Entra</li><li>Plan and implement privileged access via Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management (PIM) for Entra roles, Azure resources, and PIM for Groups, including break-glass accounts</li><li>Monitor identity activity by using logs, workbooks, and reports (sign-in/audit/provisioning logs, diagnostic settings, KQL in Log Analytics, Identity Secure Score)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C591' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>SY0-701</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 1.0 General Security Concepts (12%)</h3><ul><li>1.1 Compare and contrast various types of security controls (categories: technical/managerial/operational/physical; types: preventive/deterrent/detective/corrective/compensating/directive)</li><li>1.2 Summarize fundamental security concepts (CIA, non-repudiation, AAA, Zero Trust, physical security, deception/disruption technology)</li><li>1.3 Explain the importance of change management processes and the impact to security</li><li>1.4 Explain the importance of using appropriate cryptographic solutions</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 2.0 Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Mitigations (22%)</h3><ul><li>2.1 Compare and contrast common threat actors and motivations</li><li>2.2 Explain common threat vectors and attack surfaces</li><li>2.3 Explain various types of vulnerabilities</li><li>2.4 Given a scenario, analyze indicators of malicious activity</li><li>2.5 Explain the purpose of mitigation techniques used to secure the enterprise</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 3.0 Security Architecture (18%)</h3><ul><li>3.1 Compare and contrast security implications of different architecture models</li><li>3.2 Given a scenario, apply security principles to secure enterprise infrastructure</li><li>3.3 Compare and contrast concepts and strategies to protect data</li><li>3.4 Explain the importance of resilience and recovery in security architecture</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 4.0 Security Operations (28%)</h3><ul><li>4.1 Given a scenario, apply common security techniques to computing resources</li><li>4.2 Explain the security implications of proper hardware, software, and data asset management</li><li>4.3 Explain various activities associated with vulnerability management</li><li>4.6 Given a scenario, implement and maintain identity and access management</li><li>4.7 Explain the importance of automation and orchestration related to secure operations</li><li>4.8/4.9 Explain appropriate incident response activities; given a scenario, use data sources to support an investigation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 5.0 Security Program Management and Oversight (20%)</h3><ul><li>5.1 Summarize elements of effective security governance</li><li>5.2 Explain elements of the risk management process</li><li>5.3 Explain the processes associated with third-party risk assessment and management</li><li>5.4 Summarize elements of effective security compliance</li><li>5.5 Explain types and purposes of audits and assessments</li><li>5.6 Given a scenario, implement security awareness practices</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C628' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Neo4j</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Cypher (40%)</h3><ul><li>Read data with MATCH, WHERE, and RETURN clauses</li><li>Filter results by node/relationship properties and labels</li><li>Write data with CREATE, MERGE, SET, and DELETE</li><li>Use graph patterns to traverse nodes and relationships (including variable-length paths)</li><li>Aggregate and order results (COUNT, COLLECT, ORDER BY, LIMIT)</li><li>Use parameters and built-in functions in Cypher statements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Neo4j Fundamentals (13.8%)</h3><ul><li>Explain core graph database concepts: nodes, relationships, labels, and properties</li><li>Describe graph theory basics and when a graph database is the right fit</li><li>Understand Neo4j''s native graph storage and property-graph model</li><li>Use Neo4j Browser / tooling to explore a database</li><li>Explain ACID transaction guarantees in Neo4j</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Schema & Indexes (11.2%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage constraints (uniqueness, existence, node key)</li><li>Create and use single-property and composite indexes</li><li>Understand full-text indexes</li><li>Explain how schema/index choices affect query performance</li><li>Apply best practices for schema design</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Drivers (10%)</h3><ul><li>Connect an application to Neo4j using an official driver (e.g. Python)</li><li>Execute Cypher queries and handle results/sessions/transactions from driver code</li><li>Manage sessions, transaction functions, and error handling</li><li>Use driver configuration for routing/connection pooling basics</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Data Modeling (10%)</h3><ul><li>Translate business/domain requirements into a graph data model</li><li>Identify entities as nodes vs. relationships vs. properties</li><li>Model many-to-many relationships and avoid anti-patterns (e.g. dense nodes, over-generalized relationship types)</li><li>Iterate a model based on the questions the graph must answer</li><li>Apply naming conventions for labels, relationship types, and properties</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Importing Data (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Use LOAD CSV to import data from CSV files into a graph</li><li>Create nodes and relationships during import with MERGE to avoid duplicates</li><li>Handle large imports efficiently (batching, periodic commit considerations)</li><li>Transform and clean source data during the import process</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 7 Hands-on Challenges (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Write and execute live Cypher statements in an integrated query window against a provided dataset</li><li>Solve practical query-writing tasks combining reading, filtering, and aggregation</li><li>Demonstrate applied Cypher proficiency beyond multiple-choice recall</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C631' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ANS-C01</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Network Design (30%)</h3><ul><li>Design solutions using edge network services (CloudFront, Global Accelerator) for global traffic and performance optimization</li><li>Design DNS solutions (Route 53 public/private/hybrid hosted zones, resolvers, DNSSEC, traffic policies) for public, private, and hybrid requirements</li><li>Design load balancing solutions (ALB/NLB/GWLB) for high availability, scalability, and security</li><li>Define logging and monitoring requirements across AWS and hybrid networks (CloudWatch, Flow Logs, Traffic Mirroring, Reachability Analyzer)</li><li>Design routing strategy and hybrid connectivity architecture between on-premises networks and AWS (Direct Connect, Site-to-Site VPN, BGP, SD-WAN)</li><li>Design multi-account, multi-Region, multi-VPC routing and connectivity architectures (VPC peering, Transit Gateway, PrivateLink, VPC sharing, IP overlap handling)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Network Implementation (26%)</h3><ul><li>Implement routing and connectivity between on-premises networks and AWS (Direct Connect, VPNs, VLANs, static/dynamic routing)</li><li>Implement routing and connectivity across multiple AWS accounts, Regions, and VPCs (hub-and-spoke, Transit Gateway, PrivateLink, AWS RAM)</li><li>Implement complex hybrid and multi-account DNS architectures (conditional forwarding, DNS delegation, DNSSEC, Route 53 Resolver endpoints)</li><li>Automate and configure network infrastructure using infrastructure as code (CDK, CloudFormation, CLI, SDK/APIs) and event-driven automation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Network Management and Operation (20%)</h3><ul><li>Maintain routing and connectivity on AWS and hybrid networks (BGP over Direct Connect, Transit Gateway, route tables, quotas/limits)</li><li>Monitor and analyze network traffic to troubleshoot and optimize connectivity (CloudWatch, VPC Flow Logs, Traffic Mirroring, Reachability Analyzer, Transit Gateway Network Manager)</li><li>Optimize AWS networks for performance, reliability, and cost-effectiveness (VPC peering vs. Transit Gateway, multicast, network interface selection, subnet/CIDR optimization, jumbo frames, Global Accelerator)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Network Security, Compliance, and Governance (24%)</h3><ul><li>Implement and maintain network features to meet security and compliance needs (AWS WAF, Shield, Network Firewall, security groups, NACLs, threat modeling, perimeter VPC/three-tier architectures)</li><li>Validate and audit security using network monitoring and logging services (VPC Flow Logs, Traffic Mirroring, CloudTrail, Firewall Manager, Trusted Advisor, CloudWatch alarms)</li><li>Implement and maintain confidentiality of data and communications in transit (IPsec, TLS termination/passthrough, VPN over Direct Connect, ACM/ACM Private CA certificate management, DNSSEC)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C635' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MB-910</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Describe Dynamics 365 Customer Insights (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe use cases and capabilities of Customer Insights - Journeys (lead generation/qualification, marketing forms, segments, email marketing, customer journeys, event management)</li><li>Describe use cases and capabilities of Customer Insights - Data (unified customer profiles, measures, segments, predictions)</li><li>Describe how to use Microsoft 365 Copilot with Customer Insights - Journeys</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Describe Dynamics 365 Sales (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe leads, lead qualification, opportunity management, quote lifecycle, and order/invoice management processes</li><li>Describe guided selling (business process flows), the product catalog, price lists, and unit groups</li><li>Describe sales pipeline and forecasting concepts</li><li>Describe Sales Insights, LinkedIn Sales Insights, and the Dynamics 365 Sales mobile app</li><li>Describe Microsoft 365 Copilot for Sales and the Sales accelerator</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Describe Dynamics 365 Customer Service (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe workload management: cases, basic routing rulesets (queues), Unified Routing, and the inbox for agents</li><li>Describe knowledge management and the case lifecycle (SLAs, entitlements)</li><li>Describe Omnichannel for Customer Service and agent productivity tools</li><li>Describe reporting and data visualization options in Customer Service</li><li>Describe use cases for Copilot in Customer Service</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Describe Dynamics 365 Field Service (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe the work order lifecycle and inspections in Field Service</li><li>Describe the Field Service mobile app and Copilot use cases in Field Service</li><li>Describe resource management and scheduling processes</li><li>Describe asset management, customer assets, and Connected Field Service for Dynamics 365</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Explore the core capabilities of customer engagement apps in Dynamics 365 (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Describe customer engagement apps, Microsoft Power Platform, and Microsoft Dataverse as the foundation</li><li>Navigate to and within customer engagement apps; describe Copilot capabilities across the apps</li><li>Describe customers, activities, search options, and filter criteria</li><li>Describe reporting capabilities including dashboards, charts, and views</li><li>Describe integration with Microsoft Teams, Outlook, Excel/Word, and SharePoint</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C665' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-204</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Develop Azure compute solutions (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement containerized solutions: create/manage container images, publish to Azure Container Registry, run containers via Azure Container Instances, build solutions with Azure Container Apps</li><li>Implement Azure App Service Web Apps: create the app, configure diagnostics/logging, deploy code and containerized solutions, configure TLS/API settings/service connections, implement autoscaling, configure deployment slots</li><li>Implement Azure Functions: create and configure a Functions app, implement input and output bindings, implement triggers via data operations, timers, and webhooks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Develop for Azure storage (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Develop solutions using Azure Cosmos DB: perform container/item operations via SDK, set the appropriate consistency level, implement change feed notifications</li><li>Develop solutions using Azure Blob Storage: set/retrieve properties and metadata, perform data operations via SDK, implement storage policies and data lifecycle management</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement Azure security (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Authenticate/authorize users via the Microsoft Identity platform and Microsoft Entra ID</li><li>Create and implement shared access signatures</li><li>Implement solutions that interact with Microsoft Graph</li><li>Secure app configuration data using Azure App Configuration or Azure Key Vault</li><li>Develop code that uses keys, secrets, and certificates stored in Azure Key Vault</li><li>Implement Managed Identities for Azure resources</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Monitor and troubleshoot Azure solutions (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor and analyze metrics, logs, and traces via Azure Monitor Application Insights</li><li>Implement availability tests and alerts</li><li>Instrument an app or service to use Application Insights</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Connect to and consume Azure services and third-party services (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement Azure API Management: create an instance, create/document APIs, configure access to APIs, implement policies for APIs</li><li>Develop event-based solutions using Azure Event Grid and Azure Event Hubs</li><li>Develop message-based solutions using Azure Service Bus and Azure Queue Storage</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C711' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CAS-005</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Governance, Risk, and Compliance (20%)</h3><ul><li>Implement governance components (security program documentation, GRC tools, change/configuration management, data governance)</li><li>Perform risk management activities (risk assessment frameworks, third-party/supply chain risk, confidentiality/integrity/availability/privacy risk considerations)</li><li>Explain how compliance affects security strategy (industry standards e.g. PCI DSS, ISO/IEC 27000, NIST CSF; privacy regulations e.g. GDPR/CCPA; audits vs assessments vs certifications)</li><li>Perform threat-modeling activities (actor characteristics, ATT&CK/CAPEC/STRIDE/Cyber Kill Chain frameworks, attack surface determination)</li><li>Summarize information security challenges of AI adoption (prompt injection, model theft/inversion, AI-enabled attacks, AI-enabled assistants/digital workers)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Security Architecture (27%)</h3><ul><li>Analyze requirements to design resilient systems (component placement, availability/integrity design, recoverability, scaling)</li><li>Implement security throughout the systems life cycle (security requirements, SAST/DAST/IAST/RASP, SCA, SBOM, CI/CD, supply chain and hardware assurance)</li><li>Integrate appropriate controls into secure architecture design (attack surface management, detection/threat-hunting enablers, DLP, hybrid infrastructures)</li><li>Apply security concepts to access, authentication, and authorization system design (provisioning/deprovisioning, federation, SSO, PKI, access control models)</li><li>Securely implement cloud capabilities in an enterprise environment (CASB, shared responsibility model, IaC via Terraform/Ansible, container/serverless security)</li><li>Integrate Zero Trust concepts into system architecture design (continuous authorization, microsegmentation, deperimeterization via SASE/SD-WAN)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Security Engineering (31%)</h3><ul><li>Troubleshoot IAM components in an enterprise environment (subject access control, MFA, PAM, federation protocols SAML/OAuth/OpenID)</li><li>Analyze requirements to enhance endpoint and server security (EDR, HIPS/HIDS, application control, MDM, threat-actor TTPs)</li><li>Troubleshoot complex network infrastructure security issues (DNS security, email security DKIM/SPF/DMARC, TLS/PKI issues, DDoS, ACL issues)</li><li>Implement hardware security technologies and techniques (roots of trust, TPM/HSM, secure boot, tamper detection, firmware attacks)</li><li>Secure specialized and legacy systems against threats (OT/SCADA/ICS, IoT, embedded systems, industry-specific challenges)</li><li>Use automation to secure the enterprise (scripting, IaC, SOAR, generative AI, SCAP/CVE/CVSS) and apply advanced cryptographic concepts and use cases (post-quantum cryptography, homomorphic encryption, tokenization, digital signatures)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Security Operations (22%)</h3><ul><li>Analyze data to enable monitoring and response activities (SIEM, aggregate data analysis, behavior baselines, reporting/dashboards)</li><li>Analyze vulnerabilities and attacks to recommend mitigations reducing the attack surface (injection, XSS, deserialization, input validation, patching)</li><li>Apply threat-hunting and threat intelligence concepts (OSINT, TIPs, STIX/TAXII, Sigma/YARA rule languages, indicators of attack)</li><li>Analyze data and artifacts in support of incident response activities (malware analysis, reverse engineering, network/host/metadata analysis, root cause analysis, insider threat)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C718' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Professional</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Designing and planning a cloud solution architecture (25%)</h3><ul><li>Design cloud infrastructure meeting business requirements: use cases/product strategy, functional & non-functional requirements, business continuity, cost optimization, workload disposition (build/buy/modify/deprecate), KPIs/ROI, security & compliance, observability</li><li>Design cloud infrastructure meeting technical requirements: Well-Architected Framework alignment, HA/fail-over design, resource flexibility, scalability, performance/latency, Gemini Cloud Assist, backup & recovery</li><li>Design network, storage, and compute resources: on-prem/multicloud integration, Google Cloud AI/ML solutions (Gemini LLMs, Agent Builder, Model Garden, AI Hypercomputer), cloud-native networking (VPC, peering, firewalls, load balancers, shared VPC, Private Service Connect), data processing/storage type selection, mapping compute needs to platform products (GKE, Cloud Run), choosing compute resources (spot VMs, custom machine types)</li><li>Create a migration plan: integrating with existing systems, assessing/migrating systems & data (Google Cloud Migration Center), migration methodologies/workload testing/network & dependency planning, software license & financial impact</li><li>Envision future solution improvements: cloud/technology evolution, evolving business needs, cloud-first design approach</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Managing and provisioning a cloud solution infrastructure (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure network topologies: hybrid and multicloud extension, security protection (intrusion protection, access control, firewalls), VPC design and load balancing</li><li>Configure individual storage systems: data storage allocation, processing/compute provisioning, security/access management, data transfer & latency, retention/lifecycle management, data growth planning, backup & recovery</li><li>Configure compute systems: resource provisioning, compute volatility (spot vs standard), cloud-native network config for compute (Compute Engine, GKE, serverless, VMware Engine), infrastructure orchestration & patch management, container orchestration, serverless computing</li><li>Leverage Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform for end-to-end ML workflows: Agent Platform Pipelines, data integration, AI Hypercomputer usage (GPUs/TPUs, large-scale model training)</li><li>Configure prebuilt solutions or APIs with Agent Platform: Google AI APIs (Search, Conversation, Vision, Image, Video, Audio), Gemini Enterprise features (AI Agents, NotebookLM), integrating Model Garden models</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Designing for security and compliance (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Design for security: IAM, resource hierarchy (orgs/folders/projects), data security (key management, encryption, secret management), separation of duties</li><li>Security controls: auditing, VPC Service Controls, context-aware access, organization policy, hierarchical firewall policy, Cloud KMS customer-managed keys</li><li>Secure remote access: Identity-Aware Proxy, service account impersonation, Chrome Enterprise Premium, Workload Identity Federation; securing the software supply chain and securing AI (Model Armor, Sensitive Data Protection, secure model deployment)</li><li>Design for compliance: legislation/regulation (health, children''s, data privacy, sovereignty), commercial sensitive data (PCI, PII), industry certifications (e.g., SOC 2), audits and logs</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Analyzing and optimizing technical and business processes (15%)</h3><ul><li>Analyze and define technical processes: SDLC, CI/CD, troubleshooting/root cause analysis, testing & validation of software/infrastructure, service catalog & provisioning, disaster recovery</li><li>Analyze and define business processes: stakeholder management (influencing/facilitation), change management, team assessment/skills readiness, decision-making processes, customer success management, cost/resource optimization (CapEx/OpEx), business continuity</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section 5: Managing implementation (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Advise development and operations teams on deployment: application & infrastructure deployment, API management best practices (Apigee), testing frameworks (load/unit/integration), data & system migration/management tooling, Gemini Cloud Assist</li><li>Interact with Google Cloud programmatically: Cloud Shell Editor/Code/Terminal, Google Cloud SDKs (gcloud, gsutil, bq), cloud emulators (Bigtable, Spanner, Pub/Sub, Firestore), Infrastructure as Code (Terraform), Google API best practices and client libraries</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Section 6: Ensuring solution and operations excellence (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Understand and apply the operational excellence pillar of the Google Cloud Well-Architected Framework</li><li>Google Cloud Observability: monitoring and logging, profiling and benchmarking, alerting strategies</li><li>Deployment and release management</li><li>Assist with support of deployed solutions and evaluate quality control measures</li><li>Ensure reliability of solutions in production: chaos engineering, penetration testing, load testing</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C740' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-104</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Manage Azure identities and governance (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage Microsoft Entra users and groups, including licenses and self-service password reset (SSPR)</li><li>Manage external (guest) users</li><li>Manage built-in Azure roles and assign RBAC roles at different scopes</li><li>Implement and manage Azure Policy, resource locks, and tags</li><li>Manage resource groups, subscriptions, and management groups</li><li>Manage costs using alerts, budgets, and Azure Advisor recommendations</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement and manage storage (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure storage account access: firewalls/VNets, SAS tokens, stored access policies, access keys, identity-based access for Azure Files</li><li>Create and configure storage accounts, redundancy, object replication, and encryption</li><li>Manage data with Azure Storage Explorer and AzCopy</li><li>Create and configure Azure Files shares and Blob Storage containers</li><li>Configure storage tiers, soft delete, snapshots, blob lifecycle management, and blob versioning</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Deploy and manage Azure compute resources (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Interpret, modify, and deploy resources using ARM templates or Bicep files</li><li>Create and configure virtual machines, including encryption at host, VM sizes, disks, availability zones/sets, and Scale Sets</li><li>Provision and manage containers via Azure Container Registry, Container Instances, and Container Apps</li><li>Create and configure Azure App Service, including plans, scaling, custom domains/TLS, backup, networking, and deployment slots</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Implement and manage virtual networking (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure virtual networks, subnets, peering, public IPs, and user-defined routes; troubleshoot connectivity</li><li>Configure network security groups (NSGs) and application security groups; evaluate effective security rules</li><li>Implement Azure Bastion and configure service/private endpoints for Azure PaaS</li><li>Configure Azure DNS, internal/public load balancers, and troubleshoot load balancing</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Monitor and maintain Azure resources (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Interpret metrics, configure log settings, and query/analyze logs in Azure Monitor</li><li>Set up alert rules, action groups, and alert processing rules</li><li>Use Azure Monitor Insights and Network Watcher/Connection Monitor</li><li>Create Recovery Services and Backup vaults; configure backup policies and perform backup/restore</li><li>Configure Azure Site Recovery, perform failover, and interpret backup reports/alerts</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C756' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>No</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Parts, assembly modeling, management (27%)</h3><ul><li>Manage sheet metal design &mdash; create/edit parts using face, flange, contour flange, bend tools; use sheet metal defaults window</li><li>Use and determine appropriate pattern tools &mdash; rectangular, circular, feature-based; mirror and copy components/features (incl. Content Center reuse)</li><li>Modify parts and assembly models parametrically &mdash; edit via parameters table, update/validate drawings after parameter changes, link parameters across parts/assemblies or from Excel, export parameters to iParts</li><li>Insert and position components in an assembly &mdash; place parts/Content Center parts/iParts, replace components/sub-assemblies, constrain per design intent</li><li>Create weldment assemblies &mdash; apply welds, perform weld prep, perform machining operations within a weldment</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Drawing, documentation, visualization (14%)</h3><ul><li>Place and manage drawing views &mdash; override dimension styles (Reference/Critical/Tolerance), create required views, show assemblies retracted/extended, create Snapshot views via IPN files</li><li>Validate drawings &mdash; confirm drawing reflects model after updates, recall when a model vs. drawing annotation edit is needed, reflect iProperty updates on drawings</li><li>Annotate drawings &mdash; edit geometric tolerances, place symbols (feature control frames, surface finish, etc.), manage BOM in an assembly</li><li>Use View and Inspect tabs for parts/assemblies &mdash; activate/modify section views, save view representations, run surface analysis (zebra, curvature, section), obtain interference between components</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Administrative, metadata (17%)</h3><ul><li>Recognize project file function &mdash; file/library paths for design projects, templates, libraries, Content Center, single-user project setup</li><li>Share company standards &mdash; material libraries, sheet metal/drawing styles, import a customized ApplicationOptions.xml, determine active sheet metal style defaults</li><li>Manage iProperties &mdash; create/use custom iProperties, manage drawing properties</li><li>Share files &mdash; use Pack and Go to share an assembly, export to secondary formats (PDF, DXF, STP, STL), understand parent/child file relationships</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Modeling strategies, approaches (42%)</h3><ul><li>Utilize appropriate modeling strategies &mdash; design strategy for complex repeating geometry, capture design intent, build robust parametric models, choose reference planes/sketch profiles, explain Derive style types</li><li>Utilize appropriate model editing strategies &mdash; edit parametric values, use user-placed workplanes/axes/points, analyze interference at nominal/max/min tolerance</li><li>Import secondary file formats &mdash; identify imported geometry needing repair, understand 2D DXF import use cases</li><li>Recognize browser bar functionality &mdash; promote/demote, End of Part/Assembly, consumed work features, share sketch, rearrange feature order</li><li>Use and leverage model states &mdash; activate/edit/export model states for parts, change placed model states/derived parts/iParts/iAssemblies in assemblies, edit factory vs. member scope</li><li>Demonstrate knowledge of adaptivity, component relationships, and flexibility between features and sketches</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C774' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PK0-005</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 1.0 Project Management Concepts (33%)</h3><ul><li>Project characteristics and methodologies/frameworks (Agile/Scrum, Kanban, Waterfall, PRINCE2, SDLC)</li><li>Compare and contrast Agile vs. Waterfall approaches</li><li>Apply the change control process (change control board, change log, scope creep management)</li><li>Perform risk management activities (risk identification, qualitative/quantitative analysis, risk responses)</li><li>Perform issue management activities and schedule development/management (critical path, dependencies, resource loading)</li><li>Quality/performance management, communication management, meeting management, team & resource management, and procurement/vendor selection concepts</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 2.0 Project Life Cycle Phases (30%)</h3><ul><li>Discovery/concept preparation phase artifacts (business case, ROI analysis, CapEx vs. OpEx)</li><li>Project initiation phase activities (project charter, stakeholder identification, RACI/responsibility assignment matrix)</li><li>Project planning phase activities (scope statement, WBS, project schedule, communication plan, QA plan, initial risk assessment)</li><li>Project execution phase activities (executing tasks per plan, organizational change management, vendor management, tracking/reporting, conflict management)</li><li>Project closing phase activities (deliverable validation, contract closure, closeout report, lessons learned, project sign-off)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 3.0 Tools and Documentation (19%)</h3><ul><li>Tracking charts and tools (Gantt chart, PERT chart, milestone chart, project network diagram, risk register, issue/defect/change logs)</li><li>Project management productivity tools: communication, collaboration, meeting, documentation/office production, scheduling tools</li><li>Analyze quality and performance charts (histograms, Pareto charts, run charts, scatter diagrams, fishbone/Ishikawa diagrams, control charts, burnup/burndown, velocity chart, decision tree)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 4.0 Basics of IT and Governance (18%)</h3><ul><li>Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) factors related to project management</li><li>Information security concepts impacting project management (physical, operational, digital, and data security)</li><li>Compliance and privacy considerations (PII/PHI, legal/regulatory impacts, industry-specific compliance)</li><li>Basic IT concepts (infrastructure, cloud models &mdash; IaaS/PaaS/SaaS/XaaS, enterprise software systems)</li><li>Operational change-control processes during an IT project (IT infrastructure and software change control, CI/CD, production vs. staging environments)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C790' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-307</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 AI Problem Definition</h3><ul><li>Identify the problem to solve using AI (need, inputs/outputs, whether AI is warranted, measurable success)</li><li>Classify the problem type (e.g., classification, regression, unsupervised, reinforcement) based on available data</li><li>Identify areas of expertise needed (business, domain, AI, implementation)</li><li>Build a security plan (access levels, infrastructure security, attack-surface/risk assessment)</li><li>Ensure AI is used appropriately (guard against misprediction/harm, set data and algorithm-selection guidelines)</li><li>Choose transparency and validation activities (communicate data-collection purpose, review legal/industry requirements)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Data Collection, Processing, and Engineering</h3><ul><li>Choose data collection methods and determine whether an existing dataset can be used or a new one must be generated</li><li>Assess data quality and ensure data are representative (check for missing/corrupt data and bias)</li><li>Identify resource requirements (compute, time complexity, budget)</li><li>Convert data into suitable formats and select/engineer features for the AI model</li><li>Identify training and test datasets</li><li>Document data decisions for transparency to regulators and end users</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 AI Algorithms and Models</h3><ul><li>Evaluate applicability of specific algorithm families (e.g., neural network, decision tree, k-means) to the problem</li><li>Train and tune a model, gathering performance metrics and iterating</li><li>Select a specific model after experimentation while avoiding overengineering, considering cost/speed/explainability</li><li>Evaluate model performance (accuracy, precision, overfitting/underfitting, cross-validation) and sensitivity/specificity</li><li>Look for potential sources of bias in the algorithm and training data</li><li>Confirm regulatory adherence and obtain stakeholder approval</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Application Integration and Deployment</h3><ul><li>Train customers on product use, limitations, and expectations; share documentation</li><li>Plan to address potential challenges of models in production</li><li>Design a production pipeline (training/prediction) and integrate the AI with the application</li><li>Test accuracy, robustness, and speed of the AI through the application</li><li>Support the AI solution (maintenance documentation, support team, feedback mechanism, drift detector)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Maintaining and Monitoring AI in Production</h3><ul><li>Engage in oversight: log performance, monitor systems, act on alerts, watch for drift/degraded operation</li><li>Assess business impact via key performance indicators, comparing pre/post-change metrics</li><li>Measure impacts on individuals and communities; identify and mitigate subgroup issues</li><li>Handle user feedback (satisfaction, confusion) and incorporate it into future versions</li><li>Decide on a regular basis whether to retrain, continue using as-is, or decommission the AI</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C798' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-204</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Develop Azure compute solutions (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage container images; publish to Azure Container Registry; run containers via Azure Container Instances and Azure Container Apps</li><li>Create an Azure App Service Web App and configure diagnostics/logging, TLS, API settings, and service connections</li><li>Deploy code and containerized solutions to App Service; implement autoscaling and configure deployment slots</li><li>Create and configure an Azure Functions app</li><li>Implement Azure Functions input/output bindings</li><li>Implement Azure Functions triggers via data operations, timers, and webhooks</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Develop for Azure storage (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Perform operations on Azure Cosmos DB containers and items using the SDK</li><li>Set the appropriate consistency level for Cosmos DB operations</li><li>Implement Cosmos DB change feed notifications</li><li>Set and retrieve Azure Blob Storage properties and metadata</li><li>Perform data operations on Blob Storage using the appropriate SDK</li><li>Implement Blob Storage lifecycle management and storage policies</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement Azure security (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Authenticate and authorize users via the Microsoft Identity platform and Microsoft Entra ID</li><li>Create and implement shared access signatures (SAS)</li><li>Implement solutions that interact with Microsoft Graph</li><li>Secure app configuration data using Azure App Configuration or Azure Key Vault</li><li>Develop code that uses keys, secrets, and certificates stored in Azure Key Vault</li><li>Implement Managed Identities for Azure resources</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Monitor and troubleshoot Azure solutions (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor and analyze metrics, logs, and traces using Azure Monitor Application Insights</li><li>Implement availability tests and alerts</li><li>Instrument an app or service to use Application Insights</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Connect to and consume Azure services and third-party services (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create an Azure API Management instance</li><li>Create and document APIs; configure access to APIs; implement policies for APIs</li><li>Implement event-based solutions using Azure Event Grid</li><li>Implement event-based solutions using Azure Event Hubs</li><li>Implement message-based solutions using Azure Service Bus</li><li>Implement message-based solutions using Azure Queue Storage</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C799' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CKAD</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Application Design and Build (20%)</h3><ul><li>Define, build and modify container images</li><li>Choose and structure the appropriate Pod design (multi-container patterns: sidecar, init, ambassador, adapter)</li><li>Utilize persistent and ephemeral volumes</li><li>Understand multi-container Pod design patterns (e.g. sidecar, init and others)</li><li>Utilize Jobs and CronJobs</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Application Deployment (20%)</h3><ul><li>Use Kubernetes primitives to implement common deployment strategies (e.g. blue/green or canary)</li><li>Understand Deployments and how to perform rolling updates</li><li>Use the Helm package manager to deploy existing packages</li><li>Kustomize</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Application Observability and Maintenance (15%)</h3><ul><li>Understand API deprecations</li><li>Implement probes and health checks (liveness, readiness, startup)</li><li>Use built-in CLI tools to monitor Kubernetes applications</li><li>Utilize container logs</li><li>Debugging in Kubernetes</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Application Environment, Configuration and Security (25%)</h3><ul><li>Discover and use resources that extend Kubernetes (CRD, Operators)</li><li>Understand authentication, authorization and admission control</li><li>Understand requests, limits, quotas</li><li>Understand ConfigMaps</li><li>Define resource requirements</li><li>Create & consume Secrets</li><li>Understand ServiceAccounts</li><li>Understand Application Security (SecurityContexts, Capabilities, etc.)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Services and Networking (20%)</h3><ul><li>Demonstrate basic understanding of NetworkPolicies</li><li>Provide and troubleshoot access to applications via services</li><li>Use Ingress rules to expose applications</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C810' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-101</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Networking Fundamentals</h3><ul><li>Define network concepts: Internet, intranet, extranet, client-server, peer-to-peer</li><li>Define transmission types: unicast, multicast, broadcast; network devices including IoT</li><li>Define cloud and virtualization concepts: hypervisors, virtual machines, virtual switches</li><li>Describe remote access methods: VPN, Remote Desktop</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Network Infrastructures</h3><ul><li>Define LAN characteristics: perimeter networks/DMZ, VLANs, wired vs wireless LAN</li><li>Define WAN characteristics: DSL, site-to-site, cable modem, satellite, cellular (3G/4G/5G)</li><li>Identify wireless networking methods: 802.11, Bluetooth, WPA/WPA2/WEP/802.1X, ad hoc, wireless bridging, interference</li><li>Compare and contrast network topologies and access methods: star, mesh, ring, bus, logical vs physical</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Network Hardware</h3><ul><li>Describe switch characteristics: managed/unmanaged, VLAN capability, Layer 2/3 switching, MAC table, spanning tree protocol</li><li>Describe router characteristics: static/dynamic routing, routing tables, port forwarding, QoS, network segmentation, convergence</li><li>Describe physical media characteristics: fiber optic, twisted pair (CAT5-CAT7), crossover vs straight-through, EMI/cross-talk susceptibility</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Protocols and Services</h3><ul><li>Describe the OSI model: layer purpose, associated devices/protocols/applications, MAC address</li><li>Describe the TCP/IP model: layer purpose, associated devices/protocols/applications</li><li>Describe IPv4 concepts: classful vs classless addressing, subnetting, subnet mask, private address classes</li><li>Describe IPv6 concepts: addressing, IPv4-to-IPv6 transition (tunneling, dual stack), link-local vs global, multicast</li><li>Identify well-known ports and protocols: HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP, IMAP, DNS, RDP, SSH</li><li>Describe name resolution and networking services: DNS/WINS, DNS record types, DHCP, NAT, firewalls</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Troubleshooting</h3><ul><li>Describe the troubleshooting process in a small-medium business network, including professional conduct</li><li>Use appropriate hardware troubleshooting tools: multimeter, cable tester, toner, TDR/OTDR</li><li>Use Windows software tools: ping, ipconfig, tracert, pathping, nslookup, hostname, netstat, arp</li><li>Use Linux software tools: ping, ip addr, traceroute, tracepath, dig, host, netstat, arp</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C815' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AI-300</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Design and implement an MLOps infrastructure (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage a Machine Learning workspace, datastores, and compute targets</li><li>Configure identity and access management (IAM) for workspaces</li><li>Create and manage data assets, environments, and components; share assets across workspaces via registries</li><li>Deploy Machine Learning workspaces and resources by using Bicep and Azure CLI</li><li>Automate resource provisioning with GitHub Actions workflows and restrict network access</li><li>Manage source control for machine learning projects using Git</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement machine learning model lifecycle and operations (27.5%)</h3><ul><li>Configure experiment tracking with MLflow; use automated ML and notebooks for training/exploration</li><li>Automate hyperparameter tuning and run model training scripts as jobs</li><li>Implement training pipelines and manage distributed training for large/deep learning models</li><li>Register MLflow models, package feature-retrieval specs, and evaluate models using responsible AI principles</li><li>Deploy models as real-time or batch endpoints with managed inference; implement progressive rollout/safe rollback</li><li>Monitor production models for data drift and performance, and configure retraining/alert triggers</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Design and implement a GenAIOps infrastructure (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and configure Microsoft Foundry resources and project environments</li><li>Configure identity/access management (managed identities, RBAC) and network security for Foundry</li><li>Deploy infrastructure using Bicep templates and Azure CLI</li><li>Deploy and manage foundation models via serverless API endpoints and managed compute; select appropriate models</li><li>Configure provisioned throughput units for high-volume workloads and manage model versioning/deployment strategies</li><li>Design, version, and manage prompts (variants, comparison) using Git-based source control</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Implement generative AI quality assurance and observability (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create test datasets and data mapping for comprehensive model evaluation</li><li>Implement AI quality metrics, including groundedness, relevance, coherence, and fluency</li><li>Configure risk and safety evaluations for harmful content detection</li><li>Set up automated evaluation workflows using built-in and custom metrics</li><li>Monitor performance metrics (latency, throughput, response times) and track cost/token consumption</li><li>Configure detailed logging, tracing, and debugging for production troubleshooting</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Optimize generative AI systems and model performance (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Optimize RAG retrieval performance by tuning similarity thresholds, chunk sizes, and retrieval strategies</li><li>Select and fine-tune embedding models for domain-specific use cases</li><li>Implement and optimize hybrid search combining semantic and keyword-based retrieval</li><li>Evaluate/improve RAG system performance using relevance metrics and A/B testing</li><li>Design and implement advanced fine-tuning methods, including synthetic data creation</li><li>Manage a fine-tuned model from development through production deployment</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C840' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Unity</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Debugging, problem-solving, and interpreting the API</h3><ul><li>Given an example of a debug log message, create the code that produced that log message</li><li>Given a code clip and its associated error message(s), determine which object(s) is/are null</li><li>Given a specific programming task requiring use of a particular API class, determine the appropriate method(s), properties, arguments, or other syntax to use</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Creating code</h3><ul><li>Indicate when and how to initialize and use variables, including appropriate use of variable modifiers and data collections such as Arrays, Lists, and Dictionaries</li><li>Given a list of keywords and syntax elements, construct a viable function declaration</li><li>Given a code clip and desired result, identify the appropriate function to control or trigger a state, including use of the Animator Controller</li><li>Given a scenario requiring a specific type of input, construct the necessary input listener (e.g. keyboard and touch input)</li><li>Demonstrate when and/or how to use the various logic and flow-control operators in C# and Unity</li><li>Given a scenario, identify appropriate actions to take when a UI element reports a change</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Evaluating code</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario about managing an event function, determine the appropriate action to take, including keyboard and touch input handling</li><li>Given a code clip that errors due to an incorrectly declared variable data type, identify the error</li><li>Given a code clip that errors due to incorrect function/variable declaration or use (e.g. public/private mismatch), identify the error, including use of Animation events</li><li>Given a code clip containing a class definition, distinguish whether the class is an ECS class or another class type</li><li>Given a set of code clips, recognize the one that follows Unity naming conventions</li><li>Given a code clip (or set of clips), recognize the comments that accurately describe what the code does</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Navigating the Interface</h3><ul><li>Describe the purpose, features, and functions of the various Unity IDE windows</li><li>Demonstrate how to change the default scripting IDE</li><li>Given a scenario (a portion of a gaming scenario, a set of animation clips, and a list of property settings), create a functional state machine</li><li>Create and program a function state machine within the Unity Animator Controller, including use of Animator function syntax</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C841' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CV0-004</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Cloud Architecture (23%)</h3><ul><li>Cloud service models (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS, FaaS) and the shared responsibility model</li><li>Service availability: regions/AZs, DR (RTO/RPO), hot/warm/cold sites, cloud bursting, edge computing</li><li>Cloud networking: VPN/dedicated connections, load balancers, CDN, firewalls, VPC peering/transit gateway, SDN/BGP</li><li>Storage resource types (object/block/file), tiered storage, SSD/HDD, performance and cost tradeoffs</li><li>Cloud-native design (microservices, loosely coupled architecture), containerization and virtualization concepts</li><li>Cost considerations (billing models, tagging, rightsizing), database types, and evolving tech (AI/ML, IoT)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Deployment (19%)</h3><ul><li>Cloud deployment models: public, private, hybrid, community, on-premises</li><li>Deployment strategies: blue-green, canary, rolling, in-place</li><li>Cloud migration types and application migration strategies (rehost, replatform, re-architect, retain, retire, refactor)</li><li>Infrastructure as Code / Configuration as Code, scripting logic, drift detection, versioning, JSON/YAML</li><li>Provisioning cloud resources against storage, performance, security, cost, availability, compliance, network and compute requirements</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Operations (17%)</h3><ul><li>Observability: logging, monitoring, metrics, tracing, alerting/triage</li><li>Scaling approaches: triggered (trending/load/event), scheduled, manual; horizontal vs vertical</li><li>Backup and recovery: backup types (full/incremental/differential), retention, replication, encryption, recovery options</li><li>Cloud resource lifecycle management: patching, updates, testing, ephemeral vs persistent data, decommissioning (EOL/EOS)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Security (19%)</h3><ul><li>Vulnerability management: scanning, identification, assessment, remediation, CVEs</li><li>Compliance and regulation: data sovereignty/ownership/locality/classification/retention, SOC2, PCI DSS, ISO 27001, CSA</li><li>Identity and access management: authentication (MFA, federation/SAML, OIDC), authorization (RBAC, OAuth 2.0), accounting/audit trails</li><li>Security best practices: Zero Trust, hardening, encryption (in transit/at rest), least privilege, container/API security, secrets management</li><li>Security controls: DLP, IPS/IDS, DDoS protection, WAF, network ACLs/security groups</li><li>Monitoring for suspicious activity: baseline deviation, phishing/social engineering, malware/ransomware, DDoS, cryptojacking</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 DevOps Fundamentals (10%)</h3><ul><li>Source control concepts: version management, code commit/push/merge, pull requests, branch management, code review</li><li>CI/CD pipeline concepts: build automation, code integration/deployment, testing, artifacts, image/package repositories</li><li>Container image workflows and package formats (RPM, Debian, tar, ZIP)</li><li>Automation and orchestration of code deployment and infrastructure workflows</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Troubleshooting (12%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot common cloud connectivity and networking issues</li><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot common security-related issues in the cloud environment</li><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot common deployment issues</li><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot common performance and capacity issues</li><li>Apply a general troubleshooting methodology (identify, establish theory, test, implement, document)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C855' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>MS-700</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Configure and manage a Teams environment (42.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan network settings for Teams (bandwidth capacity, Network planner, ports/protocols, Teams Network Assessment Tool)</li><li>Manage security and compliance settings (licensing, alert policies, admin roles, Defender for Office 365 threat policies, retention, sensitivity labels, Purview DLP/Information Barriers/Communication Compliance, Entra Conditional Access)</li><li>Plan and implement governance (Teams lifecycle management, content storage, update policies, policy packages/assignment, Microsoft 365 group creation/expiration/naming policies, archive/delete/restore teams, PowerShell/Graph operations)</li><li>Configure and manage external collaboration (external sharing settings, guest access, shared channels, B2B direct connect, multitenant organization)</li><li>Manage Teams clients and devices (Teams Phone/device licensing, device configuration profiles, Teams Rooms, device tags, remote provisioning, VDI)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Manage teams, channels, chats, and apps (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage teams (Advisor for Teams rollout, creation via admin center/client/PowerShell/Graph, templates, membership/roles, privacy/sensitivity settings, frontline teams)</li><li>Manage channels and chats (channel types, channel settings, creation/sharing policies, private/shared channel membership, messaging policies)</li><li>Manage apps for Teams (org-wide app settings, app assignment/setup policies, permissions and consent, app store customization and purchasing, uploading apps)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Manage meetings and calling (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage meetings and events (meeting types incl. webinars/town halls, meeting settings incl. Copilot, meeting/event templates and policies, town hall and webinar configuration)</li><li>Manage phone numbers and services for Teams Phone (provisioning and assigning phone numbers, voice settings/policies, voicemail policies, auto-attendants and call queues, calling policies)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Monitor, report on, and troubleshoot Teams (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Monitor and report on Teams (voice/meeting quality, alert rules, usage reporting, team creation/deletion, guest access, network connectivity test tool, feedback policies)</li><li>Troubleshoot audio, video, and client issues (client-side logs, cache clearing, self-help diagnostics, client installation/update issues, sign-in issues, Copilot/AI troubleshooting, meeting join issues)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C864' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>Professional</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section 1: Configuring access (25%)</h3><ul><li>Manage Cloud Identity: SSO with third-party IdP via Google Cloud Directory Sync, super admin account, user lifecycle automation, Workforce Identity Federation</li><li>Manage service accounts: securing keys, short-lived credentials, Workload Identity Federation, service account impersonation</li><li>Manage authentication: password/session policy, SAML/OAuth setup, 2-step verification</li><li>Manage authorization controls: IAM roles/permissions, ACLs, IAM conditions and deny policies, least privilege, Access Context Manager, Policy Intelligence, Privileged Access Manager</li><li>Define the resource hierarchy: folders/projects at scale, organization policies, access-control inheritance</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section 2: Securing communications and establishing boundary protection (22%)</h3><ul><li>Design and configure perimeter security: Cloud NGFW rules/policies, Identity-Aware Proxy, load balancers, Certificate Authority Service, Cloud Armor WAF, Secure Web Proxy, Cloud DNS security</li><li>Configure boundary segmentation: VPC security properties, VPC peering, Shared VPC, firewall rules, VPC Service Controls</li><li>Establish private connectivity: private connectivity between VPCs/projects, HA VPN/Cloud Interconnect, Private Google Access, Private Service Connect, Cloud NAT</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section 3: Ensuring data protection (23%)</h3><ul><li>Protect sensitive data and prevent data loss: Sensitive Data Protection (DLP), restricting access to BigQuery/Cloud Storage/Cloud SQL, Secret Manager, compute instance metadata protection</li><li>Manage encryption at rest, in transit, and in use: default encryption vs CMEK vs Cloud EKM, software/hardware keys, key rotation/revocation, object lifecycle policies, Confidential Computing</li><li>Secure AI workloads: security/privacy controls for AI/ML systems, IaaS/PaaS-hosted training model security, Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform security controls</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section 4: Managing operations (19%)</h3><ul><li>Automate infrastructure and application security: CVE scanning in CI/CD, Binary Authorization for GKE/Cloud Run, VM/container image hardening automation, policy and drift detection at scale (CSPM)</li><li>Configure logging, monitoring, and detection: network logs (Cloud NGFW, VPC flow logs, Packet Mirroring, Cloud IDS, Log Analytics), logging strategy design, incident response/remediation, secure log access, log export to external SIEMs, Cloud Audit Logs, Security Command Center monitoring</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section 5: Supporting compliance requirements (11%)</h3><ul><li>Determine technical needs across compute, data, network, and storage for regulatory compliance</li><li>Evaluate the shared responsibility model</li><li>Configure security controls for compliance: Assured Workloads, organizational policies, Access Transparency, Access Approval, data regionalization</li><li>Determine the Google Cloud environment in scope for regulatory compliance</li><li>Map compliance requirements to Google Cloud services and security controls (network/access segmentation, audit log coverage)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C876' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AZ-500</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Secure identity and access (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Manage Azure built-in role assignments and custom roles (Azure roles and Microsoft Entra roles)</li><li>Plan and manage Azure resources in Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management (PIM), settings and assignments</li><li>Implement multi-factor authentication (MFA) and Conditional Access policies for Azure resources</li><li>Manage access to enterprise applications in Microsoft Entra ID, including OAuth permission grants</li><li>Manage Microsoft Entra app registrations, permission scopes, and permission consent</li><li>Manage and use service principals and managed identities</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Secure networking (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement Network Security Groups (NSGs), Application Security Groups (ASGs), and user-defined routes (UDRs)</li><li>Plan and implement Virtual Network peering, VPN gateway, Virtual WAN (secured virtual hub), and encryption over ExpressRoute</li><li>Plan and implement private access to Azure resources: Service Endpoints, Private Endpoints, Private Link services</li><li>Plan and implement network security for App Service/Functions, App Service Environment, and Azure SQL Managed Instance</li><li>Plan, implement, and manage Azure Firewall, Firewall Manager, Application Gateway, Front Door/CDN, and Web Application Firewall (WAF)</li><li>Configure TLS for applications, monitor with Network Watcher, and recommend Azure DDoS Protection Standard</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Secure compute, storage, and databases (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan and implement remote VM access via Azure Bastion and just-in-time (JIT) VM access</li><li>Configure network isolation, authentication, and security monitoring for AKS, Azure Container Instances, Azure Container Apps, and Azure Container Registry</li><li>Configure disk encryption (Azure Disk Encryption, encryption at host, confidential disk encryption) and API Management security</li><li>Configure storage account access control, access keys, secure access to Azure Files/Blob Storage, BYOK, and double encryption at infrastructure level</li><li>Enable Microsoft Entra database authentication, database auditing, dynamic data masking, and Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) for Azure SQL</li><li>Protect against data security threats using soft delete, backups, versioning, and immutable storage</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Secure Azure using Microsoft Defender for Cloud and Microsoft Sentinel (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create, assign, and interpret Azure Policy policies/initiatives; configure Key Vault network settings, access, and manage certificates/secrets/keys with rotation and backup/recovery</li><li>Identify and remediate security risks using Defender for Cloud Secure Score/Inventory; assess and manage compliance standards, including custom standards</li><li>Connect hybrid/multi-cloud environments (AWS, GCP) to Microsoft Defender for Cloud; implement Microsoft Defender External Attack Surface Management (EASM)</li><li>Enable cloud workload protection plans (Defender for Servers, Databases, Storage), agentless scanning, and Defender Vulnerability Management for VMs</li><li>Connect and configure Defender for Cloud DevOps Security (GitHub, Azure DevOps, GitLab)</li><li>Manage and respond to security alerts, configure workflow automation, data collection rules (DCRs), and in Microsoft Sentinel configure data connectors, analytics rules, and automation</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C893' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CLSSBB-001</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Section I &ndash; Organizational Roadblocks & Lean Management</h3><ul><li>Identify organizational roadblocks and resistance to change</li><li>Understand continuous improvement approaches (overview)</li><li>Apply Lean and Six Sigma fundamentals</li><li>Use Lean management metrics: Takt Time, Cycle Time, PCE, Lead Time, SWIP, Setup/Changeover time</li><li>Apply Lean tools: 5S, Kaizen, SMED, Heijunka</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Section II &ndash; Pre-Define and Define Phase</h3><ul><li>Compare DMAIC versus DFSS approaches</li><li>Assess pre-define prerequisites and project prioritization (NPV, IRR, enterprise vs. line-of-business view)</li><li>Develop project charters and manage team dynamics</li><li>Build SIPOC/COPIS process maps</li><li>Capture Voice of Customer/Business/Process and define CTQ, CTC, CTS</li><li>Apply the Kano Model and Quality Function Deployment; establish baseline performance metrics and Rolled Throughput Yield</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Section III &ndash; Measure Phase</h3><ul><li>Identify data types and distributions (Normal, Binomial, Poisson, Weibull)</li><li>Perform Measurement Systems Analysis and GAGE R&R</li><li>Calculate process capability indices (Cp, Cpk, Cpkm)</li><li>Conduct normality testing</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Section IV &ndash; Analyze Phase</h3><ul><li>Perform regression analysis (simple, multiple, curvilinear)</li><li>Use Fishbone diagrams and Pareto charts for root-cause analysis</li><li>Conduct hypothesis testing (parametric and non-parametric methods)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Section V &ndash; Improve Phase</h3><ul><li>Perform cost-benefit analysis</li><li>Design and analyze experiments (DOE, factorial designs)</li><li>Prioritize improvement solutions using decision matrices</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Section VI &ndash; Control Phase</h3><ul><li>Apply Taguchi''s Loss Function</li><li>Build and interpret control charts (variable and attribute)</li><li>Develop control plans and execute project closure</li><li>Introduce Total Productive Maintenance</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C913' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>PL-400</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Create a technical design (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Analyze technical architecture to identify solution components and implementation approach</li><li>Design authentication and authorization strategy for solution components</li><li>Determine whether requirements can be met with out-of-the-box functionality</li><li>Determine where to implement business logic (cloud computing, client-side, business rules, plug-ins, Power Automate)</li><li>Determine when to use standard, virtual, or elastic tables vs. connectors</li><li>Assess impact of Power Platform security features (DLP, security roles, teams, business units, row sharing) and design reusable components, custom connectors, Dataverse code components, automations, and integrations</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Build Power Platform solutions (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Troubleshoot operational security issues</li><li>Configure Dataverse security roles to support code components (least privilege)</li><li>Manage Power Platform environments for development</li><li>Manage solution dependencies and solution layers</li><li>Create and use environment variables</li><li>Implement/extend Power Platform Pipelines and CI/CD automations using Power Platform Build Tools</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement Power Apps improvements (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Implement complex Power Fx formulas and functions</li><li>Build reusable component libraries</li><li>Utilize Power Automate cloud flows to implement business logic from a canvas app</li><li>Troubleshoot canvas and model-driven app issues using Monitor and browser-based debugging tools</li><li>Optimize canvas app performance (pre-loading data, query delegation)</li><li>Optimize model-driven app performance (forms and views)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Extend the user experience (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Build JavaScript code targeting the Client API object model and determine event handler registration approach</li><li>Create client scripting that targets the Dataverse Web API</li><li>Configure commands and buttons using Power Fx and JavaScript; implement navigation to custom pages</li><li>Demonstrate use of PCF component lifecycle events and configure a component manifest</li><li>Implement component interfaces and package/deploy/consume a PCF component</li><li>Configure and use Device, Utility, and Web API features in PCF component logic</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Extend the platform (32.5%)</h3><ul><li>Create a Dataverse plug-in: execution pipeline stages, execution context, Pre/Post Images, Organization service operations, custom API messages, Plug-in Registration Tool, business events</li><li>Create custom connectors: Open API definitions, authentication, policy templates, Azure Function integration, data transformation</li><li>Use platform APIs: Dataverse Web API, Organization service, API limit retry policies, OAuth authentication, performance/concurrency/bulk operations</li><li>Process workloads with Azure Functions: long-running operations, scheduled/event-driven triggers, managed identity authentication</li><li>Configure Power Automate cloud flows: Dataverse connector actions/triggers, complex expressions, Azure Key Vault, error handling, trigger filters/retry policies, child flows, Entra ID service principals</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Develop integrations (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Publish a Dataverse event using IServiceEndpointNotificationService or the Plug-in Registration Tool</li><li>Register service endpoints including webhooks, Azure Service Bus, and Azure Event Hub</li><li>Recommend options for listening to Dataverse events</li><li>Perform data synchronization using change tracking</li><li>Develop code that utilizes alternate keys</li><li>Utilize the UpsertRequest message to synchronize data</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C915' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>CS0-004</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Security Operations (34%)</h3><ul><li>Explain system and network architecture concepts in security operations (architecture components, identity, logging: ingestion, time sync, retention, integrity)</li><li>Analyze indicators of potential malicious activity across network, endpoint, cloud, and identity layers</li><li>Use tools to determine malicious activity (SIEM query writing, EDR/XDR, packet analysis with Wireshark/tcpdump/Suricata/Zeek, artifact analysis with YARA/CyberChef/VirusTotal)</li><li>Explain threat intelligence and threat-hunting concepts, frameworks, and data sources</li><li>Describe efficiency and process improvement in security operations (automation, workflows)</li><li>Summarize concepts related to the use of AI in security operations (use cases, risks such as hallucination/data exposure/prompt injection, and governance)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Vulnerability Management (26%)</h3><ul><li>Implement the appropriate vulnerability scanning method (credentialed/non-credentialed, agent-based/agentless, asset inventory and scan planning)</li><li>Analyze output from vulnerability assessment tools (deduplication, false positive handling)</li><li>Prioritize and mitigate vulnerabilities using risk-based scoring (CVSS in business context) and threat intelligence</li><li>Explain concepts related to control types, risks, and vulnerability management (compliance-driven scanning such as PCI DSS/CIS/ISO 27000, exception tracking, compensating controls)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Incident Response and Management (24%)</h3><ul><li>Summarize concepts related to attack methodology frameworks (MITRE ATT&CK, Cyber Kill Chain, Diamond Model)</li><li>Outline the incident response process from preparation through recovery and lessons learned</li><li>Implement incident response techniques including triage, evidence handling and chain of custody, escalation, and root cause analysis</li><li>Align incident response with business continuity and disaster recovery</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Reporting and Communication (16%)</h3><ul><li>Communicate vulnerability findings through reports, dashboards, and KPIs</li><li>Document security incidents and produce post-incident reviews</li><li>Track effectiveness metrics such as detection time, response time, and remediation effectiveness</li><li>Deliver risk-focused, stakeholder-appropriate communication (executive summaries vs. technical documentation)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C916' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>TDA-C01</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Domain 1: Connect to and Transform Data (24%)</h3><ul><li>Connect to data sources: choose appropriate source, live vs extract, relational databases, spreadsheets, .hyper/.tde files, custom SQL queries, Tableau Server data sources</li><li>Prepare data for analysis: assess data quality (completeness, consistency, accuracy), perform cleaning operations, organize data into folders</li><li>Use multiple data sources: establish relationships, create joins, union tables, blend data; use Data Interpreter, pivot, split; create extract filters</li><li>Perform data transformation in Tableau Prep: unions, joins, aggregations, filtering, pivots based on business scenario</li><li>Customize fields: change default field properties, rename columns, convert discrete/continuous and dimension/measure, create aliases</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Domain 2: Explore and Analyze Data (41%)</h3><ul><li>Create calculated fields: date calculations (DATEPARSE, DATENAME), string functions, logical/Boolean expressions, number functions, type conversion, aggregate functions, FIXED LOD calculations</li><li>Create quick and custom table calculations: moving average, percent of total, running total, percentile, compound growth rate, year-to-date/month-to-date/year-over-year, index, ranking, first-last</li><li>Create and use filters: apply to dimensions/measures, configure Top N/Bottom N/include/exclude/wildcard/conditional, context filters, apply across multiple sheets and data sources</li><li>Create parameters to enable interactivity in calculations, filters, and reference lines</li><li>Structure the data using sets, bins, hierarchies, and groups</li><li>Map data geographically (symbol, heat, density, choropleth/filled maps) and use the Analytics feature (totals/subtotals, reference lines/bands, trend lines, forecasting, predictive models)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Domain 3: Create Content (26%)</h3><ul><li>Create basic charts from scratch (bar, line, pie, highlight table, scatter plot, histogram, tree map, bubbles, Gantt, box plot, dual axis, combo) and sort data including custom sort</li><li>Create dashboards and stories: combine sheets using containers and layout options, add objects, create stories</li><li>Add interactivity to dashboards: filter/URL/highlight actions, sheet swapping via parameters or sheet selector, navigation buttons, user-guiding sentences</li><li>Format dashboards: apply color/font/shapes/styling, custom shapes and color palettes, annotations, tooltips, padding, gridline/banding removal, responsive design for device layouts</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Domain 4: Publish and Manage Content on Tableau Server and Tableau Online (9%)</h3><ul><li>Publish content: publish a workbook, publish a data source, print content, export content</li><li>Schedule data updates: schedule data extract refreshes, schedule a Tableau Prep workflow</li><li>Manage published workbooks: create alerts, create subscriptions</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C919' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>INF-105</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Security Principles</h3><ul><li>Explain common security principles: hardening, defense-in-depth, CIA triad, code of ethics, Zero Trust, privacy (incl. AI use cases), data classification/retention, security governance</li><li>Explain cybersecurity frameworks and best practices: NIST Cybersecurity Framework, ISO/IEC 27001, CIS Critical Security Controls</li><li>Explain vulnerabilities, threats, and common attacks (malware, brute force, SQL injection, privilege escalation, ransomware, DDoS, botnets, MITM, IoT vulnerabilities, insider threats, APT, spoofing)</li><li>Recognize social engineering attacks: tailgating, impersonation, phishing variants (spear/vishing/smishing/whaling), pharming, malicious QR/URL redirection, AI-driven attack sophistication</li><li>Explain access management: AAA, RADIUS, MFA methods, password policies, biometric auth, cloud-based resource sharing</li><li>Explain how encryption protects confidentiality/integrity: symmetric/asymmetric encryption, hashing, PKI, certificates, data in transit/at rest/in use</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Securing the Network</h3><ul><li>Identify vulnerabilities in commonly used protocols (TCP, ARP, ICMP, DHCP, DNS, SMTP, SNMP, HTTP/HTTPS, FTP/SFTP, Telnet/SSH)</li><li>Describe the role of addressing in network security: segmentation (DMZ, VLANs), NAT, public/private/internal/external/trusted networks</li><li>Describe network security technologies: honeypots, proxy servers, IDS/IPS, firewalls, ACLs, VPN, NAC, cloud security (VPC, security groups), input validation/malware detection/spam filtering</li><li>Validate wireless network security: MAC filtering, wireless encryption standards/protocols, SSID</li><li>Examine network security logs (firewall, IDS/IPS) to identify anomalies</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Securing Endpoint Devices</h3><ul><li>Apply security settings to harden Windows, macOS, and Linux operating systems using CIS benchmarks</li><li>Use endpoint tools for security assessment: netstat, nslookup, nmap, zenmap, ss</li><li>Use packet capture utilities (Wireshark, tcpdump) to identify anomalies</li><li>Demonstrate familiarity with endpoint security policies/standards: PCI DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, BYOD, patch/device management</li><li>Interpret system logs (Event Viewer, audit logs, syslog) to identify anomalies</li><li>Perform malware removal: scanning, remediation, and incident response (containment, quarantine, treatment, inoculation)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Vulnerability Assessment and Risk Management</h3><ul><li>Use threat intelligence sources to identify vulnerabilities: CVEs, vulnerability databases, cybersecurity reports/news, collective intelligence</li><li>Explain risk management: vulnerability vs. risk, mitigation strategies, risk severity levels, likelihood of occurrence, IT system security assessments</li><li>Explain the penetration testing process: reconnaissance, port scanning, DAST and SAST application testing, reporting to stakeholders</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Incident Handling</h3><ul><li>Monitor security events for escalation: role of SIEM/SOAR, true/false positive vs. negative differentiation</li><li>Explain digital forensics process and attack frameworks: evidence handling/chain of custody, Cyber Kill Chain, MITRE ATT&CK, Diamond Model, Pyramid of Pain</li><li>Explain cybersecurity incident response elements: NIST SP 800-61 lifecycle stages, compliance framework impact (GDPR, HIPAA, PCI-DSS, FERPA, FISMA)</li><li>Explain disaster recovery and business continuity planning: DRP/BCP features, backup types, hot/cold spares, DR controls</li><li>Assist users in restoring data after an incident: restore points, RPO/RTO, hot/warm/cold standby</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C920' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>ACP</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Modeling (31%)</h3><ul><li>Create and modify advanced architectural components (wall types with layers/sweeps/reveals, curtain walls, roofs/floors/ceiling types, stairs incl. multi-level, railings, openings, columns, joining/attaching/hosting)</li><li>Create, configure, and apply materials (custom materials/libraries, apply to system/loadable families, Split Face and Paint tools)</li><li>Configure rooms (area/volume computations, room parameters, room bounding elements incl. linked files)</li><li>Create and configure basic 3D parametric families (correct template, reference planes, parameters, family categories, visibility/graphics overrides, formulas, solid/void geometry, nested/shared families, loadable vs in-place)</li><li>Create topography (points, point elevations, building pads, subregions, topography from linked CAD/CSV)</li><li>Create, modify, and manage model groups (use cases, hosted/non-hosted elements, in/out-of-group relationships)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Documentation (24%)</h3><ul><li>Create and control advanced model views, visibility, and graphics (view templates, filters, visibility overrides, object styles, view types, dependent views, view properties, crop boundaries/scope boxes, plan regions)</li><li>Configure and manage annotative elements (text styles/leaders, keynotes, dimension styles, generic annotation families, matchlines/view references)</li><li>Use document revisions (control, issue, and manage revisions on sheets)</li><li>Create and manage legends (legend components, color fill legends, keynote legends)</li><li>Create and control detail and drafting views (drafting views, filled/masking regions, repeating detail components, line styles, fill patterns)</li><li>Create and configure basic 2D parametric families and detail groups (tags with labels/linework, detail components, detail group placement/origin/attachment)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Collaboration and coordination (22%)</h3><ul><li>Configure worksets and initiate worksharing (activate worksharing, detached models, display settings, worksets in linked models)</li><li>Link and manage various file formats (Revit links with positioning, link visibility/graphics, Manage Links dialog for images/PDFs/DWGs/point clouds, linking vs importing CAD)</li><li>Perform basic model maintenance (errors/warnings, selective purge, audit and compact, exploding DWG implications)</li><li>Manage and configure phasing (element phase status, project phase settings/filters/overrides, mapping phases in linked models)</li><li>Create, configure, and manage design options (design option sets, assign to views, move elements between options/main model)</li><li>Use the Copy/Monitor process (copy and monitor elements from linked models, copy options, coordination review)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Project standards and setup (11%)</h3><ul><li>Configure custom user interface settings (save reminders, file locations, tabs, shortcuts, element selections, snaps)</li><li>Configure and manage project settings and location (project parameters, object styles, project units, transfer project standards, Project North/True North, project location, project information)</li><li>Use and manage the project browser (browser organization schemes, search function)</li><li>Configure print and export settings (print sets, export to CAD, export to IFC/image/PDF, save library files, export schedules)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Information analysis (11%)</h3><ul><li>Create and manage schedules (schedule from linked models/phases/design options, instance/type/calculated/combined parameters, schedule types incl. filtering/sorting/grouping, note blocks, key schedules)</li><li>Create and edit area schemes and area plans (area schemes and boundaries, color fill legends, scheme-to-plan/schedule relationships)</li><li>Create sun and shadow studies (still/single/multi-day solar studies, geographic location, exporting sun studies)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C921' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>DA0-002</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Data Concepts and Environments (20%)</h3><ul><li>Explain data concepts: database types (relational/non-relational), file extensions (.csv, .xlsx, .json, .txt, .jpg, .dat), data structures (structured/semi-structured/unstructured, tables, schema, dimensional tables), and data types (string, numeric, datetime, spatial, boolean, large objects, GUID/UUID)</li><li>Identify types of data sources: databases, APIs, website data, files, logs, and data repositories (data lakes, lakehouses, marts, silos, warehouses)</li><li>Identify infrastructure concepts: cloud providers (AWS, Azure, Google), cloud/on-prem models (private, public, hybrid), storage types (object, file, local, shared, block), and containerization</li><li>Identify common data analysis tools: coding environments/IDEs, BI software (Tableau, Power BI, Looker), packages/libraries (pandas, tidyverse, Anaconda), programming languages (SAS, Python, R, Scala), and DBMS tools (SQL Server Management Studio, MySQL Workbench, MongoDB Compass, DBeaver, Toad, Azure Data Studio)</li><li>Identify artificial intelligence (AI) concepts: generative AI/LLMs, foundational models, deep learning, natural language processing (NLP), and robotic process automation (RPA) including automated reporting</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Data Acquisition and Preparation (22%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, use data acquisition methods: data integration, querying (join, concatenate, filter, union, grouping, aggregate, nested queries), basic query optimization (indexing, parameterization, subsets, temporary tables), ETL/ELT, and data collection (surveying, sampling)</li><li>Given a scenario, perform data exploration to identify possible inconsistencies with a data set: missing values, duplication, redundancy, outliers, completeness, and validation</li><li>Given a scenario, perform appropriate data transformation and cleansing techniques: string manipulation (RegEx), conversion, clustering/binning, augmentation, exploding, scaling, standardization, imputation, parsing, merging, appending, derived variables/calculated fields, and deletion</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Data Analysis (24%)</h3><ul><li>Given a set of requirements, determine the appropriate communication approach for data analysis: mock-ups, accessibility (auditory, visual), technical vs. non-technical audience, level of detail, internal vs. external, user persona type (C-suite vs. individual contributor), sensitive vs. non-sensitive data, and KPIs</li><li>Given a scenario, select the appropriate statistical method or function: basic statistical methods (prescriptive, descriptive, predictive, inferential) and functions/measures (mathematical measures of central tendency and dispersion, logical, date, string)</li><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot basic issues using the appropriate tool or method: connectivity-related, user-reported, basic SQL code, and corrupted data issues; tools/methods including enable logging, validate data source, and consulting vendor communities/online resources</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Visualization and Reporting (20%)</h3><ul><li>Given a scenario, use the appropriate visual elements: types (charts, maps, pivot tables, infographics) and design elements (labels, legends, branding, color schemes)</li><li>Given a scenario, use the appropriate delivery or consumption method: executive summary, self-service portal, dashboards (static, dynamic, recurring, ad hoc), and data versioning techniques (snapshot, real-time)</li><li>Given a scenario, troubleshoot issues using report validation techniques: issues (excessive load time, slow refresh rate, large data size, filter not working correctly, stale data, corrupt data) and techniques (data filtering, code/calc/peer review, source validation, data structure changes, monitoring alerts)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Data Governance (14%)</h3><ul><li>Explain data management concepts: integration, documentation (data flow diagram, data explainability report, data dictionary, hierarchy structure, data lineage), source of truth, data versioning (snapshots, refresh intervals), and metadata</li><li>Summarize concepts related to data compliance: retention, GDPR, jurisdictional requirements, replication, storage, data ethics, PCI DSS, audit, classification, and incident reporting (data breach, security)</li><li>Compare and contrast data privacy and protection practices: role-based access control, encryption (in transit, at rest), data usage/sharing, NIST, PII, PHI, anonymization, and masking</li><li>Compare and contrast data quality assurance practices: requirement testing, stress test, UAT, source control, unit test, data health check/data drifts, automated data quality monitoring, data profiling/quality metrics, and ISO standards</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C923' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>AI-102</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Plan and manage an Azure AI solution (22.5%)</h3><ul><li>Select the appropriate Microsoft Foundry service for generative AI, computer vision, NLP, speech, information extraction, and knowledge mining needs</li><li>Plan, create, and deploy a Microsoft Foundry Service resource; choose and deploy AI models; install/use SDKs and APIs; integrate into a CI/CD pipeline; plan container deployment</li><li>Monitor an Azure AI resource, manage costs, and manage/protect account keys and authentication</li><li>Implement content moderation, responsible AI content filters/blocklists, prompt shields and harm detection</li><li>Design a responsible AI governance framework</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Implement generative AI solutions (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Plan, prepare, and deploy a generative AI solution (hub, project, resources) with Microsoft Foundry, including prompt flow and prompt templates</li><li>Implement a RAG pattern by grounding a model in your own data; evaluate models and flows</li><li>Provision Azure OpenAI in Foundry Models, deploy a model, submit prompts, use DALL-E and multimodal models</li><li>Configure generation parameters, model monitoring/diagnostics, and optimize/scale deployed resources</li><li>Apply prompt engineering techniques and fine-tune a generative model; implement orchestration of multiple generative AI models</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Implement an agentic solution (7.5%)</h3><ul><li>Understand the role and use cases of an AI agent</li><li>Configure resources and create an agent with the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service</li><li>Implement complex agents with Microsoft Agent Framework</li><li>Implement multi-agent orchestration, multi-user, and autonomous-capability workflows</li><li>Test, optimize, and deploy an agent</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Implement computer vision solutions (12.5%)</h3><ul><li>Select visual features, detect objects, generate image tags, and interpret image analysis responses</li><li>Extract and convert handwritten/printed text from images (OCR) using Azure Vision in Foundry Tools</li><li>Choose, label, train, evaluate, publish, and consume custom vision models (classification and object detection)</li><li>Use Azure AI Video Indexer to extract insights from video or live streams</li><li>Use Spatial Analysis to detect presence and movement of people in video</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Implement natural language processing solutions (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Extract key phrases and entities, determine sentiment, detect language, and detect PII in text</li><li>Translate text and documents; implement text-to-speech, speech-to-text, and custom speech solutions (incl. SSML)</li><li>Create, train, evaluate, deploy, and consume custom language understanding models (intents, entities, utterances)</li><li>Build and publish custom question-answering knowledge bases, including multi-turn and multi-language solutions</li><li>Implement custom translation models (train, improve, publish)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Implement knowledge mining and information extraction solutions (17.5%)</h3><ul><li>Provision an Azure AI Search resource; create indexes, skillsets, data sources, and indexers; query indexes (semantic and vector search)</li><li>Implement custom skills and manage Knowledge Store projections (file, object, table)</li><li>Provision Azure Document Intelligence; use prebuilt models and train/test/publish custom and composed document models</li><li>Extract information with Azure Content Understanding: OCR pipelines, document classification/summarization, entity/table/image extraction from documents, images, video, and audio</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C926' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>N10-009</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Networking Concepts (23%)</h3><ul><li>OSI model layers and encapsulation/decapsulation</li><li>Network topologies, architectures and types (LAN, WAN, SD-WAN, hybrid, cloud)</li><li>Cloud concepts and connectivity options (NFV, VPC, hybrid/multi-cloud)</li><li>Common ports, protocols, and traffic types</li><li>Transmission media and transceivers (copper, fiber, wireless standards)</li><li>IPv4 subnetting and IPv6 addressing schemes</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Network Implementation (20%)</h3><ul><li>Routing technologies and configurations (static, dynamic, BGP/OSPF concepts)</li><li>Switching technologies (VLANs, trunking, STP, port security)</li><li>Wireless devices and configurations (WLAN standards, encryption, deployment)</li><li>Networked devices for specific purposes (firewalls, load balancers, IDS/IPS, proxies)</li><li>IP addressing services (DHCP, DNS, NAT) implementation</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Network Operations (19%)</h3><ul><li>Documentation practices (network diagrams, IP address management, standard operating procedures)</li><li>Monitoring network performance (SNMP, flow data, log aggregation, baselines)</li><li>Business continuity and disaster recovery concepts (backups, site resiliency)</li><li>High availability and scalability concepts (load balancing, NIC teaming, clustering)</li><li>Change management and lifecycle management of network operations</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Network Security (14%)</h3><ul><li>Physical security controls (locks, cameras, badge access)</li><li>Device hardening techniques (ACLs, disabling unused ports/services, patching)</li><li>Common attacks and their mitigations (DoS, VLAN hopping, rogue DHCP/AP, social engineering)</li><li>Network access control concepts (802.1X, NAC, port security)</li><li>Secure remote access methods (VPNs, IPsec, RDP, SSH)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Network Troubleshooting (24%)</h3><ul><li>Network troubleshooting methodology (identify, establish theory, test, implement, document)</li><li>Cabling and physical connectivity issue resolution</li><li>Network software tools and commands (ping, traceroute, ipconfig/ifconfig, packet capture)</li><li>Wireless network issue troubleshooting (interference, coverage, channel overlap)</li><li>General networking issue resolution (DNS, DHCP, routing, VLAN misconfiguration)</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C938' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>200-301</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Network Fundamentals (20%)</h3><ul><li>Explain the role and function of network components (routers, L2/L3 switches, next-gen firewalls/IPS, access points, controllers, endpoints, servers, PoE)</li><li>Describe network topology architectures (two-tier, three-tier, spine-leaf, WAN, SOHO, on-premises and cloud)</li><li>Configure and verify IPv4 addressing/subnetting and IPv6 addressing/prefix, including IPv6 address types</li><li>Compare TCP to UDP; compare physical interface and cabling types and identify interface/cable issues</li><li>Explain virtualization fundamentals (server virtualization, containers, VRFs) and describe switching concepts (MAC learning/aging, frame switching/flooding, MAC address table)</li><li>Describe wireless principles (nonoverlapping Wi-Fi channels, SSID, RF, encryption)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Network Access (20%)</h3><ul><li>Configure and verify VLANs (normal range) spanning multiple switches, including access ports and InterVLAN connectivity</li><li>Configure and verify interswitch connectivity (trunk ports, 802.1Q, native VLAN) and Layer 2 discovery protocols (CDP, LLDP)</li><li>Configure and verify Layer 2/Layer 3 EtherChannel (LACP)</li><li>Interpret basic operations of Rapid PVST+ Spanning Tree Protocol (root port/bridge, port states/roles, PortFast, root guard/loop guard/BPDU filter/BPDU guard)</li><li>Describe Cisco Wireless Architectures, AP modes, and physical infrastructure connections of WLAN components (AP, WLC, access/trunk ports, LAG)</li><li>Describe network device management access (Telnet, SSH, HTTP, HTTPS, console, TACACS+/RADIUS, cloud managed) and interpret wireless LAN GUI configuration for client connectivity</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 IP Connectivity (25%)</h3><ul><li>Interpret the components of a routing table (routing protocol code, prefix, network mask, next hop, administrative distance, metric, gateway of last resort)</li><li>Determine how a router makes a forwarding decision by default (longest prefix match, administrative distance, routing protocol metric)</li><li>Configure and verify IPv4 and IPv6 static routing (default, network, host, floating static routes)</li><li>Configure and verify single area OSPFv2 (neighbor adjacencies, point-to-point, broadcast DR/BDR selection, router ID)</li><li>Describe the purpose, functions, and concepts of first hop redundancy protocols</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 IP Services (10%)</h3><ul><li>Configure and verify inside source NAT using static and pools</li><li>Configure and verify NTP in client and server mode, and DHCP client/relay</li><li>Explain the role of DHCP and DNS, and the function of SNMP, within the network</li><li>Describe the use of syslog features including facilities and severity levels</li><li>Explain forwarding per-hop behavior (PHB) for QoS (classification, marking, queuing, congestion, policing, shaping)</li><li>Configure network devices for remote access using SSH; describe TFTP/FTP capabilities</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Security Fundamentals (15%)</h3><ul><li>Define key security concepts (threats, vulnerabilities, exploits, mitigation techniques) and security program elements (user awareness, training, physical access control)</li><li>Configure and verify device access control using local passwords and security password policy elements (MFA, certificates, biometrics)</li><li>Describe IPsec remote access and site-to-site VPNs</li><li>Configure and verify access control lists and Layer 2 security features (DHCP snooping, dynamic ARP inspection, port security)</li><li>Compare authentication, authorization, and accounting (AAA) concepts</li><li>Describe wireless security protocols (WPA, WPA2, WPA3) and configure/verify WLAN within the GUI using WPA2 PSK</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Automation and Programmability (10%)</h3><ul><li>Explain how automation impacts network management; compare traditional networks with controller-based networking</li><li>Describe controller-based, software-defined architecture (overlay, underlay, fabric; separation of control/data plane; northbound/southbound APIs)</li><li>Explain AI (generative and predictive) and machine learning in network operations</li><li>Describe characteristics of REST-based APIs (authentication types, CRUD, HTTP verbs, data encoding)</li><li>Recognize the capabilities of configuration management mechanisms such as Ansible and Terraform</li><li>Recognize components of JSON-encoded data</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C975' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
INSERT INTO catalog_product_entity_text (entity_type_id,attribute_id,store_id,entity_id,value) SELECT 4,@ad,0,entity_id,'<p>This course prepares you for the <strong>N/A</strong> certification exam, covering all official exam domains and their approximate weightings:</p><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 1 Architecting low-code AI solutions (13%)</h3><ul><li>Build models in BigQuery ML or Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform AutoML (classification, regression, forecasting, clustering) based on the business problem</li><li>Perform feature engineering/selection using BigQuery ML; generate predictions using BigQuery ML</li><li>Train models using Agent Platform AutoML; fine-tune Gemini models using BigQuery</li><li>Evaluate and select the appropriate model from Agent Platform Model Garden for a given task</li><li>Build applications using industry-specific APIs (Document AI, Vision, Translate) and tune models for specific use cases (Gemini, Imagen, Veo)</li><li>Optimize Gemini-based applications for cost, latency, and availability</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 2 Collaborating within and across teams to manage data and models (16%)</h3><ul><li>Organize and explore tabular, text, and image data for efficient experimenting, training, and serving</li><li>Choose the right preprocessing tool by scale/complexity (BigQuery SQL, Dataflow, Apache Spark, in-memory Python frameworks)</li><li>Create/consolidate features in Agent Platform Feature Store; ensure data privacy and handle PII</li><li>Prototype models in Agent Platform Workbench or Colab Enterprise notebooks using PyTorch, sklearn, JAX and Model Garden models</li><li>Choose the right environment for experimentation (Experiments on Agent Platform, Agent Platform Pipelines, Kubeflow Pipelines)</li><li>Evaluate predictive and gen AI solutions (metrics, LLM-as-a-judge) and track model artifacts/versions/lineage</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 3 Scaling prototypes into ML models (21%)</h3><ul><li>Choose model type (ARIMA, DNN, LLM), product (AutoML, BigQuery ML, Pipelines), deployment strategy, and modeling technique given interpretability needs</li><li>Organize and ingest structured/unstructured training data (Cloud Storage, BigQuery) into training pipelines</li><li>Train models via different SDKs (Agent Platform custom training, Kubeflow on GKE, AutoML, Tabular Workflows)</li><li>Troubleshoot ML model training failures and perform hyperparameter tuning</li><li>Fine-tune foundational models from Agent Platform/Model Garden and judge when tuning is warranted</li><li>Evaluate compute/accelerator options (CPU, GPU, TPU) and distributed training strategies (data/model parallelism)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 4 Serving and scaling models (20%)</h3><ul><li>Deploy models for batch and online inference (Agent Platform, Model Garden, Cloud Run, GKE)</li><li>Package/serve models from different frameworks (PyTorch, XGBoost) using prebuilt/custom containers</li><li>Organize and version models in Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform Model Registry</li><li>Implement rollout strategies (A/B testing, canary deployments) and inference pre/postprocessing</li><li>Manage and serve features via Agent Platform Feature Store; deploy to public/private endpoints</li><li>Choose appropriate serving hardware (CPU/GPU/TPU/edge) and scale serving backend based on throughput</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 5 Automating and orchestrating ML pipelines (18%)</h3><ul><li>Validate data and models within end-to-end ML pipelines</li><li>Build and orchestrate pipelines using managed/unmanaged services or templates (Agent Platform Pipelines, Managed Service for Apache Airflow, Ray on Agent Platform)</li><li>Ensure consistent data preprocessing between training and serving</li><li>Determine an appropriate model retraining policy</li><li>Deploy models in CI/CD/CT pipelines (e.g., Cloud Build)</li></ul><h3 class="course-topic-h3">Domain 6 Monitoring AI solutions (13%)</h3><ul><li>Build secure AI systems against data/model exfiltration, malicious prompting, and sensitive-data leakage to LLMs (Regex, safety filters, Model Armor)</li><li>Align with responsible AI practices, including monitoring for bias</li><li>Provide model explainability on Agent Platform (e.g., Agent Platform Inference)</li><li>Configure Model Monitoring on Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform for continuous evaluation metrics</li><li>Monitor for training-serving skew, data drift, concept drift, and feature attribution drift</li><li>Monitor, test, and evaluate gen AI solutions</li></ul>' FROM catalog_product_entity WHERE sku='C997' ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE value=VALUES(value);
